{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_f1c4fdae48bf4db7aad6a786","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cat \"$TALLY_BRIEF\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task instruments: Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"container/rootfs\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:40d1c04d4d9aecd32e3601201fcede60e7657c30fdf61fe36824f59271a861ac\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py && grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l | grep -qx 3 && python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v\"],\"description\":\"All three modules compile, carry notices, and their tests pass.\",\"id\":\"instruments-compile-with-notices\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"Instruments importable inside the image with FN_ kill-switches, default off\",\"Notice headers travel with every adapted module\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Create container/rootfs/ carrying three instrument modules adapted from the Apache-2.0 reference implementation, per specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3, renamed to the FN_ env prefix: fn_synctrace.py (wraps the handful of tensor methods that force a blocking device-to-host sync, ~25 events per step, driven from a FN_PROFILE window), fn_offload_batch.py (the store-batch and promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload defect; env FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC and FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC), and fn_expert_union.py (counts distinct routed experts per decode step; the reference wrapped a routing entry the workload never calls — re-target the wrap onto the stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py as established in specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4; env FN_EXPERT_UNION with FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT). Every module keeps an adaptation notice header naming the upstream file and license. Add tests/test_instruments.py asserting: py_compile passes for each module, each carries the notice header, and fn_offload_batch budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants (floor at max group size; promote counted in blocks). Boundaries: touch only container/rootfs/ and tests/.\",\"id\":\"instruments\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b\",\"title\":\"Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"c1363cb2308e16f3d96bd92e8cde7c94261d4cb9\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-ed7013e7b4ab/instruments\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f\",\"taskId\":\"instruments\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":4,\"recheckedCursor\":4,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"details":{}}}
{"type":"tool_execution_end","toolCallId":"call_f1c4fdae48bf4db7aad6a786","toolName":"bash","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task instruments: Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"container/rootfs\\\",\\\"tests\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:40d1c04d4d9aecd32e3601201fcede60e7657c30fdf61fe36824f59271a861ac\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py && grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l | grep -qx 3 && python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v\"],\"description\":\"All three modules compile, carry notices, and their tests pass.\",\"id\":\"instruments-compile-with-notices\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"Instruments importable inside the image with FN_ kill-switches, default off\",\"Notice headers travel with every adapted module\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Create container/rootfs/ carrying three instrument modules adapted from the Apache-2.0 reference implementation, per specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3, renamed to the FN_ env prefix: fn_synctrace.py (wraps the handful of tensor methods that force a blocking device-to-host sync, ~25 events per step, driven from a FN_PROFILE window), fn_offload_batch.py (the store-batch and promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload defect; env FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC and FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC), and fn_expert_union.py (counts distinct routed experts per decode step; the reference wrapped a routing entry the workload never calls — re-target the wrap onto the stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py as established in specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4; env FN_EXPERT_UNION with FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT). Every module keeps an adaptation notice header naming the upstream file and license. Add tests/test_instruments.py asserting: py_compile passes for each module, each carries the notice header, and fn_offload_batch budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants (floor at max group size; promote counted in blocks). Boundaries: touch only container/rootfs/ and tests/.\",\"id\":\"instruments\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b\",\"title\":\"Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"c13