{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Mission complete. Task `instruments` is done and committed on the assigned lane.\n\n**What landed** (commit `9a3e54d` on `tally-work/flashnext-ed7013e7b4ab/instruments`, all paths inside the binding write boundary `container/rootfs/` + `tests/`):\n\n1. **`container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py`** — adapted from `ds4_synctrace.py` (AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ `a8f620d`, Apache-2.0): wraps the 7 Tensor methods that force blocking D2H syncs (`item`, `tolist`, `cpu`, `numpy`, `nonzero`, `__float__`, `__int__`), ~25 events/step, driven from the `FN_PROFILE` window with no env var of its own (nothing installs at import → default off). The upstream limitation caveat (bool-mask indexing bypasses the hook) is retained verbatim.\n\n2. **`container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py`** — adapted from `ds4_offload_batch.py`: the store-batch/promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload ratchet defect. Env renamed to `FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC` / `FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC` (≤ 0 ⇒ `None` ⇒ stock behaviour). Arithmetic and both load-bearing invariants unchanged; still torch-free (`import os` only).\n\n3. **`container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py`** — adapted from `ds4_expert_union.py` with the mandated re-target: the upstream wrap (`gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data`) is never called by this workload, so the wrap now sits on the stock fused-mixture router entry **`fused_topk`** in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py` (per qsa-53896.md §4). `num_local_experts` comes off `gating_output.shape[-1]` — host metadata, preserving the no-sync discipline. Kill switch `FN_EXPERT_UNION` (default off), window env `FN_EU_START`/`FN_EU_CALLS`/`FN_EU_OUT`; every failure path swallows exceptions.\n\n4. **`tests/test_instruments.py`** — 11 host-runnable tests: py_compile with cfile into a tempdir, notice-header checks (names upstream file, repo, license), FN_ env-surface rename verified (and stock `DS4_*` env names asserted absent), tracked-bytecode overlay invariant, and the reference budget invariants (floor clamps exactly to max group size at frac 0.001; promote counted in blocks, capped at the tier, floored at 1; all disabled/degenerate paths return `None`; env-read paths with garbage fallback).\n\n**Verification:** the exact acceptance argv passes — all three modules compile, `grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l` = 3, `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v` → 11/11 OK. Full repo suite (`unittest discover -s tests`) → 20/20 OK. Not pushed, not merged, no other worklist task read.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: my bytecode-in-overlay test pins to `git ls-files` rather than the filesystem, because the acceptance command's own plain `py_compile` creates a transient (gitignored) `__pycache__` in the overlay — what ships into the image via `COPY` is only the tracked content, which is what the invariant guards."}}
