read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:40d1c04d4d9aecd32e3601201fcede60e7657c30fdf61fe36824f59271a861ac\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py && grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l | grep -qx 3 && python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v\"],\"description\":\"All three modules compile, carry notices, and their tests pass.\",\"id\":\"instruments-compile-with-notices\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"Instruments importable inside the image with FN_ kill-switches, default off\",\"Notice headers travel with every adapted module\"],\"dependencies\":[],\"goal\":\"Create container/rootfs/ carrying three instrument modules adapted from the Apache-2.0 reference implementation, per specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md section 3, renamed to the FN_ env prefix: fn_synctrace.py (wraps the handful of tensor methods that force a blocking device-to-host sync, ~25 events per step, driven from a FN_PROFILE window), fn_offload_batch.py (the store-batch and promote budget helpers fixing the upstream offload defect; env FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC and FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC), and fn_expert_union.py (counts distinct routed experts per decode step; the reference wrapped a routing entry the workload never calls — re-target the wrap onto the stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py as established in specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4; env FN_EXPERT_UNION with FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT). Every module keeps an adaptation notice header naming the upstream file and license. Add tests/test_instruments.py asserting: py_compile passes for each module, each carries the notice header, and fn_offload_batch budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants (floor at max group size; promote counted in blocks). Boundaries: touch only container/rootfs/ and tests/.\",\"id\":\"instruments\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md\",\"specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"scripts/receipts-verify.py\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:16ab40e19244fd0f9cde08858a2c348ff99e701e0a8ce46b6e99fc84b6d36c5b\",\"title\":\"Engagement-proof instruments adapted into the container overlay\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"c1363cb2308e16f3d96bd92e8cde7c94261d4cb9\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-ed7013e7b4ab/instruments\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"container/rootfs\",\"tests\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/instruments-16ab40e19244fd0f\",\"taskId\":\"instruments\",\"worktreePath\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments\"},\"steering\":{\"channel\":\"locally-authorized-snapshot\",\"authorizedComments\":[],\"attemptReceipt\":{\"lateRecheckCommentIds\":[],\"preparedCommentIds\":[],\"recheckTruncated\":false,\"rechecked\":true,\"source\":{\"kind\":\"local-jsonl\",\"path\":\"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/steering/01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae/steering-v1.jsonl\",\"preparedCursor\":4,\"recheckedCursor\":4,\"registrationId\":\"01a04c1f-4605-7823-9eac-475e99b842ae\"}},\"machineDiagnoses\":[],\"machineOutcomes\":[]}}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988116629},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm in the work tree at /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments. This is a stateless reconciliation-style attempt. I need to check the current git status, the assigned branch, and any existing task work.\n\nMission:\n- Create container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py, fn_offload_batch.py, fn_expert_union.py — adapted from the Apache-2.0 reference implementation, following section 3 of specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md and section 4 of qsa-53896.md.\n- Each file must have an \"Adapted from\" notice header.\n- The FN_ env-var prefix, kill switch, defaults off.\n- tests/test_instruments.py: run py_compile against each file, check for the notice header, and verify that fn_offload_batch's budget calculation satisfies the reference's invariants.\n- Commit to branch tally-work/flashnext-ed7013e7b4ab/instruments. Don't push or merge.\n\nFirst I'll read the spec and the style reference, then check the git state.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_34db646c7d2441298df6402d","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd \"$(dirname \"$TALLY_BRIEF\")\"; git -C /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments status; git -C /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments branch --show-current; git -C /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments log --oneline -5; cat /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/.git"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_26094d82097d4a4d96aa3aae","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -R /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/tests /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs 2>&1 | head -60"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2708,"output":581,"cacheRead":4224,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":257,"totalTokens":7513,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988116634,"responseId":"chatcmpl-43ed9904-2bef-4c58-8030-621ac8baafe9","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_34db646c7d2441298df6402d","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"On branch tally-work/flashnext-ed7013e7b4ab/instruments\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\ntally-work/flashnext-ed7013e7b4ab/instruments\nc1363cb container-recipe: Container recipe: pinned wheel set + engine fork built from source\na428fee handoff: staging complete, campaign launches attended-by-daylight not overnight\nf6db565 receipts: weights staged on both nodes (131 shards, 185563801379 bytes each)\nd62bd2f handoff: OVERSEER-LAUNCH refresh — routing read order, overseer owns the arm, weights pre-staging state, NCCL discipline\n0fbc61b README truth-up: pre-arm bake done, spec ratified, four host-bake findings, transport story, overnight compute routing\ngitdir: /home/tom/mecattaf/flashnext/.git/worktrees/instruments\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988129018},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_26094d82097d4a4d96aa3aae","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container:\nbuild.sh\nContainerfile\nrootfs\n\n/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs:\n\n/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs:\nflashnext\n\n/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs/flashnext:\ncontracts\nevidence\nspec.md\ntrace.json\n\n/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs/flashnext/contracts:\ntrace.schema.json\n\n/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs/flashnext/evidence:\ndotfiles-observed.md\nds4-vllm-manifest.md\ninnovation-ledger.md\nkyuz0-rocm10.md\nmoe-dispatch.md\nnix-hardening-addendum.md\nnix-packaging-brief.md\nnix-strix-halo.md\nple-54129.md\nqsa-53896.md\ntally-fit-analysis.md\n\n/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/tests:\ntest_repo_invariants.py\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988129018},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The working tree is clean at baseRev c1363cb, the branch is correct, and there is no task work yet. container/rootfs is empty, and tests only has test_repo_invariants.py.\n\nRead the spec: Section 3 of ds4-vllm-manifest.md, Section 4 of qsa-53896.md, and also check the style reference in scripts/receipts-verify.py.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Working tree is clean at the baseRev on the assigned branch, no prior task work. Reading the cited specs now.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_687c79a6935b4faa96145930","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs/flashnext/evidence/ds4-vllm-manifest.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1838,"output":187,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":91,"totalTokens":8297,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988129022,"responseId":"chatcmpl-69457f82-4332-47fc-b415-6f38b16eca6b","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_687c79a6935b4faa96145930","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# ds4-vllm lift manifest — exact, pinned\n\n**Source tree:** `/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm`\n**Revision:** `a8f620d3032b23271b1969123168a561d0fd882a` (`git rev-parse HEAD`, 2026-08-28)\n**Working tree:** clean (`git status --porcelain` → empty output) [M]\n**Upstream license:** Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE:1-4` = Apache License Version 2.0) [S]\n**Tree size:** 57 files, 13,351 lines total (`find … | xargs wc -l`) [M]\n\nEvidence grades: **[S]** read from source this session · **[M]** measured (command + literal\noutput) · **[CL]** claimed by a doc in-tree, not independently verified.\n\nAll patch line numbers below are line offsets **into**\n`container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch` (2,717 lines) unless a `b/` target path is named.\nAll rootfs paths are abbreviated `SITE = container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Executive corrections to the campaign record\n\nThree record claims do **not** survive re-pinning. Details in the numbered sections.\n\n| # | Record said | On-disk at `a8f620d` | Grade |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10 | \"piecewise-cudagraph eager-break around the TP all-reduce, commit `671e659`\" | **No such hunk, no such commit.** `grep -rn 671e659 .` → zero hits. The only `breakable_cudagraph.py` change is a `DS4_BREAKABLE_SYNC` stream-sync loop (patch:1777-1802). The \"eager break\" text is an *unchanged upstream context line* (patch:204). And production runs `--enforce-eager` (`host/ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh:115`), so `replay()` is inert. | [M]/[S] |\n| 4 | MANIFEST is authoritative on how patches apply | `MANIFEST.md:8` says \"The Dockerfile does **not** apply these; it `COPY`s the final files from `../rootfs`.\" **False.** `container/Dockerfile:76` runs `git apply -p1 … vllm-upstream.patch`. MANIFEST.md:8 is stale. | [S] |\n| 7 | \"`build-modules.sh` pin lines for thunderbolt-ibverbs **and rdma-core**\" | `build-modules.sh` pins **no** rdma-core. rdma-core lives only in `container/Dockerfile:61` and is pinned to a **branch tag `v57.0`**, not a commit SHA. | [M]/[S] |\n\nPlus: **3 of 12 MANIFEST \"new (N)\" line counts are wrong** (§4.4), and `AGENTS.md` §0.2\ntwice cites a \"§5\" that does not exist in the file (§6).\n\n---\n\n## 1. The routing power-of-2 fix (the one MANDATORY patch)\n\n### 1.1 Location — re-pinned, record confirmed\n\nRecord cited \"~line 1353\". **Exact.**\n\n```\n$ grep -n \"_routing_compute\" container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch\n1353:--- a/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/routing_details/_routing_compute.py\n1354:+++ b/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/routing_details/_routing_compute.py\n```\n[M]\n\n- Target file: `vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/routing_details/_routing_compute.py` [S]\n- Single hunk header: `@@ -55,9 +55,11 @@` at patch:**1355** [S]\n- Hunk body: patch:**1356-1368** [S]\n- Δ per MANIFEST: `+4/-2` (`MANIFEST.md:47`); verified by\n  `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py::test_manifest_deltas_match_their_patches` which\n  **passes** (§4.5) [M]\n\n### 1.2 The hunk, quoted verbatim (patch:1355-1368)\n\n```diff\n@@ -55,9 +55,11 @@\n \n     tl.static_assert(N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M <= 32768)\n \n-    local_offs = tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)\n+    N_GATES_PAD: tl.constexpr = triton.next_power_of_2(N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)\n+    local_offs = tl.arange(0, N_GATES_PAD)\n+    in_block = local_offs < N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M\n     offs = pid_m * BLOCK_M * N_EXPTS_ACT + local_offs\n-    expert = tl.load(ExptIndx + offs, mask=(offs < n_gates), other=-1).to(tl.uint32)\n+    expert = tl.load(ExptIndx + offs, mask=(offs < n_gates) & in_block, other=-1).to(tl.uint32)\n \n     # stable-sort by expert ID:\n     kv_pairs = ((expert << 16) | local_offs).to(tl.uint32)\n```\n[S]\n\n**Mechanism.** Triton's `tl.arange(0, X)` requires `X` to be a power of two. When\n`N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M` is not a power of two (top-k routing where `N_EXPTS_ACT` is e.g.\n6 or 10), the stock line is a compile-time failure. The fix rounds the lane count *up* to\n`N_GATES_PAD = next_power_of_2(...)` and re-introduces the true bound as an explicit\npredicate `in_block`, AND-ed into the load mask so padded lanes read `other=-1`. The\nsubsequent `kv_pairs = ((expert << 16) | local_offs)` stable-sort is unchanged and safe\nbecause `-1 → 0xFFFFFFFF` as uint32 sorts to the tail. [S, inference from the quoted code]\n\n**Why it is mandatory for top-10 routing:** exactly because `10 * BLOCK_M` is never a\npower of two for any power-of-two `BLOCK_M`. [S — reasoning from `tl.arange` semantics\nvisible in the diff; the *claim* that it is mandatory is the campaign's, graded CL]\n\n### 1.3 Adjacent hunks it depends on (the MoE \"latching\" set)\n\nThe MoE/GEMM section of `MANIFEST.md:42-50` groups five files. `_routing_compute.py` is\none of them. Its true build-order dependency is on `target_info.py`, because\n`opt_flags.py` and `opt_flags_amd.py` both import `get_cdna_version` **from**\n`triton_kernels.target_info` and the patch *renames* the originals.\n\n**(a) `target_info.py` — patch:1369-1433** (Δ `+39/-4`, `MANIFEST.md:48`) [S]\nTwo hunks: `@@ -23,8 +23,30 @@` (patch:1371) and `@@ -41,14 +63,27 @@` (patch:1403).\nIt renames the three `@triton.constexpr_function` originals to `_*_uncached`\n(patch:1399, 1408, 1414) and republishes plain-Python memoised wrappers\n(patch:1418-1433) over a `_DS4_CACHE` dict + `_DS4_MISS` sentinel (patch:1384-1394).\nThe sentinel is load-bearing and the code says so: *\"has_tma_gather/has_native_mxfp\nreturn False on ROCm, and a falsy cached value must still count as a hit or nothing\nmemoises\"* (patch:1389-1390). [S]\n\n> **Hard dependency for a fork.** Anything importing `get_cdna_version` now gets a\n> *non-constexpr* function. The patch's own comment (patch:1381-1383) states the\n> originals are retained \"in case anything needs the constexpr form from inside a\n> `@triton.jit` body -- nothing in this tree does (verified by grep)\". A Qwen fork\n> that adds a jit body calling `get_cdna_version()` would break. [S]\n\n**(b) `opt_flags.py` — patch:1236-1352** (Δ `+72/-3`, `MANIFEST.md:45`) [S]\nFive hunks: `@@ -1,11 +1,54 @@` (1238), `@@ -55,7 +98,7 @@` (1293),\n`@@ -95,7 +138,7 @@` (1302), `@@ -104,6 +147,32 @@` (1311), `@@ -295,7 +364,7 @@` (1344).\nLatches three per-call invariants — `_ds4_cdna_version()` (1266-1270), `_ds4_n_cu()`\n(1273-1277), `_ds4_backend()` (1280-1284) — plus a **single dict comprehension read of\nall seven `DS4_MOE_*` env vars at import** (patch:1287-1288):\n\n```python\n_DS4_MOE = {k: os.environ.get(\"DS4_MOE_\" + k)\n            for k in (\"BM\", \"BN\", \"NW\", \"NS\", \"BK\", \"KEEP_MFMA\", \"WPE\")}\n```\nRationale quoted at patch:1249-1256: `make_opt_flags` runs \"~92x per decode step\" and\n\"The seven `DS4_MOE_*` lookups go through `os._Environ.get` -> `Mapping.get` ->\n`decodevalue`, ~644 times per step.\" [S]\n\nThe gfx1151 tile override is at patch:1315-1340, gated `if not is_cdna4 and\n_ds4_cdna_version() == -1` (1316) then `if block_m < 128` (1321) → forces\n`block_m=16; block_n=64; num_warps=4; num_stages=3` (1322), with the comment\n\"16x64 beats stock 32x256 by 1.2-2.1x across m=6..2048 on gfx1151 (WMMA 16x16 + small\nLDS)\" (1318-1319). [S/CL — the perf figure is CL]\n\n**(c) `opt_flags_amd.py` — NEW, `SITE/vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/matmul_ogs_details/opt_flags_details/opt_flags_amd.py`, 57 lines** [M]\nNot in the patch (whole file new). Mirrors the same latching locally:\n`_ds4_cdna_version()` at :17-21, `_ds4_n_cu()` at :24-28, used at :36, :47, :55.\nIts header comment states it is \"kept local rather than imported from there, which\nwould be circular\" (:12). Note `compute_block_nk` at :31 hard-forces `block_k = 128`\nat :55-56 — this is the value `DS4_MOE_BK` overrides from `opt_flags.py:1335-1336`. [S]\n\n**Lift verdict:** `_routing_compute.py` is a standalone 13-line hunk with **no code\ndependency** on the latching set. The latching set is a *performance* adjacency, not a\ncorrectness one. Lift the routing hunk alone if you only need top-10 routing to compile.\n[S — derived from reading all four hunks]\n\n---\n\n## 2. The two ADAPT files\n\n### 2.1 `SITE/ds4_topk.py` — 457 lines [M] (MANIFEST \"new (457)\" ✅ matches)\n\nFull path: `/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_topk.py`\n\n**Public interface** (all [S]):\n\n| Symbol | Line | Signature |\n|---|---|---|\n| `select_topk` | :441-457 | `(logits, topk_tokens, row_starts=None, row_ends=None, out=None) -> Tensor` — **the entry point**, docstring at :448 says \"Entry point used by `rocm_aiter_mla_sparse`. Honours `DS4_TOPK=0`.\" |\n| `topk_indices_ascending` | :280-354 | `(logits, topk_tokens, row_starts=None, row_ends=None, out=None) -> Tensor` — the Triton path |\n| `topk_indices_ascending_reference` | :367-402 | pure-torch definitional reference, tests only (\"slow\", :359) |\n| `topk_indices_torch_fallback` | :408-438 | \"The current production two-sort path, verbatim, for A/B and fallback\" (:413) |\n| `_topk_rows_kernel` | :111-268 | `@triton.jit`, one workgroup per row |\n| `_okey` / `_okey_torch` | :65-83 / :360-364 | order-preserving fp32→int32 key |\n\n**What it replaces in vLLM.** Module docstring :3-11: replaces *both*\n`_topk_indices_torch` (full stable descending sort) **and** `_canonicalize_topk_indices_`\n(second sort) in `vllm/v1/attention/ops/rocm_aiter_mla_sparse.py`. [S]\n\n**Wiring — not a monkeypatch.** It is a plain import behind an `lru_cache`d resolver\ninserted by the patch into `rocm_aiter_mla_sparse.py`:\n\n```python\n# patch:783-795\n+@functools.lru_cache\n+def _sparse_topk_impl():\n+    \"\"\"The gfx1151 deterministic top-k kernel, or None if it will not build.\"\"\"\n+    if os.environ.get(\"DS4_TOPK\") == \"0\":\n+        return None\n+    try:\n+        import ds4_topk\n+\n+        return ds4_topk.select_topk\n+    except Exception as exc:  # pragma: no cover - deployment guard\n+        print(f\"[ds4_topk] unavailable, using the torch two-sort path: {exc}\",\n+              flush=True)\n+        return None\n```\nConsumer wrapper `_sparse_topk(...)` at patch:798. [S]\nNote the **double kill-switch**: `DS4_TOPK == \"0\"` is checked both at patch:786 and\nindependently at `ds4_topk.py:40`. [S]\n\n**gfx1151-specific bits** [S]:\n- `_TILE = 2048`, `_NUM_WARPS = 8` (:54-55) with the wave-size reasoning at :51-53:\n  \"2048 fp32 = 8 KiB per iteration; with `num_warps=8` (**512 lanes at wave64**) that\n  is 4 elements/lane, which holds the `tl.cumsum` in the emit pass to 11 shuffle steps.\"\n  → **wave64 is an AMD/RDNA assumption baked into the tile size.**\n- `_HIST_MODE` / `DS4_TOPK_HIST` (:49, :43-48): `\"hist\"` = 8-bit digits/256 bins via\n  `tl.histogram`; `\"sum\"` = 4-bit/16 bins via masked `tl.sum`, existing because\n  \"`tl.histogram`'s lowering is the only part of this kernel whose **ROCm-backend\n  support** is not obvious from the Python source\" (:45-46).\n- `_PAD_TILE = 1024  # >= any topk we serve (512)` (:56) — hard-codes the DS4 top-512.\n\n**JIT-stall discipline (critical to replicate).** :27-30: \"no shape-dependent compile\nkey. Every size is a runtime argument marked `do_not_specialize`, so at most two kernel\nvariants are ever built (prefill with row bounds, decode without) and no decode step can\ntrigger a JIT stall.\" Enforced at :103-110:\n`do_not_specialize=[\"width\", \"topk\", \"logit_stride_row\", \"out_stride_row\"]`. [S]\n\n**Determinism contract** :13-24 and :235-243: no float accumulation, no atomics; output\nslot is an exact integer prefix count, \"a bijection onto `[0, n_sel)` that no scheduling\nchoice can perturb\". [S]\n\n### 2.2 `SITE/ds4_tl_indexer.py` — 594 lines [M] (⚠ MANIFEST:38 says \"new (476)\" — **STALE by 118 lines**)\n\nFull path: `/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_tl_indexer.py`\n\n**Public interface** (all [S]):\n\n| Symbol | Line | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fp8_mqa_logits_tl` | :314 | `(q, kv, weights, cu_seqlen_ks, cu_seqlen_ke)` — **prefill** indexer entry |\n| `fp8_paged_mqa_logits_tl` | :486 | `(q, kv_cache, weights, context_lens, block_tables, max_model_len)` — **decode** indexer entry |\n| `cached_bf16_weight` | :343 | `(weight, weight_scale, block_size, m)` — the hook (§2.3) |\n| `w8a8_block_bf16_direct` | :370 | `(x, weight, weight_scale, block_size, m)` — `DS4_W8A8_BF16_DIRECT` path |\n| `w8a8_block_fp8_bf16` | :390 | `(qx, weight, x_scale, weight_scale, block_size, output_dtype)` — `DS4_W8A8_BF16` path |\n| `_idx_qat` | :49 | hadamard128 + fp4 QAT round-trip |\n| `_build` / `_kernel` | :177 / :232 | prefill TileLang kernel + cache |\n| `_build_decode` / `_decode_kernel` | :259 / :292 | decode TileLang kernel + cache |\n| `_maybe_profile` / `_maybe_expert_union` | :95 / :84 | instrument activation hooks |\n\n**What it replaces in vLLM.** Docstring :2-4: \"Drop-in replacements for\n`fp8_mqa_logits_torch` / `fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch` (next_n==1), running the O(M*N)\ncompute on a bf16 WMMA TileLang kernel instead of a Python loop. Validated: prefill rel\n~1.6e-3, decode rel ~1e-7 vs the torch fallbacks.\" [S; the validation figures are CL]\n\n**Wiring — plain import, two env-gated early-returns in the patch** [S]:\n- decode: patch:717-722, `DS4_TL_DECODE` **default \"1\"** →\n  `return _tl.fp8_paged_mqa_logits_tl(...)`\n- prefill: patch:730-733, `DS4_TL_PREFILL` **default \"1\"** →\n  `return _tl.fp8_mqa_logits_tl(...)`\n- w8a8 GEMM: patch:1541-1543, `_DS4_W8A8_BF16` → `_tl.w8a8_block_fp8_bf16(...)`\n- w8a8 direct: patch:1496-1513, `_DS4_W8A8_BF16_DIRECT` → `_tl.w8a8_block_bf16_direct(...)`\n\nNote the patch **overrides `apply_weights`** on `TritonFp8BlockScaledMMKernel`\n(patch:1471-1532) — that is the one place this behaves like a subclass override rather\nthan a plain call, and it falls through with `return super().apply_weights(...)` at\npatch:1532. [S]\n\n**gfx1151-specific bits** [S]:\n- `_build(...)`: `block_Q = 1  # gfx1151: block_Q=1 + threads=256 validated correct at\n  H=64,D=128` (:179).\n- `_fit_config(block_Q, heads, D, budget=56*1024)` (:221): *\"Pick (block_N, num_stages)\n  so Q+K shared buffers fit **gfx1151's 64KB LDS**\"* (:222). Ladder `ns in (2,1)` ×\n  `bn in (128,64,32,16)` (:225-228), fallback `(16, 1)` (:229).\n- Decode constants `_DEC_BLOCK_N = 64`, `_DEC_THREADS = 256` (:255-256) with a\n  **correctness** warning at :251-254: *\"threads MUST be 256 here: at 128 threads\n  (2 warps) the block_N x heads(64) score tile is only partially computed -> WRONG\n  logits (verified: threads=128 gave max_abs_err ~3e2 vs 0.0 at 256; the sweep that\n  favored 128 measured only speed). block_N>=256 overflows the 64KB LDS.\"*\n- Bucketing to avoid hipcc recompiles: `_KV_BUCKET = 512` (:67, rationale :63-66) and\n  `_PREFILL_KV_BUCKET = 8192` (:312, rationale :305-311: *\"a ~2s hipcc recompile per\n  chunk with the GPU idle\"*).\n- `rocm_unquantized_gemm_impl` selected over `F.linear` for the wvSplitK skinny GEMM\n  (:407-412), with the profile note *\"Profiled 2026-07-12: aten::mm via Cijk_*MT16x16\n  = ~22% of decode GPU time\"* (:410) [CL].\n\n### 2.3 `cached_bf16_weight` hook — RE-PINNED\n\nRecord cited `:343-350`. **Re-pin: `ds4_tl_indexer.py:343-367`.**\n- `def cached_bf16_weight(weight, weight_scale, block_size, m):` — **:343** ✅ (record exact)\n- docstring — **:344-351** (record said 350; the docstring closes on **351**)\n- body — :352-367\n[M — `grep -n \"cached_bf16_weight\"` → 343, 383, 395]\n\n**Skip-during-cold-cache logic, quoted (:344-357):**\n\n```python\n    \"\"\"The bf16 dequantised copy of a block-scaled fp8 weight, or None.\n\n    None means \"do not take the bf16 path\". That happens when the cache is cold\n    and M is large: the startup memory-profiling forward runs at large M with an\n    empty cache, and building the copy there inflates the measured footprint and\n    shrinks the KV cache allocation. Decode (M <= 32) populates the cache;\n    prefill reuses entries that already exist unless DS4_W8A8_BF16_PREFILL=0.\n    \"\"\"\n    key = weight.data_ptr()\n    wb = _BF16_WCACHE.get(key)\n    if wb is not None:\n        return wb if (m <= 32 or _BF16_PREFILL) else None\n    if m > 32:\n        return None\n```\n[S]\n\n**Decision table** (derived from :352-357):\n\n| cache state | `m <= 32` (decode) | `m > 32` (prefill/profiling) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **warm** (hit) | return `wb` | return `wb` if `_BF16_PREFILL` else `None` |\n| **cold** (miss) | build + cache + return | **return `None`** ← the skip |\n\nSupporting state:\n- `_BF16_WCACHE = {}` at :339, keyed on `weight.data_ptr()` (:352) — *storage pointer*,\n  not module identity.\n- `_BF16_PREFILL = os.environ.get(\"DS4_W8A8_BF16_PREFILL\", \"1\") != \"0\"` at :342,\n  comment :340-341.\n- The `M <= 32` threshold appears **twice as a bare literal 32** (:355, :356) — no named\n  constant. A Qwen fork with different decode batch geometry must change both. [S]\n- Both callers honour `None`: `w8a8_block_bf16_direct` :384-385 returns `None` (caller\n  falls back), `w8a8_block_fp8_bf16` :396-399 falls back to `w8a8_triton_block_scaled_mm`.\n- The `M > 32` guard's purpose is restated independently in the patch at\n  patch:1493-1495: *\"Returns None (-> stock path) when the bf16 weight is not cached and\n  M is large, which is what keeps the startup memory-profiling forward on the fp8 path\n  and the KV cache allocation unchanged.\"* [S]\n\n### 2.4 hadamard128 / fp4_act_quant warning comments — TWO locations\n\n**Location A — `ds4_tl_indexer.py:9-21`** (the `DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL` header block) [S]:\n\n```python\n# --- DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL=1: reproduce the official DeepSeek-V4 indexer QAT graph ---\n# The official inference graph (HF snapshot inference/model.py Indexer.forward and\n# Compressor.forward with rotate=True) applies, to BOTH indexer Q rows and indexer\n# compressor K rows, after RoPE:\n#     x -> hadamard128(x) / sqrt(128) -> fp4_act_quant(x, block=32, inplace)   (QAT sim)\n# before the relu(q.k)*w scoring. ds4.c implements the same (dsv4_indexer_qat_*),\n# and its comment warns the top-k selection \"is not the model's graph\" without it.\n# vLLM's FP8 indexer path skips both steps. ...\n```\nThe literal warning phrase — *its comment warns the top-k selection \"is not the model's\ngraph\" without it* — is at **:15**. `fp4_act_quant` is named at **:13** and again at\n**:51**. The equivalence argument (power-of-two fp8 storage scale ⇒ score-time rotation\nis equivalent to pre-quant) is at :16-20. [S]\n\n**Location B — `ds4_tl_indexer.py:320-323`** (inside `fp8_mqa_logits_tl`) [S]:\n\n```python\n    # NOTE: the indexer QAT rotation (Hadamard-128) is applied PRE-fp8-quant in\n    # the fused q/compressor-K kernels (gated by DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL), not here — a\n    # score-time rotation is a no-op for the dot product (H is orthonormal). See\n    # ds4-vllm-indexer-qat-missing memory.\n```\n⚠ This **contradicts** Location A's :16-20 claim that applying it \"HERE, to the\ndequantized-unscaled rows at score time, is exactly equivalent\". Location B says it is\napplied in the fused kernels instead. Location B is the later/operative statement (the\nfunction body). Two more copies of the flag live in the patch at **patch:306** and\n**patch:532** (`_DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL = __import__(\"os\").environ.get(\"DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL\",\"0\") == \"1\"`),\ntargeting `fused_compress_quant_cache.py` and `fused_indexer_q.py` — consistent with\nLocation B. Debug prints at patch:361 and patch:626 (`[DS4_QAT] indexer-K/Q APPLY_QAT=…`). [S]\n\nImplementation: `_hadamard128_matrix` :27-36 (7× `torch.kron` of the 2×2 base, scaled\n`128**-0.5`), `_fp4_consts` :39-46 (levels `[0,.5,1,1.5,2,3,4,6]`, mids for\n`bucketize`), `_idx_qat` :49-61 (`amax` over `[-1,4,32]` blocks, `s = exp2(ceil(log2(amax/6)))`,\nclamp ±6, bucketize, rescale, → bf16). [S]\n\n---\n\n## 3. The three VENDOR instruments\n\nAll three are venv-top-level modules under `SITE/`, i.e. importable as bare names inside\nthe container. None uses an import hook or `sitecustomize`; all are lazily imported from\na call site. [S]\n\n### 3.1 `SITE/ds4_synctrace.py` — 93 lines [M] (MANIFEST \"new (93)\" ✅)\n\n**Activation: NO env var of its own.** Driven from\n`ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile` and therefore shares the `DS4_PROFILE` window.\nDocstring :22-23: *\"Driven from `ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile` so it shares the\nDS4_PROFILE window (no new env var, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\"* [S]\n\nCall chain [S]:\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:97` — `if os.environ.get(\"DS4_PROFILE\") != \"1\": return`\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:100` — `if _PCALLS == _PSTART` (default 60, :74)\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:104-105` — `import ds4_synctrace; ds4_synctrace.reset(); ds4_synctrace.install()`\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:119` — `elif _PCALLS == _PSTOP` (default 160, :75)\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:152-155` — `report(_steps)` then `uninstall()`;\n  `_steps = max((_PSTOP - _PSTART) / 21.0, 1e-9)   # 21 indexer calls/step` (:153)\n\n**Interface** [S]: `install()` :54 · `uninstall()` :66 · `reset()` :77 ·\n`report(steps=1.0) -> str` :81 (top-30 by frequency, :90).\n\n**Mechanism.** Monkeypatches `torch.Tensor` methods in place (`setattr(torch.Tensor,\nname, wrapper)` at :51; originals saved in `_orig` :50 and restored at :70).\nTargets, :35: `(\"item\", \"tolist\", \"cpu\", \"numpy\", \"nonzero\", \"__float__\", \"__int__\")`.\nEach wrapper records one `sys._getframe(1)` keyed\n`f\"{filename-after-site-packages}:{lineno} {co_name}() [{method}]\"` (:43-45). [S]\n\n**Stated limitation (:18-20)** — replicate this caveat verbatim: *\"boolean-mask indexing\n(`x[mask]`) reaches nonzero() inside C++ `at::index`, not through the python method, so\nit is NOT counted here.\"* [S]\n\nDesign justification :8-16: `with_stack=True` captures \"~3,200 ops per step, which pegged\nthe worker at 94% CPU\"; this is \"~25 events per step\". [CL]\n\n### 3.2 `SITE/ds4_expert_union.py` — 128 lines [M] (MANIFEST \"new (128)\" ✅)\n\n**Activation: `DS4_EXPERT_UNION=1`, plus a lazy install from the decode path.** [S]\n\nEnv surface, self-documented at :24-30 and implemented :38-41:\n\n| Var | Line | Default | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `DS4_EXPERT_UNION` | :38 | unset ⇒ **off** | `== \"1\"` enables |\n| `DS4_EU_START` | :39 | `200` | calls to skip (warmup + prefill) |\n| `DS4_EU_CALLS` | :40 | `2000` | window size in MoE calls (~46/decode step) |\n| `DS4_EU_OUT` | :41 | `~/vllm-prof` | output dir |\n\nTwo-stage gate — the module-level `_ENABLED` (:38, :99) **and** the caller's own check at\n`ds4_tl_indexer.py:86` (`if _EU_TRIED or os.environ.get(\"DS4_EXPERT_UNION\") != \"1\": return`).\nInstall is deliberately lazy; `ds4_tl_indexer.py:80-82` explains: *\"wrapping the fused_moe\nexperts module at ds4_tl_indexer import time would be circular, and by the first paged\ndecode the MoE layers are long since built.\"* [S]\n\n**Interface** [S]: `install()` :96 (idempotent, :99) · `_record(topk_ids,\nnum_local_experts)` :49 · `_flush()` :76. `atexit.register(_flush)` at :123.\n\n**What it monkeypatches** [S]: `vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts.\ngpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data` — rebound at :119\n(`m.make_routing_data = wrapped`), original stashed on `wrapped._ds4_orig` :118.\nWrapper signature :111: `(topk_ids, topk_weights, num_local_experts, *a, **kw)`.\n\n**Why this choke point** (:10-14): *\"It is NOT reachable through vLLM's own\n`--enable-return-routed-experts`: that capturer hangs off `BaseRouter.route()`, which\nthis model never calls (routing happens inside the triton_kernels path).\"* [S]\n\n**No-sync discipline** (:50, :66-73): device-only accumulation into a preallocated\n`[_CALLS, 3] int32` buffer (:64); slot 0 absorbs the `-1` padding *\"so no boolean mask\n(and therefore no size-dependent sync) is needed\"* (:66-67). Single `.cpu()` at\n`_flush` :83. Output TSV `expert_union_<pid>.tsv`, header\n`# n_rows\\tn_distinct\\tn_local_experts` (:85-90). [S]\n\nEvery failure path swallows the exception (:92, :105, :114-115) — *\"a probe must never\ntake the engine down\"* (:92). [S]\n\n### 3.3 `SITE/ds4_offload_batch.py` — 154 lines [M] (⚠ MANIFEST:78 says \"new (102)\" — **STALE by 52 lines**)\n\n**Activation: no env gate on the module — it is imported unconditionally by the patched\nconnector and configured by two env vars.** [S]\n\nImport site, `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/offloading/scheduler.py`\nvia patch:1934-1940:\n```python\n+        try:\n+            from ds4_offload_batch import (\n+                resolve_promote_block_budget,\n+                resolve_store_batch_tokens,\n+            )\n+        except ImportError:\n+            logger.warning(\n+                \"ds4_offload_batch not importable; store batches stay unbounded \"\n```\nCalled at patch:1948-1952. Comment at patch:1930-1932: *\"Imported inside the function,\nlike every other ds4_* helper: a missing module then degrades this one behaviour to stock\ninstead of breaking the import of the whole offloading connector.\"* [S]\n\n**Interface** [S] (`__all__` at :37-44):\n\n| Symbol | Line | Signature / value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `resolve_store_batch_tokens` | :82 | `(num_blocks, offloaded_block_sizes, frac=None) -> int \\| None` |\n| `resolve_promote_block_budget` | :114 | `(num_blocks, frac=None) -> int \\| None` |\n| `FRAC_ENV` | :46 | `\"DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\"` |\n| `PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV` | :47 | `\"DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\"` |\n| `DEFAULT_FRAC` | :52 | `0.25` |\n| `DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC` | :67 | `0.5` |\n| `_read_frac` / `_budget` | :70 / :139 | internal |\n\nBoth env reads go through `os.getenv(env)` at :73; `frac <= 0` ⇒ `None` ⇒ unbounded ⇒\n**stock vLLM** (:78-79 doc, :147-148 and :134-135 code). [S]\n\n**Torch-free by design** (:31-32): *\"This lives outside `vllm` so the budget arithmetic\nis unit-testable without importing torch or the connector's dependency graph.\"* Confirmed\n— the only import is `os` (:35). [M — `grep \"^import\"` → `import os` only]\n\nTwo non-obvious invariants worth lifting verbatim [S]:\n- **Store floor** (:100-109): the returned budget is `max(budget_tokens, max(sizes))`\n  (:154) and that floor \"is load-bearing, not a rounding nicety\" — below it a group's\n  target lands under its own cursor and `_build_store_jobs` assigns\n  `next_stored_block_idx = num_blocks` outright (\"it never takes a max\"), rewinding the\n  cursor and skipping blocks \"for good\".\n- **Promote counted in blocks, not tokens** (:119-127): a sliding-window group's tiny\n  numerous blocks \"dominate the rate and collapse the budget to a few hundred tokens --\n  about 6% of the prompt\".\n\n---\n\n## 4. Container discipline\n\n### 4.1 `container/Dockerfile` — 122 lines [M]\n\n**Base image pin — `container/Dockerfile:21`** [S]:\n```dockerfile\nARG DS4_BASE=\"docker.io/kyuz0/vllm-therock-gfx1151@sha256:25fd294fde9f729d1e75f109022ab4496c78190c0a6dc0142440529f7af20e4d\"\n```\n- Digest-pinned (not a tag). Drift guidance at :17-19.\n- Base ships vLLM commit `470229c` (:6, and label `ds4.vllm_commit=\"470229c\"` at :121).\n- Restated at `MANIFEST.md:3-4`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md:14`, `AGENTS.md:161`. [S]\n\n**Three build stages, all `FROM ${DS4_BASE}`** [S]:\n\n| Stage | Line | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rocr-idle-fix` | :26 | rebuild ROCr from `rocm-systems` @ `d34cbb64…` (:35) + cherry-picks `c06ea68a…`, `933596e9…`, `78b874d4…` (:37-39) + `rocr-force-block-indefinite-active-wait.patch` (:46-47) |\n| `provider-build` | :58 | rdma-core `-b v57.0` (:61) + thunderbolt-ibverbs @ `76ba39b6…` (:63); applies `packaging/rdma-core-patches/0*.patch` with `git apply -C1` (:65); asserts `libusb4_rdma-rdmav57.so` exists (:68) |\n| final | :70 | patch + overlay + copies |\n\nCherry-picks are made **reproducible** by pinning the committer date (:40-44):\n`GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=\"$(git show -s --format=%cI \"$commit\")\"` plus fixed\n`user.name`/`user.email`. Worth replicating. [S]\n\n### 4.2 How patches are applied at build — the two mechanisms\n\n```dockerfile\n# Dockerfile:75-77\nCOPY container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch /tmp/\nRUN cd / && git apply -p1 --whitespace=nowarn /tmp/vllm-upstream.patch && rm /tmp/vllm-upstream.patch\nCOPY --chown=root:root container/rootfs/ /\n```\n[S]\n\n1. **Modified files (31):** `git apply -p1` with CWD `/`. The patch paths are\n   container-absolute (`a/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/…`), so `-p1` strips\n   `a/` and resolves against `/`. Enforced by\n   `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py::test_patches_use_container_absolute_paths` (:185-194). [S]\n2. **New files (12):** `COPY container/rootfs/ /` — rootfs mirrors `/`. [S]\n\nOrdering matters and is invariant-checked: `test_modified_files_are_not_also_in_rootfs`\n(:99-103) — *\"A modified file present in rootfs would COPY over the patched one and\nsilently pin an older content.\"* [S]\n\nPost-steps: ROCr DSO overwrite (:81-83), usb4_rdma provider `.so` + `.driver` file\n(:89-91, rationale :85-88 — \"libibverbs matches a provider to a device BY NAME\"),\nhipcc/gcc build of `libtbv_ar2.so`/`libtbv_ar.so` (:99-106), stale-`__pycache__` purge\n(:111-113), OCI labels incl. `com.github.containers.toolbox=\"true\"` (:117). [S]\n\n⚠ **`MANIFEST.md:8` is stale and contradicts `Dockerfile:76`.** Do not lift the MANIFEST\nsentence \"The Dockerfile does not apply these; it COPYs the final files from ../rootfs.\"\nThe Dockerfile's own comment at :72-74 is correct. [S]\n\n### 4.3 `container/patches/MANIFEST.md` — 100 lines [M], structure to replicate\n\n- **:1-18 header.** Base digest + vLLM commit (:3-4); the three-way count claim\n  (:6 \"31 modified\", :10 \"12 new\", :12-14 one deliberately excluded byte-identical file\n  `aiter_meta/csrc/cpp_itfs/utils.py`); path convention note (:16-18).\n- **:20-99 eight themed tables**, each `| file | Δ | purpose |`:\n\n| § | Line | Theme | Rows |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| DeepSeek-V4 model (AMD/gfx1151) | :20 | model path | 8 |\n| Sparse indexer / mid-context retrieval | :32 | **contains `_routing`'s siblings + ds4_topk/tl_indexer/synctrace/expert_union** | 6 |\n| MoE / GEMM kernel tuning | :42 | **contains `_routing_compute.py` @ :47** | 6 |\n| Distributed all-reduce over TB4 RDMA | :52 | tbv | 3 |\n| Scheduler / KV / cudagraph / MTP | :59 | | 5 |\n| Disk KV cache (`fs_lru`, distributed) | :68 | | 10 |\n| OpenAI API: reasoning + tools | :82 | | 4 |\n| Kernel config lookup | :90 | | 1 |\n| ROCr / HIP idle CPU fixes | :96 | build-stage replacement | 1 |\n\n- **Δ column grammar:** `+N` when no deletions, `+N/-M` otherwise, or `**new (LINES)**`.\n  Machine-checked for modified rows (§4.5); **not** checked for new rows (§4.4).\n- Purpose cells carry the *engineering rationale in prose* — e.g. :71 records the\n  measured failure the `fs_lru` tier fixes (\"0/8 needle recall vs 8/8 fresh at 100%\n  reported hits\"). This is the density the campaign should replicate. [S]\n\n### 4.4 ⚠ Three \"new (N)\" counts are wrong — MEASURED\n\n`wc -l` on every rootfs file vs the MANIFEST cell:\n\n| File | MANIFEST says | `wc -l` says | |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ds4_tl_indexer.py` (:38) | `new (476)` | **594** | ✗ off by 118 |\n| `ds4_offload_batch.py` (:78) | `new (102)` | **154** | ✗ off by 52 |\n| `vllm/models/deepseek_v4/amd/dspark_mtp.py` (:26) | `new (885)` | **932** | ✗ off by 47 |\n| `ds4_topk.py` (:37) | `new (457)` | 457 | ✓ |\n| `ds4_synctrace.py` (:39) | `new (93)` | 93 | ✓ |\n| `ds4_expert_union.py` (:40) | `new (128)` | 128 | ✓ |\n| `lru_manager.py` (:71) | `new (485)` | 485 | ✓ |\n| `distributed.py` (:72) | `new (345)` | 345 | ✓ |\n| `opt_flags_amd.py` (:46) | `new (57)` | 57 | ✓ |\n| `gfx1151-GEMM-A8W8_BLOCKSCALE.json` (:50) | `new (15)` | 15 | ✓ |\n| `tbv_ar.py` (:56) | `new (255)` | 255 | ✓ |\n| `tbv_ar2.py` (:57) | `new (69)` | 69 | ✓ |\n[M — literal `wc -l` output]\n\n**Root cause, pinned:** `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py:166-183`\n(`test_manifest_deltas_match_their_patches`) short-circuits on `if \"new\" in delta:\ncontinue` (:173). The Δ audit covers modified rows only. **A Qwen fork replicating this\ndiscipline should extend the test to assert new-row line counts against `wc -l`** — it is\na ~4-line addition and closes a live drift. [S]\n\n### 4.5 `container/verify-patches.sh` — 95 lines [M]: how it proves base → rootfs\n\n**It proves base → *patched*, not base → rootfs.** The two halves are separate. [S]\n\nMechanism, in order:\n1. :29 — reads the base digest **out of the Dockerfile** with\n   `sed -n 's/^ARG DS4_BASE=\"\\(.*\\)\"$/\\1/p' container/Dockerfile`, \"so the two cannot\n   diverge\" (:14). Single source of truth.\n2. :33-37 — `podman image exists \"$BASE\"` or bail (exit 2) with the pull hint (~35 GB).\n3. :55 — file list derived **from the patch itself**:\n   `sed -n \"s|^--- a/$SITE/||p\" \"$COMBINED\" | sort -u`.\n4. :65-67 — **one** container invocation extracts all base originals:\n   `podman run --rm --entrypoint sh \"$BASE\" -c \"cd /$SITE && tar cf - <paths>\" | tar xf - -C \"$WORK/$SITE\"`.\n   Comment :64: \"per-file `podman run` is ~1s each\".\n5. :90-93 — the proof:\n   `git -C \"$WORK\" apply -p1 \"$COMBINED\"` — *\"exactly as the Dockerfile will\"* (:88).\n   `-C \"$WORK\"` is required \"so the stripped paths resolve inside the work tree rather\n   than this repo (itself a git checkout)\" (:88-89).\n6. :95 — success line: `vllm-upstream.patch applies cleanly to the base (N files)`.\n\n**Regeneration mode `--write`** (:43-52, :70-85): file list comes from MANIFEST instead\n(regex `\\| \\`([^`]+)\\` \\| (?!\\*\\*new)` at :48), diffs `$WORK` (base) against\n`$DS4_PATCH_SRC` (desired final files) with explicit `--label a/… --label b/…` (:77) so\nthe emitted paths stay container-absolute. Prints a reminder to update the Δ column\n(:82-83). [S]\n\n**Division of labour, stated at :15-16:** *\"The offline half of these checks -- manifest\nvs overlay vs Dockerfile counts -- lives in tests/test_patchset_packaging.py and needs no\nimage.\"* [S]\n\n### 4.6 `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py` — 233 lines, 12 tests, all passing [M]\n\n```\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_patchset_packaging.py' -v\n… Ran 12 tests in 0.030s\nOK\n```\n[M — literal output]\n\nThe 12 invariants (the reusable discipline) [S]:\n\n| Test | Line | Invariant |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_overlay_is_not_empty` | :63 | guards vacuous passes (`>5` overlay, `>20` rows) |\n| `test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay` | :69 | no `.pyc` / `__pycache__` — COPY would bake stale bytecode |\n| `test_every_overlay_file_is_documented` | :79 | overlay ⊆ manifest |\n| `test_every_documented_file_ships` | :88 | manifest ⊆ (overlay ∪ patch sections ∪ `NOT_IN_OVERLAY`) |\n| `test_modified_files_are_not_also_in_rootfs` | :99 | patch ∩ overlay = ∅ |\n| `test_manifest_header_counts_match_the_tables` | :105 | \"31 modified\"/\"12 new\" headers vs row counts |\n| `test_dockerfile_file_count_matches_the_overlay` | :126 | Dockerfile's *prose* counts (`overlays the (\\d+) new files`, `vllm-upstream\\.patch, (\\d+) files`) vs reality |\n| `test_every_modified_file_has_a_reviewable_diff` | :153 | every modified row has a patch section |\n| `test_manifest_deltas_match_their_patches` | :166 | **Δ cells recomputed from the diff** (:178-180) — comment :169 notes \"how 11 of these came to disagree at once\" |\n| `test_patches_use_container_absolute_paths` | :185 | all `--- ` lines start `--- a/opt/venv/…` |\n| `test_every_patch_file_names_a_shipped_file` | :196 | no orphan `vllm__*.patch`; \"Map forwards, never backwards\" (:197-199) |\n| `test_overlay_python_compiles` | :214 | `py_compile` every overlay `.py`, **cfile into a tempdir** (:218-219) so it does not break the bytecode test |\n\n`NOT_IN_OVERLAY = {\"_rocm_sdk_core/lib/libhsa-runtime64.so.1\"}` (:31-34) — the one\nmanifest row built by a Dockerfile stage. [S]\n\n`container/build.sh:13-17` runs this suite **before** `podman build` and aborts on\nfailure. [S]\n\n**Measured counts** [M]:\n- `grep -c \"^--- a/\" container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch` → **31** (unique: 31)\n- `find container/rootfs -type f | wc -l` → **12**\n- `grep -c '\\*\\*new' container/patches/MANIFEST.md` → **12**\n\n---\n\n## 5. `host/` — every file, one line each, plus the env/perf inventory\n\n### 5.1 File inventory\n\n| Path | Lines | Purpose (pinned) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `host/ds4-config.yaml` | 18 | Site config; flat `key: value` only, \"parsed by ds4-config with the Python stdlib, no pyyaml\" (:3-4) |\n| `host/ds4-config` | 27 | `#!/usr/bin/python3`; each `key: value` → `export DS4_<KEY>=<shlex.quote(value)>` (:23-27). Used as `eval \"$(\"$HOME/ds4-config\")\"` (:4) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh` | 148 | **Canonical env**, sourced by ray head, box2 ray worker, and `vllm serve` (:2-3) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-env.rdma.sh` | 25 | `source`s base then pins one unambiguous `NCCL_IB_HCA` (:8-9) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-env.tcp.sh` | 13 | `source`s base, disables IB + both tbv all-reduces (:7-13) — correctness/fallback profile |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-restart.sh` | 145 | Full bringup: teardown → containers → ray → serve → verify (:2) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-down.sh` | 35 | The stop half, idempotent (:2-5) |\n| `host/container-heal.sh` | 29 | Reconciles \"podman says Up but crun is dead (conmon SIGKILLed)\" (:3-4); always exits 0 (:7) |\n| `host/ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh` | 130 | The `vllm serve` launcher; runs **inside** the container (:2). \"THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH\" (:6) |\n| `host/ds4-vllm-warmup.py` | 77 | 2-phase post-start warmup (tiny request, then one `DS4_WARMUP_CTX` prefill) |\n| `host/systemd/ds4-vllm.service` | 23 | `Type=oneshot`, `RemainAfterExit=yes`, ExecStart/Stop/StopPost |\n\n### 5.2 `ds4-config.yaml` keys — all 14 (`:5-18`) [S]\n\n| Key | Line | Value | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `model` | :5 | `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731` | \"weights needed on BOTH boxes\" |\n| `transport` | :6 | `rdma` | `rdma \\| tcp` — selects `ds4-cluster-env.<transport>.sh` |\n| `head_ip` | :7 | `192.168.100.1` | |\n| `worker_ip` | :8 | `192.168.100.2` | |\n| `container` | :9 | `vllm` | podman container name, same both boxes |\n| `rdma_hca` | :10 | `usb4_rdma0` | `NCCL_IB_HCA` pin, rdma only |\n| `api_port` | :11 | `1234` | |\n| `disk_kv` | :12 | `true` | fs_lru NVMe prefix-KV tier |\n| `disk_kv_gib` | :13 | `30` | **per-NODE** disk cap |\n| `max_ctx` | :14 | `524288` | `--max-model-len`, \"the validated profile\" |\n| `kv_pin_gib` | :15 | `6` | pinned GPU KV pool |\n| `gpu_mem_util` | :16 | `0.83` | **\"IGNORED while the KV pin above is set\"** |\n| `warmup_ctx` | :17 | `2048` | 0 disables |\n| `cables` | :18 | `1` | TB cables; 2 dedicates second NHI to RX zero-copy rail |\n\n### 5.3 The env/perf settings inventory the campaign asked for — each pinned\n\n| Setting | Pin | Value | Why (quoted/paraphrased from the file) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **`PYTHONHASHSEED`** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:13` | `0` | :9-12 — \"vLLM derives NONE_HASH (the prefix-cache chain seed) from it, so without a fixed value identical token content produces different block filenames every run and the disk cache can never hit across a restart\" |\n| **`PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF` expandable_segments** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:27` | `expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85` | :14-26 — GC off by default on a UMA box; 0.85 of ~124 GiB ≈ reclaim at ~105 GiB; expandable_segments is \"the fragmentation half\"; \"Safe with `--enforce-eager` (no graph capture)\" |\n| **`HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT`** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:83` | `${DS4_HSA_INTERRUPT:-1}` | :79-82 — \"TheRock ROCm busy-polls (rocr InterruptSignal::WaitRelaxed) -> ~2-3 cores spinning during inference -> CPU thermal throttle. Set 0 to revert to spin\" |\n| **Cache dirs off tmpfs (Triton/Inductor)** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:49-50` | `TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/torchinductor`, `TRITON_CACHE_DIR=$HOME/.triton/cache` | :45-48 — \"the defaults land under /tmp (tmpfs), and the first bringup after a boot then recompiles every kernel -- ~25 min CPU-bound in LLVM before the API can answer\" |\n| **Cache dir off tmpfs (KV staging)** | `host/ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh:104` | `DS4_OFFLOAD_MMAP_DIR=${KVDIR%/}-stage` | :99-103 — must be a **SIBLING** of the cache dir, never inside it: \"fs_lru owns root_dir exclusively… will `os.remove()` it when it becomes the LRU victim. Nesting staging under root_dir therefore hands the evictor the live mmap.\" Implementation: `patch:2443` |\n| **Per-call-invariant latching (MoE)** | `patch:1261-1288` + `opt_flags_amd.py:13-28` + `patch:1384-1433` | 3 device queries + 7 env reads + 4 target queries | patch:1249-1260; justified by \"must be exported before `ray start` so both TP ranks agree, so a per-call read cannot observe anything a first-use read would not\" |\n| **Per-call-invariant latching (W8A8 flags)** | `patch:1449-1459` | `_DS4_W8A8_BF16`, `_DS4_W8A8_BF16_DIRECT` at import | patch:1449-1451 — \"a per-call lookup buys nothing and costs ~255 os.environ hits per decode step\" |\n| `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` surgery | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:89-96` | strips **only** `/opt/rocm/llvm/lib` | :84-88 — that path's runtimes \"change ROCr's initialization order and reproduce the AsyncEventsLoop spin even with the patched DSO preloaded\" |\n| `LD_PRELOAD` of patched ROCr | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:103-116` | prepends `…/_rocm_sdk_core/lib/libhsa-runtime64.so.1` | :97-102; `DS4_HSA_PRELOAD=0` disables only the preload |\n| `HSA_ENABLE_MWAITX` | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:121` | `${DS4_HSA_MWAITX:-0}` | :117-120 — optional fallback for *finite* active waits |\n| `PYTHONWARNINGS` | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:28` | append `ignore::FutureWarning` | :5-8 — per-step `all_gather_into_tensor` deprecation → journal spam |\n| `VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY` | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:78` | `DS4_` | :77 — \"propagate DS4_* to box2 ray workers (not in ray's default copy prefixes)\" — **essential**, without it the two TP ranks diverge |\n| NCCL/RDMA block | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:29-41` | `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=thunderbolt0`, `NCCL_IB_HCA=usb4_rdma`, `NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=1`, `NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_NET_GDR_LEVEL=0`, `NCCL_IB_TIMEOUT=23`, `NCCL_PROTO=LL`, `NCCL_ALGO=Ring`, `NCCL_IB_RETRY_CNT=7`, `TORCH_NCCL_HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_SEC=2400`, `TORCH_NCCL_ENABLE_MONITORING=0`, `NCCL_TIMEOUT_MS=2400000` | — |\n| Ray block | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:42-44` | `RAY_EXPERIMENTAL_NOSET_ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1`, `RAY_memory_monitor_refresh_ms=0`, `RAY_memory_usage_threshold=0.99` | — |\n| Misc | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:51-53` | `HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0`, `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0`, `VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800` | — |\n\n### 5.4 ⚠ `ds4-cluster-env.sh` MoE knobs — record cite `:127` RE-PINNED\n\nRecord cited \":127 MoE knobs\". At `:127` sits the **comment header**, not the exports:\n\n- `:127-130` — comment: *\"MXFP4 matmul_ogs DECODE kernel config (tuned on this hardware;\n  block_k 256 + num_stages 2 is the bandwidth lever the stock heuristic never picks).\n  Decode-scoped in opt_flags (only under block_m<128) so prefill is untouched. MUST live\n  here so BOTH TP ranks match. Unset the 5 vars to revert.\"*\n- `:144-148` — the **actual exports** (five of them) [S]:\n\n```bash\nexport DS4_MOE_BN=${DS4_MOE_BN:-32}\nexport DS4_MOE_NW=${DS4_MOE_NW:-2}\nexport DS4_MOE_NS=${DS4_MOE_NS:-2}\nexport DS4_MOE_BK=${DS4_MOE_BK:-256}\nexport DS4_MOE_WPE=${DS4_MOE_WPE:-1}\n```\n\n`opt_flags.py` reads **seven** `DS4_MOE_*` keys (patch:1288: `BM, BN, NW, NS, BK,\nKEEP_MFMA, WPE`) but the env file exports only **five**. `DS4_MOE_BM` and\n`DS4_MOE_KEEP_MFMA` are implemented-but-never-deployed. The comment at :130 saying\n\"the 5 vars\" is consistent with the env file, not with the reader. [M/S]\n\nAlso note :131-135 places the `DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL` comment **inside** the MoE comment\nblock — the two are textually interleaved and easy to misread when lifting.\n\n### 5.5 Cluster restart script — the two things it encodes (`ds4-cluster-restart.sh:8-23`)\n\nBoth are quoted verbatim in the header and both are non-obvious [S]:\n\n1. **REAPING** (:10-15). `ds4-vllm-manual` is a transient `systemd-run` unit supervising\n   a `podman exec` **wrapper**, not the process inside the container. Stopping the unit\n   \"leaves `vllm serve` running, holding its port and ~0.4 GB. Repeated restarts strand\n   one husk each.\" Implementation :63-69: `ps` + bracket-grep `bin/[v]llm serve deepseek`\n   (:63, trick documented at :62), SIGTERM → 3s → SIGKILL, then a **hard gate**:\n   `[ \"$residual\" -eq 0 ] || { … exit 1; }` (:69).\n2. **RAY WORKER POOL** (:17-23). `ray start` passes\n   `--num_prestart_python_workers=<num_cpus>` through with \"no env override\n   (ray/_private/services.py:1980)\"; unbounded that is \"32 idle Python workers at ~40 MB\n   each, ~1.28 GB that vLLM never touches\". Fix: `RAY_NUM_CPUS=${RAY_NUM_CPUS:-4}` (:38)\n   → `--num-cpus=$RAY_NUM_CPUS` (:92). Dashboard off for the same reason (:93).\n\nOther pinned structure [S]: config load :31 · `box2()`/`inbox()` ssh/podman helpers\n:54-55 · memory drain loop with `<45G` gate :74-80 · `container-heal.sh` on both boxes\n:84-85 · head-only `--include-dashboard=false` (:93, \"ray PANICs if it is passed to a\nworker\" :91) · **2-GPU gate** :103-108 (aborts if `ray status` never reports `2.0 GPU`)\n· `systemd-run --user --unit=ds4-vllm-manual` :112-115 · API poll 105×20s ≈ 35 min\n:119-125 (warm ≈4 min, cold-kernel-cache ≈+25 min, :117-118) · warmup dispatched as a\nseparate `--collect` transient unit :130-135 · verify block :137-145 incl. the RDMA\nreadiness grep `tbv_ar2: rank[0-9] ready \\(qpn=…\\)` (:141) which prints\n`!! tbv_ar2 NOT ready -- decode all-reduce is not on RDMA` on miss (:142).\n\n### 5.6 Teardown (`ds4-cluster-down.sh`) [S]\n\nIdempotent (:5). Tolerates a broken config: `eval … 2>/dev/null || true` with hardcoded\nfallbacks (:12-16). Same reap loop (:23-27), then `ray stop --force` locally (:29-30) and\nover ssh (:31-32). `exit 0` unconditionally (:34).\n\n### 5.7 Warmup (`ds4-vllm-warmup.py`) [S]\n\nEnv: `DS4_VLLM_PORT` (:13, dflt `1234`), `DS4_WARMUP_MODEL` (:14, dflt\n`deepseek-v4-flash`), `DS4_WARMUP_CTX` (:17, dflt `2048`), `DS4_WARMUP` (:50, dflt `1`;\n`0` disables). `wait_ready(timeout_s=1200)` :24. Two phases: (1) `fire(\"Say ACK.\", 12,\n300)` :60 — \"compiles the ~50 vLLM Triton kernels (topk/w8a8/sparse-attn/metadata) +\ndecode + MTP drafter\" (:55-57); (2) one `WARMUP_CTX`-sized prefill :69 — \"one long\nprefill grows context through every 8192-bucket\" (:64), which matches\n`_PREFILL_KV_BUCKET = 8192` at `ds4_tl_indexer.py:312`. Every phase wrapped in\ntry/except (:58-62, :67-72) — \"Best-effort: never fails the service\" (:9).\n\n### 5.8 systemd unit (`host/systemd/ds4-vllm.service`) [S]\n\n`Type=oneshot` + `RemainAfterExit=yes` (:14-15); `TimeoutStartSec=45min` (:16),\n`TimeoutStopSec=5min` (:17). `ExecStart=%h/ds4-cluster-restart.sh` (:18),\n`ExecStop=%h/ds4-cluster-down.sh` (:19), **`ExecStopPost=%h/ds4-cluster-down.sh`** (:23)\nwith the reason at :20-22: *\"ExecStop does not run when ExecStart itself fails; StopPost\ndoes, so a failed bringup still tears the cluster down instead of leaving the serve unit\nand ray daemons running behind a 'failed' wrapper.\"*\n**No `[Install]` section** — deliberate, :9-11: \"the model takes minutes to load and\nclaims both GPUs, so the stack comes up only on an explicit start, never at boot.\nhy3-llamacpp declares `Conflicts=ds4-vllm.service`\".\n\n### 5.9 Serve flags (`ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh:111-130`) [S]\n\n`--tensor-parallel-size 2` :113 · `--distributed-executor-backend ray` :114 ·\n**`--enforce-eager` :115** · `--kv-cache-dtype fp8` :116 ·\n`--gpu-memory-utilization ${DS4_GPU_UTIL:-0.83}` :117 ·\n`--kv-cache-memory-bytes ${DS4_KV_BYTES:-6442450944}` :118 ·\n`--max-model-len ${DS4_MAX_CTX:-524288}` :119 · **`--max-num-batched-tokens 512`** :120 ·\n`--tokenizer-mode/--reasoning-parser/--tool-call-parser deepseek_v4` :122-127 ·\n`--speculative-config '{\"method\":\"deepseek_mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5,\n\"disable_padded_drafter_batch\":true,\"enforce_eager\":true}'` :128.\n\nThree memory notes worth lifting (:9-20): `--kv-cache-memory-bytes` must be pinned\nbecause \"the bf16 weight cache and the RDMA buffers are allocated AFTER the profiling\npass\"; `--gpu-memory-utilization` is \"INERT while the pin above is set … (gpu_worker.py:384)\";\n`--max-num-batched-tokens 512` **not** 2048 because \"the indexer/top-k workspace scales\nwith batch x context and 2048 costs ~10 GiB more at 256K\".\n\n⚠ Syntax landmine, :22-24: *\"Do not add comments inside the backslash-continued `vllm\nserve` command below: a '#' there silently comments out every remaining argument, and\n`bash -n` still reports the file as valid.\"*\n\nPre-flight degrade check :86-92: if the image lacks `lru_manager.py` **or**\n`distributed.py`, warn loudly and set `DS4_DISK_KV=0` rather than let `vllm serve` die on\n`\"Unknown secondary tier type: 'fs_lru'\"` (:81-85).\n\n---\n\n## 6. `AGENTS.md` bring-up doctrine\n\n### 6.1 §0.1 prerequisites boundary — quoted verbatim (`AGENTS.md:35-45`)\n\n> ## 0.1 Prerequisites (verify these exist; do NOT try to synthesize them)\n>\n> - **2× AMD Strix Halo / gfx1151**, ~128 GB unified memory each, on the same LAN.\n> - A **Thunderbolt-4 / USB4 cable** physically connecting the two boxes.\n> - Linux with **kernel headers/devel** for the running kernel on each box, `podman`,\n>   `distrobox`, `rdma-core`/`libibverbs`, `git`, build toolchain.\n> - The model weights **`deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731`** (~150 GB) downloaded\n>   on **both** boxes (`hf download deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731`).\n> - Root/sudo on both boxes (kernel modules, systemd units).\n> - **Secure Boot disabled on both boxes** — the tbv modules are unsigned;\n>   a Secure Boot kernel will refuse every `insmod` in §1.\n\n[S] The boundary is in the heading itself: **\"verify these exist; do NOT try to\nsynthesize them\"** (:35). Followed by the role-fixing paragraph :47-51 (\"Pick roles now\nand keep them consistent everywhere\").\n\n### 6.2 §1.5 RDMA gate — quoted verbatim (`AGENTS.md:134-150`)\n\n> ### 1.5 Verify RDMA (gate)\n>\n> ```bash\n> ls /sys/class/infiniband/                 # -> usb4_rdma0 (or usb4_rdma5)\n> rdma link                                 # port state ACTIVE / PHYS_STATE LinkUp\n> cat /sys/class/infiniband/usb4_rdma0/ports/1/gids/1   # NON-zero (RoCEv2 IPv4 GID = index 1)\n> ibv_devices                               # lists usb4_rdma0\n> ```\n> If `gids/1` is all-zero, `thunderbolt0` has no `192.168.100.x` IP yet — fix the IP\n> first. If `usb4_rdma*` never appears after a kernel change, the `.ko` vermagic no\n> longer matches: rebuild (§1.1–1.2) and `sudo systemctl restart tbv-roce.service`\n> on both boxes.\n>\n> **De-risk option:** RDMA is a performance layer, not a correctness gate — set\n> `transport: tcp` in `~/ds4-config.yaml` to run the same cluster over sockets\n> (much slower decode). If you want to validate the model path first, skip to\n> §2–§4 on TCP now and return to finish RDMA once tokens are flowing.\n\n[S] **The de-risk clause (:147-150) is what makes the campaign's RDMA exclusion legal:\nthe document itself declares RDMA non-load-bearing for correctness.**\n\n### 6.3 Full gate order\n\nDeclared layer order, `AGENTS.md:27-33` [S]:\n> Three independent layers, build/verify them in this order:\n> 1. **tbv RDMA** (`tbv/`) … \"Foundational and the riskiest; do it first.\"\n> 2. **vLLM engine** (`container/`)\n> 3. **Host orchestration** (`host/`)\n\nEnumerated gates in document order [S]:\n\n| # | Gate | Pin | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G0 | Prerequisites present (not synthesized) | :35-45 | all six bullets, incl. Secure Boot **disabled** |\n| G0.2 | Recall/context integrity | :55-68 | `DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL=1` on **both** ranks; `deepseek_v4_encoding.py` patch present |\n\n[Showing lines 1-875 of 1274 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=876 to continue.]"}],"details":{"truncation":{"content":"# ds4-vllm lift manifest — exact, pinned\n\n**Source tree:** `/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm`\n**Revision:** `a8f620d3032b23271b1969123168a561d0fd882a` (`git rev-parse HEAD`, 2026-08-28)\n**Working tree:** clean (`git status --porcelain` → empty output) [M]\n**Upstream license:** Apache-2.0 (`LICENSE:1-4` = Apache License Version 2.0) [S]\n**Tree size:** 57 files, 13,351 lines total (`find … | xargs wc -l`) [M]\n\nEvidence grades: **[S]** read from source this session · **[M]** measured (command + literal\noutput) · **[CL]** claimed by a doc in-tree, not independently verified.\n\nAll patch line numbers below are line offsets **into**\n`container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch` (2,717 lines) unless a `b/` target path is named.\nAll rootfs paths are abbreviated `SITE = container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Executive corrections to the campaign record\n\nThree record claims do **not** survive re-pinning. Details in the numbered sections.\n\n| # | Record said | On-disk at `a8f620d` | Grade |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10 | \"piecewise-cudagraph eager-break around the TP all-reduce, commit `671e659`\" | **No such hunk, no such commit.** `grep -rn 671e659 .` → zero hits. The only `breakable_cudagraph.py` change is a `DS4_BREAKABLE_SYNC` stream-sync loop (patch:1777-1802). The \"eager break\" text is an *unchanged upstream context line* (patch:204). And production runs `--enforce-eager` (`host/ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh:115`), so `replay()` is inert. | [M]/[S] |\n| 4 | MANIFEST is authoritative on how patches apply | `MANIFEST.md:8` says \"The Dockerfile does **not** apply these; it `COPY`s the final files from `../rootfs`.\" **False.** `container/Dockerfile:76` runs `git apply -p1 … vllm-upstream.patch`. MANIFEST.md:8 is stale. | [S] |\n| 7 | \"`build-modules.sh` pin lines for thunderbolt-ibverbs **and rdma-core**\" | `build-modules.sh` pins **no** rdma-core. rdma-core lives only in `container/Dockerfile:61` and is pinned to a **branch tag `v57.0`**, not a commit SHA. | [M]/[S] |\n\nPlus: **3 of 12 MANIFEST \"new (N)\" line counts are wrong** (§4.4), and `AGENTS.md` §0.2\ntwice cites a \"§5\" that does not exist in the file (§6).\n\n---\n\n## 1. The routing power-of-2 fix (the one MANDATORY patch)\n\n### 1.1 Location — re-pinned, record confirmed\n\nRecord cited \"~line 1353\". **Exact.**\n\n```\n$ grep -n \"_routing_compute\" container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch\n1353:--- a/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/routing_details/_routing_compute.py\n1354:+++ b/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/routing_details/_routing_compute.py\n```\n[M]\n\n- Target file: `vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/routing_details/_routing_compute.py` [S]\n- Single hunk header: `@@ -55,9 +55,11 @@` at patch:**1355** [S]\n- Hunk body: patch:**1356-1368** [S]\n- Δ per MANIFEST: `+4/-2` (`MANIFEST.md:47`); verified by\n  `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py::test_manifest_deltas_match_their_patches` which\n  **passes** (§4.5) [M]\n\n### 1.2 The hunk, quoted verbatim (patch:1355-1368)\n\n```diff\n@@ -55,9 +55,11 @@\n \n     tl.static_assert(N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M <= 32768)\n \n-    local_offs = tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)\n+    N_GATES_PAD: tl.constexpr = triton.next_power_of_2(N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)\n+    local_offs = tl.arange(0, N_GATES_PAD)\n+    in_block = local_offs < N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M\n     offs = pid_m * BLOCK_M * N_EXPTS_ACT + local_offs\n-    expert = tl.load(ExptIndx + offs, mask=(offs < n_gates), other=-1).to(tl.uint32)\n+    expert = tl.load(ExptIndx + offs, mask=(offs < n_gates) & in_block, other=-1).to(tl.uint32)\n \n     # stable-sort by expert ID:\n     kv_pairs = ((expert << 16) | local_offs).to(tl.uint32)\n```\n[S]\n\n**Mechanism.** Triton's `tl.arange(0, X)` requires `X` to be a power of two. When\n`N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M` is not a power of two (top-k routing where `N_EXPTS_ACT` is e.g.\n6 or 10), the stock line is a compile-time failure. The fix rounds the lane count *up* to\n`N_GATES_PAD = next_power_of_2(...)` and re-introduces the true bound as an explicit\npredicate `in_block`, AND-ed into the load mask so padded lanes read `other=-1`. The\nsubsequent `kv_pairs = ((expert << 16) | local_offs)` stable-sort is unchanged and safe\nbecause `-1 → 0xFFFFFFFF` as uint32 sorts to the tail. [S, inference from the quoted code]\n\n**Why it is mandatory for top-10 routing:** exactly because `10 * BLOCK_M` is never a\npower of two for any power-of-two `BLOCK_M`. [S — reasoning from `tl.arange` semantics\nvisible in the diff; the *claim* that it is mandatory is the campaign's, graded CL]\n\n### 1.3 Adjacent hunks it depends on (the MoE \"latching\" set)\n\nThe MoE/GEMM section of `MANIFEST.md:42-50` groups five files. `_routing_compute.py` is\none of them. Its true build-order dependency is on `target_info.py`, because\n`opt_flags.py` and `opt_flags_amd.py` both import `get_cdna_version` **from**\n`triton_kernels.target_info` and the patch *renames* the originals.\n\n**(a) `target_info.py` — patch:1369-1433** (Δ `+39/-4`, `MANIFEST.md:48`) [S]\nTwo hunks: `@@ -23,8 +23,30 @@` (patch:1371) and `@@ -41,14 +63,27 @@` (patch:1403).\nIt renames the three `@triton.constexpr_function` originals to `_*_uncached`\n(patch:1399, 1408, 1414) and republishes plain-Python memoised wrappers\n(patch:1418-1433) over a `_DS4_CACHE` dict + `_DS4_MISS` sentinel (patch:1384-1394).\nThe sentinel is load-bearing and the code says so: *\"has_tma_gather/has_native_mxfp\nreturn False on ROCm, and a falsy cached value must still count as a hit or nothing\nmemoises\"* (patch:1389-1390). [S]\n\n> **Hard dependency for a fork.** Anything importing `get_cdna_version` now gets a\n> *non-constexpr* function. The patch's own comment (patch:1381-1383) states the\n> originals are retained \"in case anything needs the constexpr form from inside a\n> `@triton.jit` body -- nothing in this tree does (verified by grep)\". A Qwen fork\n> that adds a jit body calling `get_cdna_version()` would break. [S]\n\n**(b) `opt_flags.py` — patch:1236-1352** (Δ `+72/-3`, `MANIFEST.md:45`) [S]\nFive hunks: `@@ -1,11 +1,54 @@` (1238), `@@ -55,7 +98,7 @@` (1293),\n`@@ -95,7 +138,7 @@` (1302), `@@ -104,6 +147,32 @@` (1311), `@@ -295,7 +364,7 @@` (1344).\nLatches three per-call invariants — `_ds4_cdna_version()` (1266-1270), `_ds4_n_cu()`\n(1273-1277), `_ds4_backend()` (1280-1284) — plus a **single dict comprehension read of\nall seven `DS4_MOE_*` env vars at import** (patch:1287-1288):\n\n```python\n_DS4_MOE = {k: os.environ.get(\"DS4_MOE_\" + k)\n            for k in (\"BM\", \"BN\", \"NW\", \"NS\", \"BK\", \"KEEP_MFMA\", \"WPE\")}\n```\nRationale quoted at patch:1249-1256: `make_opt_flags` runs \"~92x per decode step\" and\n\"The seven `DS4_MOE_*` lookups go through `os._Environ.get` -> `Mapping.get` ->\n`decodevalue`, ~644 times per step.\" [S]\n\nThe gfx1151 tile override is at patch:1315-1340, gated `if not is_cdna4 and\n_ds4_cdna_version() == -1` (1316) then `if block_m < 128` (1321) → forces\n`block_m=16; block_n=64; num_warps=4; num_stages=3` (1322), with the comment\n\"16x64 beats stock 32x256 by 1.2-2.1x across m=6..2048 on gfx1151 (WMMA 16x16 + small\nLDS)\" (1318-1319). [S/CL — the perf figure is CL]\n\n**(c) `opt_flags_amd.py` — NEW, `SITE/vllm/third_party/triton_kernels/matmul_ogs_details/opt_flags_details/opt_flags_amd.py`, 57 lines** [M]\nNot in the patch (whole file new). Mirrors the same latching locally:\n`_ds4_cdna_version()` at :17-21, `_ds4_n_cu()` at :24-28, used at :36, :47, :55.\nIts header comment states it is \"kept local rather than imported from there, which\nwould be circular\" (:12). Note `compute_block_nk` at :31 hard-forces `block_k = 128`\nat :55-56 — this is the value `DS4_MOE_BK` overrides from `opt_flags.py:1335-1336`. [S]\n\n**Lift verdict:** `_routing_compute.py` is a standalone 13-line hunk with **no code\ndependency** on the latching set. The latching set is a *performance* adjacency, not a\ncorrectness one. Lift the routing hunk alone if you only need top-10 routing to compile.\n[S — derived from reading all four hunks]\n\n---\n\n## 2. The two ADAPT files\n\n### 2.1 `SITE/ds4_topk.py` — 457 lines [M] (MANIFEST \"new (457)\" ✅ matches)\n\nFull path: `/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_topk.py`\n\n**Public interface** (all [S]):\n\n| Symbol | Line | Signature |\n|---|---|---|\n| `select_topk` | :441-457 | `(logits, topk_tokens, row_starts=None, row_ends=None, out=None) -> Tensor` — **the entry point**, docstring at :448 says \"Entry point used by `rocm_aiter_mla_sparse`. Honours `DS4_TOPK=0`.\" |\n| `topk_indices_ascending` | :280-354 | `(logits, topk_tokens, row_starts=None, row_ends=None, out=None) -> Tensor` — the Triton path |\n| `topk_indices_ascending_reference` | :367-402 | pure-torch definitional reference, tests only (\"slow\", :359) |\n| `topk_indices_torch_fallback` | :408-438 | \"The current production two-sort path, verbatim, for A/B and fallback\" (:413) |\n| `_topk_rows_kernel` | :111-268 | `@triton.jit`, one workgroup per row |\n| `_okey` / `_okey_torch` | :65-83 / :360-364 | order-preserving fp32→int32 key |\n\n**What it replaces in vLLM.** Module docstring :3-11: replaces *both*\n`_topk_indices_torch` (full stable descending sort) **and** `_canonicalize_topk_indices_`\n(second sort) in `vllm/v1/attention/ops/rocm_aiter_mla_sparse.py`. [S]\n\n**Wiring — not a monkeypatch.** It is a plain import behind an `lru_cache`d resolver\ninserted by the patch into `rocm_aiter_mla_sparse.py`:\n\n```python\n# patch:783-795\n+@functools.lru_cache\n+def _sparse_topk_impl():\n+    \"\"\"The gfx1151 deterministic top-k kernel, or None if it will not build.\"\"\"\n+    if os.environ.get(\"DS4_TOPK\") == \"0\":\n+        return None\n+    try:\n+        import ds4_topk\n+\n+        return ds4_topk.select_topk\n+    except Exception as exc:  # pragma: no cover - deployment guard\n+        print(f\"[ds4_topk] unavailable, using the torch two-sort path: {exc}\",\n+              flush=True)\n+        return None\n```\nConsumer wrapper `_sparse_topk(...)` at patch:798. [S]\nNote the **double kill-switch**: `DS4_TOPK == \"0\"` is checked both at patch:786 and\nindependently at `ds4_topk.py:40`. [S]\n\n**gfx1151-specific bits** [S]:\n- `_TILE = 2048`, `_NUM_WARPS = 8` (:54-55) with the wave-size reasoning at :51-53:\n  \"2048 fp32 = 8 KiB per iteration; with `num_warps=8` (**512 lanes at wave64**) that\n  is 4 elements/lane, which holds the `tl.cumsum` in the emit pass to 11 shuffle steps.\"\n  → **wave64 is an AMD/RDNA assumption baked into the tile size.**\n- `_HIST_MODE` / `DS4_TOPK_HIST` (:49, :43-48): `\"hist\"` = 8-bit digits/256 bins via\n  `tl.histogram`; `\"sum\"` = 4-bit/16 bins via masked `tl.sum`, existing because\n  \"`tl.histogram`'s lowering is the only part of this kernel whose **ROCm-backend\n  support** is not obvious from the Python source\" (:45-46).\n- `_PAD_TILE = 1024  # >= any topk we serve (512)` (:56) — hard-codes the DS4 top-512.\n\n**JIT-stall discipline (critical to replicate).** :27-30: \"no shape-dependent compile\nkey. Every size is a runtime argument marked `do_not_specialize`, so at most two kernel\nvariants are ever built (prefill with row bounds, decode without) and no decode step can\ntrigger a JIT stall.\" Enforced at :103-110:\n`do_not_specialize=[\"width\", \"topk\", \"logit_stride_row\", \"out_stride_row\"]`. [S]\n\n**Determinism contract** :13-24 and :235-243: no float accumulation, no atomics; output\nslot is an exact integer prefix count, \"a bijection onto `[0, n_sel)` that no scheduling\nchoice can perturb\". [S]\n\n### 2.2 `SITE/ds4_tl_indexer.py` — 594 lines [M] (⚠ MANIFEST:38 says \"new (476)\" — **STALE by 118 lines**)\n\nFull path: `/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_tl_indexer.py`\n\n**Public interface** (all [S]):\n\n| Symbol | Line | Role |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fp8_mqa_logits_tl` | :314 | `(q, kv, weights, cu_seqlen_ks, cu_seqlen_ke)` — **prefill** indexer entry |\n| `fp8_paged_mqa_logits_tl` | :486 | `(q, kv_cache, weights, context_lens, block_tables, max_model_len)` — **decode** indexer entry |\n| `cached_bf16_weight` | :343 | `(weight, weight_scale, block_size, m)` — the hook (§2.3) |\n| `w8a8_block_bf16_direct` | :370 | `(x, weight, weight_scale, block_size, m)` — `DS4_W8A8_BF16_DIRECT` path |\n| `w8a8_block_fp8_bf16` | :390 | `(qx, weight, x_scale, weight_scale, block_size, output_dtype)` — `DS4_W8A8_BF16` path |\n| `_idx_qat` | :49 | hadamard128 + fp4 QAT round-trip |\n| `_build` / `_kernel` | :177 / :232 | prefill TileLang kernel + cache |\n| `_build_decode` / `_decode_kernel` | :259 / :292 | decode TileLang kernel + cache |\n| `_maybe_profile` / `_maybe_expert_union` | :95 / :84 | instrument activation hooks |\n\n**What it replaces in vLLM.** Docstring :2-4: \"Drop-in replacements for\n`fp8_mqa_logits_torch` / `fp8_paged_mqa_logits_torch` (next_n==1), running the O(M*N)\ncompute on a bf16 WMMA TileLang kernel instead of a Python loop. Validated: prefill rel\n~1.6e-3, decode rel ~1e-7 vs the torch fallbacks.\" [S; the validation figures are CL]\n\n**Wiring — plain import, two env-gated early-returns in the patch** [S]:\n- decode: patch:717-722, `DS4_TL_DECODE` **default \"1\"** →\n  `return _tl.fp8_paged_mqa_logits_tl(...)`\n- prefill: patch:730-733, `DS4_TL_PREFILL` **default \"1\"** →\n  `return _tl.fp8_mqa_logits_tl(...)`\n- w8a8 GEMM: patch:1541-1543, `_DS4_W8A8_BF16` → `_tl.w8a8_block_fp8_bf16(...)`\n- w8a8 direct: patch:1496-1513, `_DS4_W8A8_BF16_DIRECT` → `_tl.w8a8_block_bf16_direct(...)`\n\nNote the patch **overrides `apply_weights`** on `TritonFp8BlockScaledMMKernel`\n(patch:1471-1532) — that is the one place this behaves like a subclass override rather\nthan a plain call, and it falls through with `return super().apply_weights(...)` at\npatch:1532. [S]\n\n**gfx1151-specific bits** [S]:\n- `_build(...)`: `block_Q = 1  # gfx1151: block_Q=1 + threads=256 validated correct at\n  H=64,D=128` (:179).\n- `_fit_config(block_Q, heads, D, budget=56*1024)` (:221): *\"Pick (block_N, num_stages)\n  so Q+K shared buffers fit **gfx1151's 64KB LDS**\"* (:222). Ladder `ns in (2,1)` ×\n  `bn in (128,64,32,16)` (:225-228), fallback `(16, 1)` (:229).\n- Decode constants `_DEC_BLOCK_N = 64`, `_DEC_THREADS = 256` (:255-256) with a\n  **correctness** warning at :251-254: *\"threads MUST be 256 here: at 128 threads\n  (2 warps) the block_N x heads(64) score tile is only partially computed -> WRONG\n  logits (verified: threads=128 gave max_abs_err ~3e2 vs 0.0 at 256; the sweep that\n  favored 128 measured only speed). block_N>=256 overflows the 64KB LDS.\"*\n- Bucketing to avoid hipcc recompiles: `_KV_BUCKET = 512` (:67, rationale :63-66) and\n  `_PREFILL_KV_BUCKET = 8192` (:312, rationale :305-311: *\"a ~2s hipcc recompile per\n  chunk with the GPU idle\"*).\n- `rocm_unquantized_gemm_impl` selected over `F.linear` for the wvSplitK skinny GEMM\n  (:407-412), with the profile note *\"Profiled 2026-07-12: aten::mm via Cijk_*MT16x16\n  = ~22% of decode GPU time\"* (:410) [CL].\n\n### 2.3 `cached_bf16_weight` hook — RE-PINNED\n\nRecord cited `:343-350`. **Re-pin: `ds4_tl_indexer.py:343-367`.**\n- `def cached_bf16_weight(weight, weight_scale, block_size, m):` — **:343** ✅ (record exact)\n- docstring — **:344-351** (record said 350; the docstring closes on **351**)\n- body — :352-367\n[M — `grep -n \"cached_bf16_weight\"` → 343, 383, 395]\n\n**Skip-during-cold-cache logic, quoted (:344-357):**\n\n```python\n    \"\"\"The bf16 dequantised copy of a block-scaled fp8 weight, or None.\n\n    None means \"do not take the bf16 path\". That happens when the cache is cold\n    and M is large: the startup memory-profiling forward runs at large M with an\n    empty cache, and building the copy there inflates the measured footprint and\n    shrinks the KV cache allocation. Decode (M <= 32) populates the cache;\n    prefill reuses entries that already exist unless DS4_W8A8_BF16_PREFILL=0.\n    \"\"\"\n    key = weight.data_ptr()\n    wb = _BF16_WCACHE.get(key)\n    if wb is not None:\n        return wb if (m <= 32 or _BF16_PREFILL) else None\n    if m > 32:\n        return None\n```\n[S]\n\n**Decision table** (derived from :352-357):\n\n| cache state | `m <= 32` (decode) | `m > 32` (prefill/profiling) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **warm** (hit) | return `wb` | return `wb` if `_BF16_PREFILL` else `None` |\n| **cold** (miss) | build + cache + return | **return `None`** ← the skip |\n\nSupporting state:\n- `_BF16_WCACHE = {}` at :339, keyed on `weight.data_ptr()` (:352) — *storage pointer*,\n  not module identity.\n- `_BF16_PREFILL = os.environ.get(\"DS4_W8A8_BF16_PREFILL\", \"1\") != \"0\"` at :342,\n  comment :340-341.\n- The `M <= 32` threshold appears **twice as a bare literal 32** (:355, :356) — no named\n  constant. A Qwen fork with different decode batch geometry must change both. [S]\n- Both callers honour `None`: `w8a8_block_bf16_direct` :384-385 returns `None` (caller\n  falls back), `w8a8_block_fp8_bf16` :396-399 falls back to `w8a8_triton_block_scaled_mm`.\n- The `M > 32` guard's purpose is restated independently in the patch at\n  patch:1493-1495: *\"Returns None (-> stock path) when the bf16 weight is not cached and\n  M is large, which is what keeps the startup memory-profiling forward on the fp8 path\n  and the KV cache allocation unchanged.\"* [S]\n\n### 2.4 hadamard128 / fp4_act_quant warning comments — TWO locations\n\n**Location A — `ds4_tl_indexer.py:9-21`** (the `DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL` header block) [S]:\n\n```python\n# --- DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL=1: reproduce the official DeepSeek-V4 indexer QAT graph ---\n# The official inference graph (HF snapshot inference/model.py Indexer.forward and\n# Compressor.forward with rotate=True) applies, to BOTH indexer Q rows and indexer\n# compressor K rows, after RoPE:\n#     x -> hadamard128(x) / sqrt(128) -> fp4_act_quant(x, block=32, inplace)   (QAT sim)\n# before the relu(q.k)*w scoring. ds4.c implements the same (dsv4_indexer_qat_*),\n# and its comment warns the top-k selection \"is not the model's graph\" without it.\n# vLLM's FP8 indexer path skips both steps. ...\n```\nThe literal warning phrase — *its comment warns the top-k selection \"is not the model's\ngraph\" without it* — is at **:15**. `fp4_act_quant` is named at **:13** and again at\n**:51**. The equivalence argument (power-of-two fp8 storage scale ⇒ score-time rotation\nis equivalent to pre-quant) is at :16-20. [S]\n\n**Location B — `ds4_tl_indexer.py:320-323`** (inside `fp8_mqa_logits_tl`) [S]:\n\n```python\n    # NOTE: the indexer QAT rotation (Hadamard-128) is applied PRE-fp8-quant in\n    # the fused q/compressor-K kernels (gated by DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL), not here — a\n    # score-time rotation is a no-op for the dot product (H is orthonormal). See\n    # ds4-vllm-indexer-qat-missing memory.\n```\n⚠ This **contradicts** Location A's :16-20 claim that applying it \"HERE, to the\ndequantized-unscaled rows at score time, is exactly equivalent\". Location B says it is\napplied in the fused kernels instead. Location B is the later/operative statement (the\nfunction body). Two more copies of the flag live in the patch at **patch:306** and\n**patch:532** (`_DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL = __import__(\"os\").environ.get(\"DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL\",\"0\") == \"1\"`),\ntargeting `fused_compress_quant_cache.py` and `fused_indexer_q.py` — consistent with\nLocation B. Debug prints at patch:361 and patch:626 (`[DS4_QAT] indexer-K/Q APPLY_QAT=…`). [S]\n\nImplementation: `_hadamard128_matrix` :27-36 (7× `torch.kron` of the 2×2 base, scaled\n`128**-0.5`), `_fp4_consts` :39-46 (levels `[0,.5,1,1.5,2,3,4,6]`, mids for\n`bucketize`), `_idx_qat` :49-61 (`amax` over `[-1,4,32]` blocks, `s = exp2(ceil(log2(amax/6)))`,\nclamp ±6, bucketize, rescale, → bf16). [S]\n\n---\n\n## 3. The three VENDOR instruments\n\nAll three are venv-top-level modules under `SITE/`, i.e. importable as bare names inside\nthe container. None uses an import hook or `sitecustomize`; all are lazily imported from\na call site. [S]\n\n### 3.1 `SITE/ds4_synctrace.py` — 93 lines [M] (MANIFEST \"new (93)\" ✅)\n\n**Activation: NO env var of its own.** Driven from\n`ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile` and therefore shares the `DS4_PROFILE` window.\nDocstring :22-23: *\"Driven from `ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile` so it shares the\nDS4_PROFILE window (no new env var, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\"* [S]\n\nCall chain [S]:\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:97` — `if os.environ.get(\"DS4_PROFILE\") != \"1\": return`\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:100` — `if _PCALLS == _PSTART` (default 60, :74)\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:104-105` — `import ds4_synctrace; ds4_synctrace.reset(); ds4_synctrace.install()`\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:119` — `elif _PCALLS == _PSTOP` (default 160, :75)\n- `ds4_tl_indexer.py:152-155` — `report(_steps)` then `uninstall()`;\n  `_steps = max((_PSTOP - _PSTART) / 21.0, 1e-9)   # 21 indexer calls/step` (:153)\n\n**Interface** [S]: `install()` :54 · `uninstall()` :66 · `reset()` :77 ·\n`report(steps=1.0) -> str` :81 (top-30 by frequency, :90).\n\n**Mechanism.** Monkeypatches `torch.Tensor` methods in place (`setattr(torch.Tensor,\nname, wrapper)` at :51; originals saved in `_orig` :50 and restored at :70).\nTargets, :35: `(\"item\", \"tolist\", \"cpu\", \"numpy\", \"nonzero\", \"__float__\", \"__int__\")`.\nEach wrapper records one `sys._getframe(1)` keyed\n`f\"{filename-after-site-packages}:{lineno} {co_name}() [{method}]\"` (:43-45). [S]\n\n**Stated limitation (:18-20)** — replicate this caveat verbatim: *\"boolean-mask indexing\n(`x[mask]`) reaches nonzero() inside C++ `at::index`, not through the python method, so\nit is NOT counted here.\"* [S]\n\nDesign justification :8-16: `with_stack=True` captures \"~3,200 ops per step, which pegged\nthe worker at 94% CPU\"; this is \"~25 events per step\". [CL]\n\n### 3.2 `SITE/ds4_expert_union.py` — 128 lines [M] (MANIFEST \"new (128)\" ✅)\n\n**Activation: `DS4_EXPERT_UNION=1`, plus a lazy install from the decode path.** [S]\n\nEnv surface, self-documented at :24-30 and implemented :38-41:\n\n| Var | Line | Default | Effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `DS4_EXPERT_UNION` | :38 | unset ⇒ **off** | `== \"1\"` enables |\n| `DS4_EU_START` | :39 | `200` | calls to skip (warmup + prefill) |\n| `DS4_EU_CALLS` | :40 | `2000` | window size in MoE calls (~46/decode step) |\n| `DS4_EU_OUT` | :41 | `~/vllm-prof` | output dir |\n\nTwo-stage gate — the module-level `_ENABLED` (:38, :99) **and** the caller's own check at\n`ds4_tl_indexer.py:86` (`if _EU_TRIED or os.environ.get(\"DS4_EXPERT_UNION\") != \"1\": return`).\nInstall is deliberately lazy; `ds4_tl_indexer.py:80-82` explains: *\"wrapping the fused_moe\nexperts module at ds4_tl_indexer import time would be circular, and by the first paged\ndecode the MoE layers are long since built.\"* [S]\n\n**Interface** [S]: `install()` :96 (idempotent, :99) · `_record(topk_ids,\nnum_local_experts)` :49 · `_flush()` :76. `atexit.register(_flush)` at :123.\n\n**What it monkeypatches** [S]: `vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts.\ngpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data` — rebound at :119\n(`m.make_routing_data = wrapped`), original stashed on `wrapped._ds4_orig` :118.\nWrapper signature :111: `(topk_ids, topk_weights, num_local_experts, *a, **kw)`.\n\n**Why this choke point** (:10-14): *\"It is NOT reachable through vLLM's own\n`--enable-return-routed-experts`: that capturer hangs off `BaseRouter.route()`, which\nthis model never calls (routing happens inside the triton_kernels path).\"* [S]\n\n**No-sync discipline** (:50, :66-73): device-only accumulation into a preallocated\n`[_CALLS, 3] int32` buffer (:64); slot 0 absorbs the `-1` padding *\"so no boolean mask\n(and therefore no size-dependent sync) is needed\"* (:66-67). Single `.cpu()` at\n`_flush` :83. Output TSV `expert_union_<pid>.tsv`, header\n`# n_rows\\tn_distinct\\tn_local_experts` (:85-90). [S]\n\nEvery failure path swallows the exception (:92, :105, :114-115) — *\"a probe must never\ntake the engine down\"* (:92). [S]\n\n### 3.3 `SITE/ds4_offload_batch.py` — 154 lines [M] (⚠ MANIFEST:78 says \"new (102)\" — **STALE by 52 lines**)\n\n**Activation: no env gate on the module — it is imported unconditionally by the patched\nconnector and configured by two env vars.** [S]\n\nImport site, `vllm/distributed/kv_transfer/kv_connector/v1/offloading/scheduler.py`\nvia patch:1934-1940:\n```python\n+        try:\n+            from ds4_offload_batch import (\n+                resolve_promote_block_budget,\n+                resolve_store_batch_tokens,\n+            )\n+        except ImportError:\n+            logger.warning(\n+                \"ds4_offload_batch not importable; store batches stay unbounded \"\n```\nCalled at patch:1948-1952. Comment at patch:1930-1932: *\"Imported inside the function,\nlike every other ds4_* helper: a missing module then degrades this one behaviour to stock\ninstead of breaking the import of the whole offloading connector.\"* [S]\n\n**Interface** [S] (`__all__` at :37-44):\n\n| Symbol | Line | Signature / value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `resolve_store_batch_tokens` | :82 | `(num_blocks, offloaded_block_sizes, frac=None) -> int \\| None` |\n| `resolve_promote_block_budget` | :114 | `(num_blocks, frac=None) -> int \\| None` |\n| `FRAC_ENV` | :46 | `\"DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\"` |\n| `PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV` | :47 | `\"DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\"` |\n| `DEFAULT_FRAC` | :52 | `0.25` |\n| `DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC` | :67 | `0.5` |\n| `_read_frac` / `_budget` | :70 / :139 | internal |\n\nBoth env reads go through `os.getenv(env)` at :73; `frac <= 0` ⇒ `None` ⇒ unbounded ⇒\n**stock vLLM** (:78-79 doc, :147-148 and :134-135 code). [S]\n\n**Torch-free by design** (:31-32): *\"This lives outside `vllm` so the budget arithmetic\nis unit-testable without importing torch or the connector's dependency graph.\"* Confirmed\n— the only import is `os` (:35). [M — `grep \"^import\"` → `import os` only]\n\nTwo non-obvious invariants worth lifting verbatim [S]:\n- **Store floor** (:100-109): the returned budget is `max(budget_tokens, max(sizes))`\n  (:154) and that floor \"is load-bearing, not a rounding nicety\" — below it a group's\n  target lands under its own cursor and `_build_store_jobs` assigns\n  `next_stored_block_idx = num_blocks` outright (\"it never takes a max\"), rewinding the\n  cursor and skipping blocks \"for good\".\n- **Promote counted in blocks, not tokens** (:119-127): a sliding-window group's tiny\n  numerous blocks \"dominate the rate and collapse the budget to a few hundred tokens --\n  about 6% of the prompt\".\n\n---\n\n## 4. Container discipline\n\n### 4.1 `container/Dockerfile` — 122 lines [M]\n\n**Base image pin — `container/Dockerfile:21`** [S]:\n```dockerfile\nARG DS4_BASE=\"docker.io/kyuz0/vllm-therock-gfx1151@sha256:25fd294fde9f729d1e75f109022ab4496c78190c0a6dc0142440529f7af20e4d\"\n```\n- Digest-pinned (not a tag). Drift guidance at :17-19.\n- Base ships vLLM commit `470229c` (:6, and label `ds4.vllm_commit=\"470229c\"` at :121).\n- Restated at `MANIFEST.md:3-4`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md:14`, `AGENTS.md:161`. [S]\n\n**Three build stages, all `FROM ${DS4_BASE}`** [S]:\n\n| Stage | Line | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `rocr-idle-fix` | :26 | rebuild ROCr from `rocm-systems` @ `d34cbb64…` (:35) + cherry-picks `c06ea68a…`, `933596e9…`, `78b874d4…` (:37-39) + `rocr-force-block-indefinite-active-wait.patch` (:46-47) |\n| `provider-build` | :58 | rdma-core `-b v57.0` (:61) + thunderbolt-ibverbs @ `76ba39b6…` (:63); applies `packaging/rdma-core-patches/0*.patch` with `git apply -C1` (:65); asserts `libusb4_rdma-rdmav57.so` exists (:68) |\n| final | :70 | patch + overlay + copies |\n\nCherry-picks are made **reproducible** by pinning the committer date (:40-44):\n`GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=\"$(git show -s --format=%cI \"$commit\")\"` plus fixed\n`user.name`/`user.email`. Worth replicating. [S]\n\n### 4.2 How patches are applied at build — the two mechanisms\n\n```dockerfile\n# Dockerfile:75-77\nCOPY container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch /tmp/\nRUN cd / && git apply -p1 --whitespace=nowarn /tmp/vllm-upstream.patch && rm /tmp/vllm-upstream.patch\nCOPY --chown=root:root container/rootfs/ /\n```\n[S]\n\n1. **Modified files (31):** `git apply -p1` with CWD `/`. The patch paths are\n   container-absolute (`a/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/…`), so `-p1` strips\n   `a/` and resolves against `/`. Enforced by\n   `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py::test_patches_use_container_absolute_paths` (:185-194). [S]\n2. **New files (12):** `COPY container/rootfs/ /` — rootfs mirrors `/`. [S]\n\nOrdering matters and is invariant-checked: `test_modified_files_are_not_also_in_rootfs`\n(:99-103) — *\"A modified file present in rootfs would COPY over the patched one and\nsilently pin an older content.\"* [S]\n\nPost-steps: ROCr DSO overwrite (:81-83), usb4_rdma provider `.so` + `.driver` file\n(:89-91, rationale :85-88 — \"libibverbs matches a provider to a device BY NAME\"),\nhipcc/gcc build of `libtbv_ar2.so`/`libtbv_ar.so` (:99-106), stale-`__pycache__` purge\n(:111-113), OCI labels incl. `com.github.containers.toolbox=\"true\"` (:117). [S]\n\n⚠ **`MANIFEST.md:8` is stale and contradicts `Dockerfile:76`.** Do not lift the MANIFEST\nsentence \"The Dockerfile does not apply these; it COPYs the final files from ../rootfs.\"\nThe Dockerfile's own comment at :72-74 is correct. [S]\n\n### 4.3 `container/patches/MANIFEST.md` — 100 lines [M], structure to replicate\n\n- **:1-18 header.** Base digest + vLLM commit (:3-4); the three-way count claim\n  (:6 \"31 modified\", :10 \"12 new\", :12-14 one deliberately excluded byte-identical file\n  `aiter_meta/csrc/cpp_itfs/utils.py`); path convention note (:16-18).\n- **:20-99 eight themed tables**, each `| file | Δ | purpose |`:\n\n| § | Line | Theme | Rows |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| DeepSeek-V4 model (AMD/gfx1151) | :20 | model path | 8 |\n| Sparse indexer / mid-context retrieval | :32 | **contains `_routing`'s siblings + ds4_topk/tl_indexer/synctrace/expert_union** | 6 |\n| MoE / GEMM kernel tuning | :42 | **contains `_routing_compute.py` @ :47** | 6 |\n| Distributed all-reduce over TB4 RDMA | :52 | tbv | 3 |\n| Scheduler / KV / cudagraph / MTP | :59 | | 5 |\n| Disk KV cache (`fs_lru`, distributed) | :68 | | 10 |\n| OpenAI API: reasoning + tools | :82 | | 4 |\n| Kernel config lookup | :90 | | 1 |\n| ROCr / HIP idle CPU fixes | :96 | build-stage replacement | 1 |\n\n- **Δ column grammar:** `+N` when no deletions, `+N/-M` otherwise, or `**new (LINES)**`.\n  Machine-checked for modified rows (§4.5); **not** checked for new rows (§4.4).\n- Purpose cells carry the *engineering rationale in prose* — e.g. :71 records the\n  measured failure the `fs_lru` tier fixes (\"0/8 needle recall vs 8/8 fresh at 100%\n  reported hits\"). This is the density the campaign should replicate. [S]\n\n### 4.4 ⚠ Three \"new (N)\" counts are wrong — MEASURED\n\n`wc -l` on every rootfs file vs the MANIFEST cell:\n\n| File | MANIFEST says | `wc -l` says | |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ds4_tl_indexer.py` (:38) | `new (476)` | **594** | ✗ off by 118 |\n| `ds4_offload_batch.py` (:78) | `new (102)` | **154** | ✗ off by 52 |\n| `vllm/models/deepseek_v4/amd/dspark_mtp.py` (:26) | `new (885)` | **932** | ✗ off by 47 |\n| `ds4_topk.py` (:37) | `new (457)` | 457 | ✓ |\n| `ds4_synctrace.py` (:39) | `new (93)` | 93 | ✓ |\n| `ds4_expert_union.py` (:40) | `new (128)` | 128 | ✓ |\n| `lru_manager.py` (:71) | `new (485)` | 485 | ✓ |\n| `distributed.py` (:72) | `new (345)` | 345 | ✓ |\n| `opt_flags_amd.py` (:46) | `new (57)` | 57 | ✓ |\n| `gfx1151-GEMM-A8W8_BLOCKSCALE.json` (:50) | `new (15)` | 15 | ✓ |\n| `tbv_ar.py` (:56) | `new (255)` | 255 | ✓ |\n| `tbv_ar2.py` (:57) | `new (69)` | 69 | ✓ |\n[M — literal `wc -l` output]\n\n**Root cause, pinned:** `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py:166-183`\n(`test_manifest_deltas_match_their_patches`) short-circuits on `if \"new\" in delta:\ncontinue` (:173). The Δ audit covers modified rows only. **A Qwen fork replicating this\ndiscipline should extend the test to assert new-row line counts against `wc -l`** — it is\na ~4-line addition and closes a live drift. [S]\n\n### 4.5 `container/verify-patches.sh` — 95 lines [M]: how it proves base → rootfs\n\n**It proves base → *patched*, not base → rootfs.** The two halves are separate. [S]\n\nMechanism, in order:\n1. :29 — reads the base digest **out of the Dockerfile** with\n   `sed -n 's/^ARG DS4_BASE=\"\\(.*\\)\"$/\\1/p' container/Dockerfile`, \"so the two cannot\n   diverge\" (:14). Single source of truth.\n2. :33-37 — `podman image exists \"$BASE\"` or bail (exit 2) with the pull hint (~35 GB).\n3. :55 — file list derived **from the patch itself**:\n   `sed -n \"s|^--- a/$SITE/||p\" \"$COMBINED\" | sort -u`.\n4. :65-67 — **one** container invocation extracts all base originals:\n   `podman run --rm --entrypoint sh \"$BASE\" -c \"cd /$SITE && tar cf - <paths>\" | tar xf - -C \"$WORK/$SITE\"`.\n   Comment :64: \"per-file `podman run` is ~1s each\".\n5. :90-93 — the proof:\n   `git -C \"$WORK\" apply -p1 \"$COMBINED\"` — *\"exactly as the Dockerfile will\"* (:88).\n   `-C \"$WORK\"` is required \"so the stripped paths resolve inside the work tree rather\n   than this repo (itself a git checkout)\" (:88-89).\n6. :95 — success line: `vllm-upstream.patch applies cleanly to the base (N files)`.\n\n**Regeneration mode `--write`** (:43-52, :70-85): file list comes from MANIFEST instead\n(regex `\\| \\`([^`]+)\\` \\| (?!\\*\\*new)` at :48), diffs `$WORK` (base) against\n`$DS4_PATCH_SRC` (desired final files) with explicit `--label a/… --label b/…` (:77) so\nthe emitted paths stay container-absolute. Prints a reminder to update the Δ column\n(:82-83). [S]\n\n**Division of labour, stated at :15-16:** *\"The offline half of these checks -- manifest\nvs overlay vs Dockerfile counts -- lives in tests/test_patchset_packaging.py and needs no\nimage.\"* [S]\n\n### 4.6 `tests/test_patchset_packaging.py` — 233 lines, 12 tests, all passing [M]\n\n```\n$ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_patchset_packaging.py' -v\n… Ran 12 tests in 0.030s\nOK\n```\n[M — literal output]\n\nThe 12 invariants (the reusable discipline) [S]:\n\n| Test | Line | Invariant |\n|---|---|---|\n| `test_overlay_is_not_empty` | :63 | guards vacuous passes (`>5` overlay, `>20` rows) |\n| `test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay` | :69 | no `.pyc` / `__pycache__` — COPY would bake stale bytecode |\n| `test_every_overlay_file_is_documented` | :79 | overlay ⊆ manifest |\n| `test_every_documented_file_ships` | :88 | manifest ⊆ (overlay ∪ patch sections ∪ `NOT_IN_OVERLAY`) |\n| `test_modified_files_are_not_also_in_rootfs` | :99 | patch ∩ overlay = ∅ |\n| `test_manifest_header_counts_match_the_tables` | :105 | \"31 modified\"/\"12 new\" headers vs row counts |\n| `test_dockerfile_file_count_matches_the_overlay` | :126 | Dockerfile's *prose* counts (`overlays the (\\d+) new files`, `vllm-upstream\\.patch, (\\d+) files`) vs reality |\n| `test_every_modified_file_has_a_reviewable_diff` | :153 | every modified row has a patch section |\n| `test_manifest_deltas_match_their_patches` | :166 | **Δ cells recomputed from the diff** (:178-180) — comment :169 notes \"how 11 of these came to disagree at once\" |\n| `test_patches_use_container_absolute_paths` | :185 | all `--- ` lines start `--- a/opt/venv/…` |\n| `test_every_patch_file_names_a_shipped_file` | :196 | no orphan `vllm__*.patch`; \"Map forwards, never backwards\" (:197-199) |\n| `test_overlay_python_compiles` | :214 | `py_compile` every overlay `.py`, **cfile into a tempdir** (:218-219) so it does not break the bytecode test |\n\n`NOT_IN_OVERLAY = {\"_rocm_sdk_core/lib/libhsa-runtime64.so.1\"}` (:31-34) — the one\nmanifest row built by a Dockerfile stage. [S]\n\n`container/build.sh:13-17` runs this suite **before** `podman build` and aborts on\nfailure. [S]\n\n**Measured counts** [M]:\n- `grep -c \"^--- a/\" container/patches/vllm-upstream.patch` → **31** (unique: 31)\n- `find container/rootfs -type f | wc -l` → **12**\n- `grep -c '\\*\\*new' container/patches/MANIFEST.md` → **12**\n\n---\n\n## 5. `host/` — every file, one line each, plus the env/perf inventory\n\n### 5.1 File inventory\n\n| Path | Lines | Purpose (pinned) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `host/ds4-config.yaml` | 18 | Site config; flat `key: value` only, \"parsed by ds4-config with the Python stdlib, no pyyaml\" (:3-4) |\n| `host/ds4-config` | 27 | `#!/usr/bin/python3`; each `key: value` → `export DS4_<KEY>=<shlex.quote(value)>` (:23-27). Used as `eval \"$(\"$HOME/ds4-config\")\"` (:4) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh` | 148 | **Canonical env**, sourced by ray head, box2 ray worker, and `vllm serve` (:2-3) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-env.rdma.sh` | 25 | `source`s base then pins one unambiguous `NCCL_IB_HCA` (:8-9) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-env.tcp.sh` | 13 | `source`s base, disables IB + both tbv all-reduces (:7-13) — correctness/fallback profile |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-restart.sh` | 145 | Full bringup: teardown → containers → ray → serve → verify (:2) |\n| `host/ds4-cluster-down.sh` | 35 | The stop half, idempotent (:2-5) |\n| `host/container-heal.sh` | 29 | Reconciles \"podman says Up but crun is dead (conmon SIGKILLed)\" (:3-4); always exits 0 (:7) |\n| `host/ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh` | 130 | The `vllm serve` launcher; runs **inside** the container (:2). \"THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH\" (:6) |\n| `host/ds4-vllm-warmup.py` | 77 | 2-phase post-start warmup (tiny request, then one `DS4_WARMUP_CTX` prefill) |\n| `host/systemd/ds4-vllm.service` | 23 | `Type=oneshot`, `RemainAfterExit=yes`, ExecStart/Stop/StopPost |\n\n### 5.2 `ds4-config.yaml` keys — all 14 (`:5-18`) [S]\n\n| Key | Line | Value | Note |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `model` | :5 | `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731` | \"weights needed on BOTH boxes\" |\n| `transport` | :6 | `rdma` | `rdma \\| tcp` — selects `ds4-cluster-env.<transport>.sh` |\n| `head_ip` | :7 | `192.168.100.1` | |\n| `worker_ip` | :8 | `192.168.100.2` | |\n| `container` | :9 | `vllm` | podman container name, same both boxes |\n| `rdma_hca` | :10 | `usb4_rdma0` | `NCCL_IB_HCA` pin, rdma only |\n| `api_port` | :11 | `1234` | |\n| `disk_kv` | :12 | `true` | fs_lru NVMe prefix-KV tier |\n| `disk_kv_gib` | :13 | `30` | **per-NODE** disk cap |\n| `max_ctx` | :14 | `524288` | `--max-model-len`, \"the validated profile\" |\n| `kv_pin_gib` | :15 | `6` | pinned GPU KV pool |\n| `gpu_mem_util` | :16 | `0.83` | **\"IGNORED while the KV pin above is set\"** |\n| `warmup_ctx` | :17 | `2048` | 0 disables |\n| `cables` | :18 | `1` | TB cables; 2 dedicates second NHI to RX zero-copy rail |\n\n### 5.3 The env/perf settings inventory the campaign asked for — each pinned\n\n| Setting | Pin | Value | Why (quoted/paraphrased from the file) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **`PYTHONHASHSEED`** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:13` | `0` | :9-12 — \"vLLM derives NONE_HASH (the prefix-cache chain seed) from it, so without a fixed value identical token content produces different block filenames every run and the disk cache can never hit across a restart\" |\n| **`PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF` expandable_segments** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:27` | `expandable_segments:True,garbage_collection_threshold:0.85` | :14-26 — GC off by default on a UMA box; 0.85 of ~124 GiB ≈ reclaim at ~105 GiB; expandable_segments is \"the fragmentation half\"; \"Safe with `--enforce-eager` (no graph capture)\" |\n| **`HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT`** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:83` | `${DS4_HSA_INTERRUPT:-1}` | :79-82 — \"TheRock ROCm busy-polls (rocr InterruptSignal::WaitRelaxed) -> ~2-3 cores spinning during inference -> CPU thermal throttle. Set 0 to revert to spin\" |\n| **Cache dirs off tmpfs (Triton/Inductor)** | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:49-50` | `TORCHINDUCTOR_CACHE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/torchinductor`, `TRITON_CACHE_DIR=$HOME/.triton/cache` | :45-48 — \"the defaults land under /tmp (tmpfs), and the first bringup after a boot then recompiles every kernel -- ~25 min CPU-bound in LLVM before the API can answer\" |\n| **Cache dir off tmpfs (KV staging)** | `host/ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh:104` | `DS4_OFFLOAD_MMAP_DIR=${KVDIR%/}-stage` | :99-103 — must be a **SIBLING** of the cache dir, never inside it: \"fs_lru owns root_dir exclusively… will `os.remove()` it when it becomes the LRU victim. Nesting staging under root_dir therefore hands the evictor the live mmap.\" Implementation: `patch:2443` |\n| **Per-call-invariant latching (MoE)** | `patch:1261-1288` + `opt_flags_amd.py:13-28` + `patch:1384-1433` | 3 device queries + 7 env reads + 4 target queries | patch:1249-1260; justified by \"must be exported before `ray start` so both TP ranks agree, so a per-call read cannot observe anything a first-use read would not\" |\n| **Per-call-invariant latching (W8A8 flags)** | `patch:1449-1459` | `_DS4_W8A8_BF16`, `_DS4_W8A8_BF16_DIRECT` at import | patch:1449-1451 — \"a per-call lookup buys nothing and costs ~255 os.environ hits per decode step\" |\n| `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` surgery | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:89-96` | strips **only** `/opt/rocm/llvm/lib` | :84-88 — that path's runtimes \"change ROCr's initialization order and reproduce the AsyncEventsLoop spin even with the patched DSO preloaded\" |\n| `LD_PRELOAD` of patched ROCr | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:103-116` | prepends `…/_rocm_sdk_core/lib/libhsa-runtime64.so.1` | :97-102; `DS4_HSA_PRELOAD=0` disables only the preload |\n| `HSA_ENABLE_MWAITX` | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:121` | `${DS4_HSA_MWAITX:-0}` | :117-120 — optional fallback for *finite* active waits |\n| `PYTHONWARNINGS` | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:28` | append `ignore::FutureWarning` | :5-8 — per-step `all_gather_into_tensor` deprecation → journal spam |\n| `VLLM_RAY_EXTRA_ENV_VAR_PREFIXES_TO_COPY` | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:78` | `DS4_` | :77 — \"propagate DS4_* to box2 ray workers (not in ray's default copy prefixes)\" — **essential**, without it the two TP ranks diverge |\n| NCCL/RDMA block | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:29-41` | `NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=thunderbolt0`, `NCCL_IB_HCA=usb4_rdma`, `NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=1`, `NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0`, `NCCL_NET_GDR_LEVEL=0`, `NCCL_IB_TIMEOUT=23`, `NCCL_PROTO=LL`, `NCCL_ALGO=Ring`, `NCCL_IB_RETRY_CNT=7`, `TORCH_NCCL_HEARTBEAT_TIMEOUT_SEC=2400`, `TORCH_NCCL_ENABLE_MONITORING=0`, `NCCL_TIMEOUT_MS=2400000` | — |\n| Ray block | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:42-44` | `RAY_EXPERIMENTAL_NOSET_ROCR_VISIBLE_DEVICES=1`, `RAY_memory_monitor_refresh_ms=0`, `RAY_memory_usage_threshold=0.99` | — |\n| Misc | `host/ds4-cluster-env.sh:51-53` | `HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0`, `VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=0`, `VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1800` | — |\n\n### 5.4 ⚠ `ds4-cluster-env.sh` MoE knobs — record cite `:127` RE-PINNED\n\nRecord cited \":127 MoE knobs\". At `:127` sits the **comment header**, not the exports:\n\n- `:127-130` — comment: *\"MXFP4 matmul_ogs DECODE kernel config (tuned on this hardware;\n  block_k 256 + num_stages 2 is the bandwidth lever the stock heuristic never picks).\n  Decode-scoped in opt_flags (only under block_m<128) so prefill is untouched. MUST live\n  here so BOTH TP ranks match. Unset the 5 vars to revert.\"*\n- `:144-148` — the **actual exports** (five of them) [S]:\n\n```bash\nexport DS4_MOE_BN=${DS4_MOE_BN:-32}\nexport DS4_MOE_NW=${DS4_MOE_NW:-2}\nexport DS4_MOE_NS=${DS4_MOE_NS:-2}\nexport DS4_MOE_BK=${DS4_MOE_BK:-256}\nexport DS4_MOE_WPE=${DS4_MOE_WPE:-1}\n```\n\n`opt_flags.py` reads **seven** `DS4_MOE_*` keys (patch:1288: `BM, BN, NW, NS, BK,\nKEEP_MFMA, WPE`) but the env file exports only **five**. `DS4_MOE_BM` and\n`DS4_MOE_KEEP_MFMA` are implemented-but-never-deployed. The comment at :130 saying\n\"the 5 vars\" is consistent with the env file, not with the reader. [M/S]\n\nAlso note :131-135 places the `DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL` comment **inside** the MoE comment\nblock — the two are textually interleaved and easy to misread when lifting.\n\n### 5.5 Cluster restart script — the two things it encodes (`ds4-cluster-restart.sh:8-23`)\n\nBoth are quoted verbatim in the header and both are non-obvious [S]:\n\n1. **REAPING** (:10-15). `ds4-vllm-manual` is a transient `systemd-run` unit supervising\n   a `podman exec` **wrapper**, not the process inside the container. Stopping the unit\n   \"leaves `vllm serve` running, holding its port and ~0.4 GB. Repeated restarts strand\n   one husk each.\" Implementation :63-69: `ps` + bracket-grep `bin/[v]llm serve deepseek`\n   (:63, trick documented at :62), SIGTERM → 3s → SIGKILL, then a **hard gate**:\n   `[ \"$residual\" -eq 0 ] || { … exit 1; }` (:69).\n2. **RAY WORKER POOL** (:17-23). `ray start` passes\n   `--num_prestart_python_workers=<num_cpus>` through with \"no env override\n   (ray/_private/services.py:1980)\"; unbounded that is \"32 idle Python workers at ~40 MB\n   each, ~1.28 GB that vLLM never touches\". Fix: `RAY_NUM_CPUS=${RAY_NUM_CPUS:-4}` (:38)\n   → `--num-cpus=$RAY_NUM_CPUS` (:92). Dashboard off for the same reason (:93).\n\nOther pinned structure [S]: config load :31 · `box2()`/`inbox()` ssh/podman helpers\n:54-55 · memory drain loop with `<45G` gate :74-80 · `container-heal.sh` on both boxes\n:84-85 · head-only `--include-dashboard=false` (:93, \"ray PANICs if it is passed to a\nworker\" :91) · **2-GPU gate** :103-108 (aborts if `ray status` never reports `2.0 GPU`)\n· `systemd-run --user --unit=ds4-vllm-manual` :112-115 · API poll 105×20s ≈ 35 min\n:119-125 (warm ≈4 min, cold-kernel-cache ≈+25 min, :117-118) · warmup dispatched as a\nseparate `--collect` transient unit :130-135 · verify block :137-145 incl. the RDMA\nreadiness grep `tbv_ar2: rank[0-9] ready \\(qpn=…\\)` (:141) which prints\n`!! tbv_ar2 NOT ready -- decode all-reduce is not on RDMA` on miss (:142).\n\n### 5.6 Teardown (`ds4-cluster-down.sh`) [S]\n\nIdempotent (:5). Tolerates a broken config: `eval … 2>/dev/null || true` with hardcoded\nfallbacks (:12-16). Same reap loop (:23-27), then `ray stop --force` locally (:29-30) and\nover ssh (:31-32). `exit 0` unconditionally (:34).\n\n### 5.7 Warmup (`ds4-vllm-warmup.py`) [S]\n\nEnv: `DS4_VLLM_PORT` (:13, dflt `1234`), `DS4_WARMUP_MODEL` (:14, dflt\n`deepseek-v4-flash`), `DS4_WARMUP_CTX` (:17, dflt `2048`), `DS4_WARMUP` (:50, dflt `1`;\n`0` disables). `wait_ready(timeout_s=1200)` :24. Two phases: (1) `fire(\"Say ACK.\", 12,\n300)` :60 — \"compiles the ~50 vLLM Triton kernels (topk/w8a8/sparse-attn/metadata) +\ndecode + MTP drafter\" (:55-57); (2) one `WARMUP_CTX`-sized prefill :69 — \"one long\nprefill grows context through every 8192-bucket\" (:64), which matches\n`_PREFILL_KV_BUCKET = 8192` at `ds4_tl_indexer.py:312`. Every phase wrapped in\ntry/except (:58-62, :67-72) — \"Best-effort: never fails the service\" (:9).\n\n### 5.8 systemd unit (`host/systemd/ds4-vllm.service`) [S]\n\n`Type=oneshot` + `RemainAfterExit=yes` (:14-15); `TimeoutStartSec=45min` (:16),\n`TimeoutStopSec=5min` (:17). `ExecStart=%h/ds4-cluster-restart.sh` (:18),\n`ExecStop=%h/ds4-cluster-down.sh` (:19), **`ExecStopPost=%h/ds4-cluster-down.sh`** (:23)\nwith the reason at :20-22: *\"ExecStop does not run when ExecStart itself fails; StopPost\ndoes, so a failed bringup still tears the cluster down instead of leaving the serve unit\nand ray daemons running behind a 'failed' wrapper.\"*\n**No `[Install]` section** — deliberate, :9-11: \"the model takes minutes to load and\nclaims both GPUs, so the stack comes up only on an explicit start, never at boot.\nhy3-llamacpp declares `Conflicts=ds4-vllm.service`\".\n\n### 5.9 Serve flags (`ds4-vllm-manual-serve.sh:111-130`) [S]\n\n`--tensor-parallel-size 2` :113 · `--distributed-executor-backend ray` :114 ·\n**`--enforce-eager` :115** · `--kv-cache-dtype fp8` :116 ·\n`--gpu-memory-utilization ${DS4_GPU_UTIL:-0.83}` :117 ·\n`--kv-cache-memory-bytes ${DS4_KV_BYTES:-6442450944}` :118 ·\n`--max-model-len ${DS4_MAX_CTX:-524288}` :119 · **`--max-num-batched-tokens 512`** :120 ·\n`--tokenizer-mode/--reasoning-parser/--tool-call-parser deepseek_v4` :122-127 ·\n`--speculative-config '{\"method\":\"deepseek_mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5,\n\"disable_padded_drafter_batch\":true,\"enforce_eager\":true}'` :128.\n\nThree memory notes worth lifting (:9-20): `--kv-cache-memory-bytes` must be pinned\nbecause \"the bf16 weight cache and the RDMA buffers are allocated AFTER the profiling\npass\"; `--gpu-memory-utilization` is \"INERT while the pin above is set … (gpu_worker.py:384)\";\n`--max-num-batched-tokens 512` **not** 2048 because \"the indexer/top-k workspace scales\nwith batch x context and 2048 costs ~10 GiB more at 256K\".\n\n⚠ Syntax landmine, :22-24: *\"Do not add comments inside the backslash-continued `vllm\nserve` command below: a '#' there silently comments out every remaining argument, and\n`bash -n` still reports the file as valid.\"*\n\nPre-flight degrade check :86-92: if the image lacks `lru_manager.py` **or**\n`distributed.py`, warn loudly and set `DS4_DISK_KV=0` rather than let `vllm serve` die on\n`\"Unknown secondary tier type: 'fs_lru'\"` (:81-85).\n\n---\n\n## 6. `AGENTS.md` bring-up doctrine\n\n### 6.1 §0.1 prerequisites boundary — quoted verbatim (`AGENTS.md:35-45`)\n\n> ## 0.1 Prerequisites (verify these exist; do NOT try to synthesize them)\n>\n> - **2× AMD Strix Halo / gfx1151**, ~128 GB unified memory each, on the same LAN.\n> - A **Thunderbolt-4 / USB4 cable** physically connecting the two boxes.\n> - Linux with **kernel headers/devel** for the running kernel on each box, `podman`,\n>   `distrobox`, `rdma-core`/`libibverbs`, `git`, build toolchain.\n> - The model weights **`deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731`** (~150 GB) downloaded\n>   on **both** boxes (`hf download deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731`).\n> - Root/sudo on both boxes (kernel modules, systemd units).\n> - **Secure Boot disabled on both boxes** — the tbv modules are unsigned;\n>   a Secure Boot kernel will refuse every `insmod` in §1.\n\n[S] The boundary is in the heading itself: **\"verify these exist; do NOT try to\nsynthesize them\"** (:35). Followed by the role-fixing paragraph :47-51 (\"Pick roles now\nand keep them consistent everywhere\").\n\n### 6.2 §1.5 RDMA gate — quoted verbatim (`AGENTS.md:134-150`)\n\n> ### 1.5 Verify RDMA (gate)\n>\n> ```bash\n> ls /sys/class/infiniband/                 # -> usb4_rdma0 (or usb4_rdma5)\n> rdma link                                 # port state ACTIVE / PHYS_STATE LinkUp\n> cat /sys/class/infiniband/usb4_rdma0/ports/1/gids/1   # NON-zero (RoCEv2 IPv4 GID = index 1)\n> ibv_devices                               # lists usb4_rdma0\n> ```\n> If `gids/1` is all-zero, `thunderbolt0` has no `192.168.100.x` IP yet — fix the IP\n> first. If `usb4_rdma*` never appears after a kernel change, the `.ko` vermagic no\n> longer matches: rebuild (§1.1–1.2) and `sudo systemctl restart tbv-roce.service`\n> on both boxes.\n>\n> **De-risk option:** RDMA is a performance layer, not a correctness gate — set\n> `transport: tcp` in `~/ds4-config.yaml` to run the same cluster over sockets\n> (much slower decode). If you want to validate the model path first, skip to\n> §2–§4 on TCP now and return to finish RDMA once tokens are flowing.\n\n[S] **The de-risk clause (:147-150) is what makes the campaign's RDMA exclusion legal:\nthe document itself declares RDMA non-load-bearing for correctness.**\n\n### 6.3 Full gate order\n\nDeclared layer order, `AGENTS.md:27-33` [S]:\n> Three independent layers, build/verify them in this order:\n> 1. **tbv RDMA** (`tbv/`) … \"Foundational and the riskiest; do it first.\"\n> 2. **vLLM engine** (`container/`)\n> 3. **Host orchestration** (`host/`)\n\nEnumerated gates in document order [S]:\n\n| # | Gate | Pin | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G0 | Prerequisites present (not synthesized) | :35-45 | all six bullets, incl. Secure Boot **disabled** |\n| G0.2 | Recall/context integrity | :55-68 | `DS4_IDX_OFFICIAL=1` on **both** ranks; `deepseek_v4_encoding.py` patch present |","truncated":true,"truncatedBy":"bytes","totalLines":1273,"totalBytes":75808,"outputLines":875,"outputBytes":51096,"lastLinePartial":false,"firstLineExceedsLimit":false,"maxLines":2000,"maxBytes":51200}},"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988134102},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The complete detailed content of ds4-vllm-manifest.md has been obtained. Section 3 describes the three VENDOR instruments. To adapt these, I should read the actual upstream source files at /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/: ds4_synctrace.py (93 lines), ds4_expert_union.py (128 lines), ds4_offload_batch.py (154 lines).\n\nAlso, I need to read Section 4 of specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md (the retargeting of the fused_topk wrap).\n\nAnd I'll also read scripts/receipts-verify.py for style reference.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me read section 4 of qsa-53896.md and the style reference, plus the upstream source files.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_04f119e8460f4a689081d7dd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"^## \" /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_691c04fbe6664c888b5cbd6b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":20265,"output":327,"cacheRead":6272,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":158,"totalTokens":26864,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988134108,"responseId":"chatcmpl-c8fb3c75-97a9-4003-91f4-789697fff23d","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_04f119e8460f4a689081d7dd","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"7:## Artifacts examined\n26:## Headline\n45:## 1. BUG A — dense-behind-a-mask: **NOT PRESENT** (both prefill and decode)\n106:## 2. BUG B — CPU/Python-loop top-k: **NOT PRESENT**\n179:## 3. Platform split\n284:## 4. MoE routing\n352:## 5. The QSA tests — what they assert, and what they cannot catch\n418:## 6. Indexer pre-scoring transform — no hadamard, no quantization\n503:## Residual UNDETERMINEDs\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988142144},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_691c04fbe6664c888b5cbd6b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"aiter\nds4_expert_union.py\nds4_offload_batch.py\nds4_synctrace.py\nds4_tl_indexer.py\nds4_topk.py\ntbv_ar2.py\ntbv_ar.py\nvllm\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988142144},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — the current worktree is at /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments. The ls output shows the rootfs directory contents... wait, the second bash command listed /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/. Alright, the upstream files exist.\n\nI'll read section 4 of qsa-53896.md, and the three upstream files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_8fdd5bae713445609ba35bd8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"sed -n '284,351p' /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_48fc78f743e3450ab6685160","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"wc -l /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_{synctrace,expert_union,offload_batch}.py; head -3 /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/LICENSE 2>/dev/null; ls /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/LICENSE* 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1484,"output":319,"cacheRead":25600,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":116,"totalTokens":27403,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988142148,"responseId":"chatcmpl-ed53d617-0ff1-4bec-a2cf-8f59abd3870b","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8fdd5bae713445609ba35bd8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## 4. MoE routing\n\n### Which layer implementation\n\n`vllm/models/qwen4_exp/nvidia/model.py:160-171` — `class Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock(Qwen3NextSparseMoeBlock)`;\nits `__init__` only rejects sequence-parallel MoE and sets `n_shared_experts`, then\n`super().__init__(...)`. **[S]** Instantiated at `nvidia/model.py:245-247` when\n`num_experts > 0 and (layer_idx+1) % decoder_sparse_step == 0` (`:239-244`). **[S]**\n\nThe parent is stock vLLM: `vllm/model_executor/models/qwen3_next.py:128` `class\nQwen3NextSparseMoeBlock(nn.Module)`, which builds `self.experts = FusedMoEFactory(... top_k=\nconfig.num_experts_per_tok, ...)` at `:215-235` and calls it at `:256-258`. **[S]** So: **vLLM\n`FusedMoE`, not `triton_kernels.matmul_ogs`, not a custom MoE.**\n\n### The routing code and the power-of-2 question\n\n`FusedMoEFactory` is defined at `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/layer.py:88` **[M]**.\nRouter selection lands in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/router_factory.py:230`\n`return FusedTopKRouter(...)` as the default fallback (`:76` comment: *\"7. FusedTopKRouter -\ndefault fallback\"*). **[S]**\n\n`FusedTopKRouter._compute_routing` — `router/fused_topk_router.py:156-174` — calls `fused_topk`\n(`:80-124`), which allocates `[M, topk]` tensors and dispatches to\n`vllm_topk_softmax` → `ops.topk_softmax` (`:33-42`) or `rocm_aiter_ops.topk_softmax` when\n`rocm_aiter_ops.is_fused_moe_enabled()` (`:64-69`, `:106-108`). **[S]**\n\n**There is no `tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)` and no power-of-2 requirement on this path.**\n`topk` is a plain runtime integer used only as a tensor dimension (`:92-103`). A\n`num_experts_per_tok = 10` routes fine.\n\n### Does the PR touch `triton_kernels` at all?\n\nNo. `grep -rln \"triton_kernels\" vllm/` returns 14 files, all mxfp4 / gpt-oss / aiter / quark /\nimport-util paths **[M]**; none of them is under `vllm/models/qwen4_exp/`. `find … -path\n\"*triton_kernels*\" -name \"*.py\"` inside the checkout returns only\n`vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py` and its test **[M]**\n— the third-party package itself is not vendored here.\n\nTwo further points that defuse the ds4-vllm concern for this PR:\n\n1. The evaluated checkpoint is **FP8**, not mxfp4:\n   `tests/evals/qwen4_exp/configs/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8.yaml` → `model_name:\n   \"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8\"`, `server_args: \"--tensor-parallel-size 4\"`; both\n   `configs/models-h200.txt` and `models-b200.txt` list only that yaml **[S]**. FP8 MoE goes\n   through `fused_moe/oracle/fp8.py` (`select_fp8_moe_backend` at `:305`, ROCm/CUDA branch at\n   `:447`), which resolves to `TritonExperts` (`:190-194`) or `rocm_aiter_moe` (`:204`) — not the\n   gpt-oss triton_kernels path.\n2. Even if it did land there, **this branch already carries the pow2 fix**:\n   `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/experts/gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.py:209-224`\n   `_patch_legacy_routing_for_nonpow2_topk()`, whose docstring names the exact defect —\n   *\"The bundled `_routing_compute_indx` does `tl.arange(0, N_EXPTS_ACT * BLOCK_M)`, which fails\n   to compile when `N_EXPTS_ACT` (top_k) is not a power of 2 (6 * 32 = 192)\"* — and installs\n   `_routing_compute_indx_pow2` with `BLOCK_SIZE_PADDED` (`:239-270`, note `local_offs =\n   tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE_PADDED)` at `:260` and `BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr = N_EXPTS_ACT *\n   BLOCK_M` at `:259`, with masking at `:262-266`). **[S]** The fix the ds4-vllm campaign called\n   mandatory is already upstream in this tree.\n\n### The ROCm (non-CUDA) build's exact path\n\n`Qwen4ExpForCausalLM` from `amd/model.py` (dispatch in §3) → `Qwen4ExpSparseMoeBlock`\n(`amd/model.py:245-247`, the file is a mirror of nvidia's — `amd/model.py:239-247` matches\n`nvidia/model.py:239-247` by grep **[M]**) → `Qwen3NextSparseMoeBlock` → `FusedMoEFactory` →\n`FusedTopKRouter` → `fused_topk` → **`rocm_aiter_ops.topk_softmax` if\n`rocm_aiter_ops.is_fused_moe_enabled()` else `ops.topk_softmax`**\n(`router/fused_topk_router.py:64-69`, `:106-111`) → experts kernel from `oracle/fp8.py`\n(`rocm_aiter_moe` at `:204`, with an aiter skip predicate at `:409-414` falling back to\n`TritonExperts`). **No triton_kernels, no `N_EXPTS_ACT`.** **[S]**\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988149777},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_48fc78f743e3450ab6685160","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   93 /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_synctrace.py\n  128 /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_expert_union.py\n  154 /home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_offload_batch.py\n  375 total\n                                 Apache License\n                           Version 2.0, January 2004\n                        http://www.apache.org/licenses/\n/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/LICENSE\n\n/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/LICENSES:\nGPL-2.0.txt\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988149777},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a grasp of the whole picture:\n\n- The wrap target of fn_expert_union.py is `fused_topk` in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py` (the standard FusedTopKRouter path), not `make_routing_data` in gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe. According to qsa-53896.md §4, the workload goes through FusedTopKRouter → fused_topk.\n\nNext, I'll read the 3 upstream files in full.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now reading the three upstream instrument modules to adapt them.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4b1d8a81827843a48d149862","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_synctrace.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d95980f9cf6a4ae097c4d1e1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_expert_union.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c9d81a36397f4638a78a786a","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/Downloads/ds4-vllm/container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_offload_batch.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":3760,"output":301,"cacheRead":25344,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":119,"totalTokens":29405,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988149781,"responseId":"chatcmpl-acb2099e-2221-41c2-8e3f-764395942ce7","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4b1d8a81827843a48d149862","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Attribute blocking device->host syncs to python call sites.\n\nThe fresh 2026-08-07 profile puts hipMemcpyWithStream at 42% of decode self-CPU\nand hipStreamSynchronize at 16% -- together the dominant cost, now that kernel\nlaunches are down 39%. But `hipMemcpyWithStream` in a profiler table is just a\ncount; it does not say which line caused it.\n\n`with_stack=True` on the torch profiler answers that in principle and is\nunusable in practice here: it captures a python stack for every one of ~3,200\nops per step, which pegged the worker at 94% CPU and stalled the engine on\nshm_broadcast.\n\nThis is the cheap alternative. It wraps only the handful of Tensor methods that\ncan force a blocking D2H, and records one `sys._getframe` per call -- ~25 events\nper step rather than ~3,200. Overhead is a dict increment on an already-blocking\noperation, i.e. noise.\n\nLimitation worth knowing: boolean-mask indexing (`x[mask]`) reaches nonzero()\ninside C++ `at::index`, not through the python method, so it is NOT counted\nhere. Anything unattributed after this is a candidate for that.\n\nDriven from ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile so it shares the DS4_PROFILE window\n(no new env var, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport collections\nimport sys\n\nimport torch\n\n_counts = collections.Counter()\n_installed = False\n_orig = {}\n# Tensor methods that block on a device->host transfer.\n_TARGETS = (\"item\", \"tolist\", \"cpu\", \"numpy\", \"nonzero\", \"__float__\", \"__int__\")\n\n\ndef _wrap(name):\n    orig = getattr(torch.Tensor, name)\n\n    def wrapper(self, *a, **kw):\n        try:\n            f = sys._getframe(1)\n            _counts[f\"{f.f_code.co_filename.split('site-packages/')[-1]}:\"\n                    f\"{f.f_lineno} {f.f_code.co_name}() [{name}]\"] += 1\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        return orig(self, *a, **kw)\n\n    _orig[name] = orig\n    setattr(torch.Tensor, name, wrapper)\n\n\ndef install():\n    global _installed\n    if _installed:\n        return\n    for n in _TARGETS:\n        try:\n            _wrap(n)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    _installed = True\n\n\ndef uninstall():\n    global _installed\n    for n, o in _orig.items():\n        try:\n            setattr(torch.Tensor, n, o)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    _orig.clear()\n    _installed = False\n\n\ndef reset():\n    _counts.clear()\n\n\ndef report(steps=1.0):\n    \"\"\"Formatted table, per-decode-step, most frequent first.\"\"\"\n    if not _counts:\n        return (\"### BLOCKING-SYNC ATTRIBUTION ###\\n  (no events -- either the \"\n                \"tracer never installed, or every sync is bool-mask indexing / \"\n                \"C++-internal and invisible to a python hook)\\n\\n\")\n    total = sum(_counts.values())\n    out = [f\"### BLOCKING-SYNC ATTRIBUTION ({total} events over {steps:.2f} \"\n           f\"decode steps = {total / max(steps, 1e-9):.1f}/step) ###\"]\n    for site, n in _counts.most_common(30):\n        out.append(f\"  {n / max(steps, 1e-9):7.1f}/step  ({n:5d})  {site}\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\\n\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988158219},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d95980f9cf6a4ae097c4d1e1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"DS4_EXPERT_UNION=1: measure how many DISTINCT experts a decode step touches.\n\nThe decode roof (docs/DS4_DECODE_CEILING.md) is dominated by routed-expert\nbytes, and those scale with the *union* of experts the step's positions select,\nnot with 6-per-token. Independent routing would put the union at ~34 experts per\nlayer for a K=6 verify; perfectly correlated routing puts it at 6. That factor\nof ~5.7 moves the physics ceiling by 60%, and nothing static can settle it --\nit has to be measured against real traffic.\n\nThis wraps `make_routing_data` in vLLM's matmul_ogs MoE path, which is the one\nchoke point where `topk_ids` exists for both the legacy-`routing_from_bitmatrix`\nand the `SparseMatrix` branch. It is NOT reachable through vLLM's own\n`--enable-return-routed-experts`: that capturer hangs off `BaseRouter.route()`,\nwhich this model never calls (routing happens inside the triton_kernels path).\n\nPer call it records (n_rows, n_distinct, n_local_experts) into a preallocated\ndevice buffer using only elementwise kernels -- no D2H copy, no sync, so it does\nnot serialise the step it is measuring. The buffer is copied out once when the\nwindow closes.\n\nCost: ~4 extra small kernel launches per MoE call, ~184 per step against the\n~5,230 the step already issues (~3.5%). Off unless DS4_EXPERT_UNION=1.\n\nEnv:\n    DS4_EXPERT_UNION=1        enable\n    DS4_EU_START=200          skip this many calls first (warmup + prefill)\n    DS4_EU_CALLS=2000         window size in MoE calls (~46/decode step)\n    DS4_EU_OUT=~/vllm-prof            output directory\n\nAnalyse the dump with host/bench/expert_union.py.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport atexit\nimport os\n\nimport torch\n\n_ENABLED = os.environ.get(\"DS4_EXPERT_UNION\") == \"1\"\n_START = int(os.environ.get(\"DS4_EU_START\", \"200\"))\n_CALLS = int(os.environ.get(\"DS4_EU_CALLS\", \"2000\"))\n_OUT = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get(\"DS4_EU_OUT\", \"~/vllm-prof\"))\n\n_buf = None          # [_CALLS, 3] int32 on device\n_n = 0               # calls seen\n_done = False\n_installed = False\n\n\ndef _record(topk_ids, num_local_experts):\n    \"\"\"Accumulate one routing call. Device-only; never synchronises.\"\"\"\n    global _buf, _n, _done\n    if _done:\n        return\n    _n += 1\n    if _n <= _START:\n        return\n    i = _n - _START - 1\n    if i >= _CALLS:\n        _flush()\n        return\n\n    ids = topk_ids.reshape(-1).long()\n    if _buf is None:\n        _buf = torch.zeros(_CALLS, 3, dtype=torch.int32, device=ids.device)\n\n    # Slot 0 absorbs the -1 padding rows so no boolean mask (and therefore no\n    # size-dependent sync) is needed; real experts land at 1..num_local.\n    seen = torch.zeros(num_local_experts + 1, dtype=torch.bool, device=ids.device)\n    seen[ids + 1] = True\n\n    _buf[i, 0] = topk_ids.shape[0]\n    _buf[i, 1] = seen[1:].sum()\n    _buf[i, 2] = num_local_experts\n\n\ndef _flush():\n    \"\"\"Copy the buffer out once and write the dump.\"\"\"\n    global _done\n    if _done or _buf is None:\n        return\n    _done = True\n    try:\n        rows = _buf.cpu().tolist()\n        os.makedirs(_OUT, exist_ok=True)\n        path = os.path.join(_OUT, f\"expert_union_{os.getpid()}.tsv\")\n        with open(path, \"w\") as fh:\n            fh.write(\"# n_rows\\tn_distinct\\tn_local_experts\\n\")\n            for n_rows, n_distinct, n_local in rows:\n                if n_rows:\n                    fh.write(f\"{n_rows}\\t{n_distinct}\\t{n_local}\\n\")\n        print(f\"[ds4_expert_union] wrote {path}\", flush=True)\n    except Exception as exc:  # a probe must never take the engine down\n        print(f\"[ds4_expert_union] flush failed: {exc}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef install():\n    \"\"\"Idempotently wrap make_routing_data. Safe to call more than once.\"\"\"\n    global _installed\n    if not _ENABLED or _installed:\n        return\n    try:\n        from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.experts import (\n            gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe as m,\n        )\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"[ds4_expert_union] not installed: {exc}\", flush=True)\n        return\n\n    orig = m.make_routing_data\n\n    def wrapped(topk_ids, topk_weights, num_local_experts, *a, **kw):\n        try:\n            _record(topk_ids, num_local_experts)\n        except Exception:\n            pass  # never let the probe break routing\n        return orig(topk_ids, topk_weights, num_local_experts, *a, **kw)\n\n    wrapped._ds4_orig = orig\n    m.make_routing_data = wrapped\n    _installed = True\n    # Also flush on shutdown, so a run that ends before the window fills still\n    # leaves a (shorter) usable dump rather than nothing.\n    atexit.register(_flush)\n    print(\n        f\"[ds4_expert_union] installed: skip {_START} calls, window {_CALLS}, \"\n        f\"out {_OUT}\",\n        flush=True,\n    )\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988158219},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c9d81a36397f4638a78a786a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n\"\"\"Store-batch budget for the KV offloading connector.\n\nWhy this exists\n---------------\n``OffloadingConnectorScheduler._build_store_jobs`` asks the offloading manager\nto stage every not-yet-offloaded block of a request in a single\n``prepare_store()`` call. That call is all-or-nothing: the CPU primary tier\nreturns ``None`` unless it can make room for *every* key at once, and the\ncaller's failure path logs ``cannot store blocks`` and ``continue``s **without\nadvancing** ``next_stored_block_idx``.\n\nSo a single refusal is not self-correcting. The next step recomputes the range\nfrom the same unadvanced cursor against a larger ``num_offloadable_tokens``,\nasks for strictly more than it just failed to get, and fails again. The ask\nratchets upward until the request is demanding its entire prefix in one call,\nwhich no small tier can ever satisfy. The observed symptom — a 182K prefill\nagainst a 256 MiB tier refusing stores — reads like \"the tier must be sized to\nthe in-flight sequence\", but the tier is a proper LRU cache with refcounting:\n``TieringOffloadingManager.complete_store`` pins a block via\n``primary.prepare_read()`` and ``_process_finished_jobs`` unpins it via\n``primary.complete_read()`` as soon as the secondary-tier write lands. Blocks\n*do* recycle. Nothing was bounding the ask.\n\nBounding it turns the primary tier into a streaming window: each step stages at\nmost a budget's worth of blocks, those drain to disk, their ref_cnt drops, and\nthe next step reuses the same slots. The tier then has to cover the drain\nlatency, not the sequence — which is what makes a 15 GB disk cache affordable\nbehind a few hundred MiB of RAM.\n\nThis lives outside ``vllm`` so the budget arithmetic is unit-testable without\nimporting torch or the connector's dependency graph.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"resolve_store_batch_tokens\",\n    \"resolve_promote_block_budget\",\n    \"DEFAULT_FRAC\",\n    \"FRAC_ENV\",\n    \"DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC\",\n    \"PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV\",\n]\n\nFRAC_ENV = \"DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\"\nPROMOTE_FRAC_ENV = \"DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\"\n\n# A quarter of the tier per step. The remaining three quarters absorb blocks\n# whose disk write is still in flight (ref_cnt > 0, so not evictable) plus the\n# resident prefix-cache entries the tier exists to serve.\nDEFAULT_FRAC = 0.25\n\n# Half the tier per request for reads. Promotion has the mirror-image failure\n# of the store ratchet, and it is worse because it wastes disk bandwidth before\n# failing: lookup() initiates one promotion per matched block with nothing\n# bounding the total, so a prefix longer than the primary tier evicts its own\n# earlier promotions to make room for later ones. The prefix is then never\n# wholly resident, _maximal_prefix_lookup never confirms it, and the request\n# recomputes everything anyway -- after paying the full disk read. Measured on\n# a 4,645-token prompt against a 258-block tier: 258 blocks (512 MiB) read from\n# disk, \"cannot store blocks\", and zero hits.\n#\n# Capping the ask below the tier size means the promoted prefix stays resident,\n# so a partial hit is real work saved instead of thrash. The remainder is left\n# for in-flight stores, which share the same tier.\nDEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC = 0.5\n\n\ndef _read_frac(frac: float | None, env: str, default: float) -> float:\n    if frac is not None:\n        return frac\n    raw = os.getenv(env)\n    if raw is None or raw == \"\":\n        return default\n    try:\n        return float(raw)\n    except ValueError:\n        return default\n\n\ndef resolve_store_batch_tokens(\n    num_blocks: int | None,\n    offloaded_block_sizes: \"list[int] | tuple[int, ...]\",\n    frac: float | None = None,\n) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Token budget for one prepare_store() call, or None for unbounded.\n\n    Args:\n        num_blocks: Blocks in the CPU primary tier. None/0 (a spec that does\n            not expose it) disables bounding.\n        offloaded_block_sizes: ``offloaded_block_size`` of every KV group. One\n            token range yields one key per group, so the key count a token\n            budget produces is the sum of the per-group rates.\n        frac: Fraction of the tier to spend per step. Defaults to\n            ``$DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC`` then ``DEFAULT_FRAC``. A value\n            <= 0 disables bounding, restoring stock vLLM behaviour.\n\n    Returns:\n        Token budget, never smaller than one block of the coarsest group.\n\n        That floor is load-bearing, not a rounding nicety. Groups keep separate\n        cursors over a shared token position, so a budget measured from the\n        laggard group has to be wide enough to reach every group's existing\n        cursor; the gap is at most one block of the coarsest group. Below the\n        floor, some group's target would land under its own cursor, and\n        ``_build_store_jobs`` assigns ``next_stored_block_idx = num_blocks``\n        outright — it never takes a max — so the cursor would rewind and the\n        blocks in between would be skipped for good.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _budget(num_blocks, offloaded_block_sizes, frac, FRAC_ENV, DEFAULT_FRAC)\n\n\ndef resolve_promote_block_budget(\n    num_blocks: int | None, frac: float | None = None\n) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Max blocks one request may promote, or None for unbounded.\n\n    Deliberately counted in **blocks, not tokens**. The token form of this\n    budget divides by the summed per-group key rate, which a sliding-window\n    group wrecks: its blocks are tiny and numerous (208 of them against 26 for\n    a full-attention group on the same 4,645 tokens), so it dominates the rate\n    and collapses the budget to a few hundred tokens -- about 6% of the prompt\n    -- even though its lookup only ever touches a bounded tail. Counting the\n    promotions themselves needs no model of any of that.\n\n    Applies to the full-attention prefix scan only; see the call site.\n    ``DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC=0`` restores stock behaviour (promote the whole\n    matched prefix, and thrash if it does not fit).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not num_blocks or num_blocks <= 0:\n        return None\n    frac = _read_frac(frac, PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV, DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC)\n    if frac <= 0:\n        return None\n    return max(1, int(num_blocks * min(frac, 1.0)))\n\n\ndef _budget(num_blocks, offloaded_block_sizes, frac, env, default):\n    if not num_blocks or num_blocks <= 0:\n        return None\n    sizes = [int(s) for s in offloaded_block_sizes if s and s > 0]\n    if not sizes:\n        return None\n\n    frac = _read_frac(frac, env, default)\n    if frac <= 0:\n        return None\n\n    budget_blocks = max(1, int(num_blocks * min(frac, 1.0)))\n    keys_per_token = sum(1.0 / s for s in sizes)\n    budget_tokens = int(budget_blocks / keys_per_token)\n\n    return max(budget_tokens, max(sizes))\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988158220},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Alright, so let me check the style reference scripts/receipts-verify.py and the existing tests (test_repo_invariants.py), the container/Containerfile (to understand how the rootfs is used), and also check the flashnext spec section regarding instruments. I might also check specs/flashnext/spec.md. I'll also take a look at scripts/receipts-verify.py.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_192eb893b33f42b5bfa802ff","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/scripts/receipts-verify.py","limit":80}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_653a2c74f7754b178b447bf7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments && head -50 container/Containerfile && grep -n \"rootfs\\|fn_\\|instrument\" container/Containerfile container/build.sh tests/test_repo_invariants.py 2>/dev/null | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":6757,"output":259,"cacheRead":26624,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":79,"totalTokens":33640,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988158225,"responseId":"chatcmpl-86979b0f-8336-4dde-911a-2d8dafba73c8","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_192eb893b33f42b5bfa802ff","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate every overnight receipt under results/receipts/.\n\nA receipt is one JSON object: {\"step\": str, \"status\": \"pass\"|\"fail\",\n\"ts\": str, \"data\": {...}}. Missing receipts are legal (the step has not\nrun); a present receipt must be well-formed, and hard bounds are enforced\nper step. Any violation exits 2 — this is the ladder gate that makes the\novernight claims graded rather than narrated.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nRECEIPTS = ROOT / \"results\" / \"receipts\"\n\n# Per-step hard bounds: step-name prefix -> checker(data) -> error or None.\ndef _residency(d):\n    for rank, gib in (d.get(\"gtt_gib_per_rank\") or {}).items():\n        if gib > 80:\n            return f\"rank {rank} GTT {gib} GiB exceeds the 80 GiB bound\"\n    if d.get(\"table_gpu_resident_bytes\", 0) != 0:\n        return \"table has GPU-resident bytes; the mmap path is not engaged\"\n    if not d.get(\"read_after_warmed_decode\", False):\n        return \"residency was not read after a warmed decode\"\n    return None\n\ndef _tp2(d):\n    if not d.get(\"byte_identical_repeat\", False):\n        return \"greedy repeat was not byte-identical\"\n    return None\n\ndef _weights(d):\n    if d.get(\"shards\", 0) < 131:\n        return f\"only {d.get('shards')} shards staged\"\n    return None\n\ndef _bench(d):\n    if d.get(\"loads_per_arm\", 0) < 3:\n        return \"fewer than 3 loads per arm\"\n    if not d.get(\"counterbalanced\", False):\n        return \"arms were not counterbalanced\"\n    return None\n\ndef _context(d):\n    ratio = d.get(\"decode_ratio_vs_short_context\")\n    if ratio is not None and ratio < 0.9:\n        return f\"full-context decode ratio {ratio} below the 0.9 bound\"\n    return None\n\ndef _smoke(d):\n    ap = (d.get(\"aperture\") or {}).get(\"ttm_pages_limit\")\n    if ap is not None and ap != 33554432:\n        return f\"aperture {ap} diverges from the 33554432-page ceiling\"\n    return None\n\nBOUNDS = {\n    \"residency\": _residency,\n    \"tp2\": _tp2,\n    \"weights\": _weights,\n    \"bench\": _bench,\n    \"context\": _context,\n    \"smoke\": _smoke,\n}\n\ndef _handoff_patch_ok() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"When the catalog patch exists it must parse as a git patch.\"\"\"\n    import subprocess\n    patch = ROOT / \"handoff\" / \"catalog-row.patch\"\n    if not patch.is_file():\n        return None\n    proc = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"apply\", \"--stat\", str(patch)],\n                          capture_output=True, text=True)\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        return f\"handoff/catalog-row.patch does not parse: {proc.stderr.strip()}\"\n    return None\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n\n[36 more lines in file. Use offset=81 to continue.]"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988166472},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_653a2c74f7754b178b447bf7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# flashnext:dev — the engine fork built from source at the exactly pinned wheel set\n# ============================================================================\n#\n# Recipe shape adapted from kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes,\n# `Dockerfile.ubuntu-repoamd` @ 23cb726, credited per THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n# That recipe is MIT licensed; the notice is retained here as required:\n#\n#   MIT License — Copyright (c) kyuz0 (amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes)\n#\n#   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a\n#   copy of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"),\n#   to deal in the Software without restriction, including without limitation\n#   the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,\n#   and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the\n#   Software is furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n#\n#   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in\n#   all copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n#\n#   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n#   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n#   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n#   AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n#   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING\n#   FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER\n#   DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.\n#\n# What changed vs the donor recipe (per IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2):\n#   - torch is pinned to the fork's exact pin 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 from the AMD\n#     stable multi-arch index (the index tops out there; no ROCm 10 wheels\n#     exist for gfx1151 — specs/flashnext/evidence/kyuz0-rocm10.md).\n#   - torchaudio is OMITTED; we drop the audio extra rather than downgrade\n#     torch to 2.11 (torchaudio capped kyuz0's auto-resolved set there).\n#   - the engine is the flashnext fork (mecattaf/vllm, branch flashnext),\n#     built from source for gfx1151, not a stock vLLM ref.\n#   - designed for overnight iteration: bind-mount a fork checkout over\n#     /opt/vllm and a host dir over /root/.ccache (see container/build.sh);\n#     the editable install then recompiles only what a one-line patch touched.\n#\n# Wheel provenance: the torch/triton/vision/rocm-sdk substrate comes ONLY\n# from the vendor stable index (spec F.11). Generic Python build tooling\n# (setuptools, wheel, packaging, setuptools-scm) and vLLM's upstream runtime\n# dependencies resolve from PyPI as upstream vLLM does; none of those is part\n# of the pinned substrate.\n\nFROM docker.io/ubuntu:24.04\n\nARG ROCM_WHL=https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/\n# The exactly pinned wheel set (IMPORTS.md section 1). The triton pin is the\n# wheel accompanying the torch 2.13.0 set on the vendor stable index —\ncontainer/Containerfile:115:# ---- the fn_ instrument overlay ----\ncontainer/Containerfile:116:# Lands the instrument modules importable at the top level of site-packages.\ncontainer/Containerfile:117:COPY container/rootfs/ /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/\ncontainer/build.sh:84:echo \"==> rootfs overlay stage (instruments land here when present)\"\ncontainer/build.sh:85:mkdir -p \"$REPO_ROOT/container/rootfs\"\ncontainer/build.sh:86:[ -e \"$REPO_ROOT/container/rootfs/.keep\" ] || touch \"$REPO_ROOT/container/rootfs/.keep\"\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988166472},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This repo's Containerfile has already COPY'd container/rootfs/ to site-packages (line 117). In other words, the modules placed in container/rootfs/ are importable under bare names inside the image.\n\nInteresting point: build.sh creates a .keep in container/rootfs. Let me check whether .keep exists inside rootfs (my earlier ls showed rootfs as empty — maybe it's gitignored). Let me check .gitignore and the container section of the flashnext spec (spec.md) to see what is expected. Also, to match the house style of the notice header, let me look at THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md too.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_47184111384d4abcb799802f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments && cat .gitignore && ls -la container/rootfs/ && sed -n '110,125p' container/Containerfile && head -60 THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d5c0b80ed5294ad8b742b3f7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments && grep -n -i \"instrument\\|fn_synctrace\\|fn_offload\\|fn_expert\\|FN_\" specs/flashnext/spec.md | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2590,"output":334,"cacheRead":32768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":135,"totalTokens":35692,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988166477,"responseId":"chatcmpl-16894bde-b015-47d4-bf7c-140bfd3c9873","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_47184111384d4abcb799802f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n.direnv/\nresult\n.engine-overlay/\nresult-engine\nresults/logs/\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 tom users 4096 Aug 29 09:21 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 tom users 4096 Aug 29 09:21 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 tom users  226 Aug 29 09:21 .keep\n# Build artifacts land inside /opt/vllm, so a bind-mounted checkout keeps\n# them across rebuilds and ccache (on PATH, auto-detected by vLLM's cmake)\n# recompiles only what changed.\nRUN pip install -e /opt/vllm --no-build-isolation\n\n# ---- the fn_ instrument overlay ----\n# Lands the instrument modules importable at the top level of site-packages.\nCOPY container/rootfs/ /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/\n\n# ---- build identity ----\nRUN mkdir -p /opt/flashnext && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, time, importlib.metadata as md\ndef ver(name):\n    try:\n        return md.version(name)\n    except md.PackageNotFoundError:\n# Third-party code and licenses\n\nThird-party sources are **fetched at pinned revisions at build time, not\nredistributed here** — what this repository itself ships is at most a\nderivative patch against them (each patch is licensed like the code it\nmodifies). Original code in this repository is licensed under\n[Apache-2.0](LICENSE). No GPL code enters this tree (the RDMA transport\nsubtree of the reference implementation is excluded from scope entirely).\n\n| Component | Upstream | License | What this repo ships |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| vLLM (+ PR #53896, #54129 content) | github.com/vllm-project/vllm; fork base `8e4e036` | Apache-2.0 | Derivative patches under `patches/`, mirrored as commits on github.com/mecattaf/vllm branch `flashnext`; provenance per file in `patches/MANIFEST.md` |\n| Cherry-picked open PRs #46012 #40963 #51511 #46110 | github.com/vllm-project/vllm pull requests | Apache-2.0 | Carried as fork commits with `Cherry-picked-from:` trailers; nothing redistributed here |\n| ds4-vllm instruments and discipline | github.com/AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ `a8f620d` | Apache-2.0 | Adapted copies under `container/rootfs/` (`fn_synctrace.py`, `fn_expert_union.py`, `fn_offload_batch.py`) retaining upstream notice headers; the packaging-test discipline reimplemented in `tests/` |\n| amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes container recipe | github.com/kyuz0/amd-strix-halo-vllm-toolboxes @ `23cb726` | MIT | `container/Containerfile` is an adaptation; MIT notice retained in that file's header |\n| nix-strix-halo | github.com/hellas-ai/nix-strix-halo @ `f0f2048` | no license published | Consumed as a Nix flake input only; nothing redistributed, nothing copied |\n| AMD ROCm wheels (torch/triton/vision, rocm 7.14.0) | repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch | per-wheel licenses | Fetched at container build; nothing redistributed |\n\n**Model weights** (`Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8`) are not included and are\ngoverned by their own license on Hugging Face.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988175418},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_d5c0b80ed5294ad8b742b3f7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"44:  scheme on this GPU and adds the in-kernel upcast, switch FN_FP8_MOE.\n81:| P5 | admission shape | the admission extends the upcast mechanism of upstream pull request 52970 to the fused-mixture oracle; refusal stays loud; FN_FP8_MOE=0 restores the stock refusal; no silent fallback is added |\n105:2.2 the admission patch lands on the fork → the verify script finds the FN_FP8_MOE switch and the upcast plumbing in the fused-mixture layer tree. [gate: fork-verify]\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988175418},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md already describes the expected outcome: \"adapted copies under `container/rootfs/` (`fn_synctrace.py`, `fn_expert_union.py`, `fn_offload_batch.py`) retaining upstream's notice headers.\" Upstream: github.com/AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ `a8f620d`, Apache-2.0.\n\nNote that rootfs has a `.keep` file (untracked? let me check with git). In the earlier `ls`, rootfs appeared empty, but `ls -la` shows `.keep`. Is `.keep` tracked? Since `git status` shows clean, `.keep` is either tracked or ignored. Let me verify. Actually, build.sh creates it at build time. Check `git ls-files container/rootfs`.\n\nOkay, the plan:\n1. Create fn_synctrace.py, fn_offload_batch.py, fn_expert_union.py in container/rootfs/:\n   - Adapted from the upstream ds4_* files, prefix renamed from DS4_ to FN_.\n   - Notice header on each file: \"Adapted from <upstream file> in github.com/AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d, Apache-2.0 license\". Should contain the string \"Adapted from\".\n   - fn_expert_union.py: retarget the wrapping to `fused_topk` in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py`. Environment variables FN_EXPERT_UNION, FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT.\n   - fn_synctrace.py: driven from the FN_PROFILE window (mention in the docstring); no env var of its own. Default off — install() only when invoked by the FN_PROFILE driver.\n   - fn_offload_batch.py: FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC, FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC.\n2. tests/test_instruments.py: unittest tests:\n   - py_compile for each module (cfile goes into tempdir to avoid committing bytecode).\n   - Each file has the notice header (\"Adapted from\").\n   - fn_offload_batch's budget arithmetic matches the reference invariants: floor is the max group size; promote counts in block units.\n   \n   The tests must be runnable without torch or vllm (host machine). py_compile is fine. Notice check is fine. Budget arithmetic test — fn_offload_batch is torch-free so it can be imported directly. But the import path: tests are run via `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v` from the repo root. fn_offload_batch lives in container/rootfs/. Tests need to add container/rootfs to sys.path or import via a path. Use importlib.util.spec_from_file_location to load the module from path. This avoids sys.path pollution. Alternatively, insert container/rootfs at the head of sys.path and import fn_offload_batch. Import via spec — cleaner, and it's also the pattern used in the repo? Let me check the style of tests/test_repo_invariants.py.\n\nAlso the \"kill switch, default off\" behavior: fn_expert_union: FN_EXPERT_UNION == \"1\" enables, default off — matches upstream. fn_synctrace: install() only when driven; module import itself does nothing — fine. fn_offload_batch: imported unconditionally by the patched connector, but frac <= 0 → None → falls back to the stock; env vars are configuration, not enablement. The task says \"instruments importable inside the image with FN_ kill switches, default off\". For offload_batch, the \"kill switch\" is the env frac=0 → falls back to stock. Default is on with DEFAULT_FRAC 0.25 — matches upstream behavior; the delivered behavior says \"default off\" — hmm. Regarding the offload module, upstream has no env gate and is imported unconditionally by the patched connector; frac<=0 → None → stock. Leave this as is; note that env frac <= 0 disables bounding (a kill switch). But \"default off\" — the DS4-style default is that bounding is on at 0.25. The acceptance criteria test only checks compilation, notice, and budget arithmetic. The goal says \"env FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC and FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\". Preserve the reference semantics.\n\nOn expert union retargeting: the fused_topk signature in fused_topk_router.py is, per qsa-53896.md §4: `fused_topk` at :80-124, allocates an [M, topk] tensor; `_compute_routing` at :156-174 calls fused_topk. What does fused_topk take? Stock vLLM: `def fused_topk(hidden_states, gating_output, topk, renormalize)` returning topk_weights, topk_ids. The wrapped `_compute_routing` calls fused_topk(hidden_states, router_logits, top_k, renormalize). num_local_experts isn't in the signature — but n_distinct requires num_local_experts. Can we get it from the module? The wrapper wraps the module-level function `fused_topk`. We can derive num_local_experts from the max of topk_ids at record time — but max() causes a sync… upstream avoided sync. Alternative: record the n_distinct count using a seen buffer sized by topk_ids.max()+1? Sync required. Better: have the wrapper pass num_local_experts as a parameter with a fallback? We don't know how the fork's fused_topk signature looks. This repo patches the engine fork; the instruments task only ships the three modules and tests. The wrapper should be defensive: wrap `fused_topk`, call orig, then record from the returned topk_ids. Actually, the upstream signature is (topk_ids, topk_weights, num_local_experts, ...) → returns routing data. New target: fused_topk(hidden_states, gating_output, topk, renormalize) → (topk_weights, topk_ids).\n\nRecording needs num_local_experts for the size of the seen buffer. Options: make num_local_experts optional; if unknown, derive from the max of topk_ids — but that's a sync. To keep the no-sync discipline, we can size the seen buffer lazily from topk_ids.max()+1… also a sync.\n\nAlternative: pass num_local_experts via env? Hmm. Actually, looking at how flashnext wires it up: the module's install() wraps router/fused_topk_router.py's fused_topk. The wrapper signature should be flexible: def wrapped(*args, **kw): res = orig(*args, **kw); then find topk_ids inside res. In _record(topk_ids, num_local_experts), derive num_local_experts = int(topk_ids.max())+1? That's a sync, violating the discipline.\n\nBetter approach: keep a module-level _N_LOCAL_EXPERTS, configurable via env FN_EU_EXPERTS, default something like 512 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next's expert count). Wait — the delivered behavior doesn't mention such a variable. Task goal: \"env FN_EXPERT_UNION and FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT\". Only those four.\n\nHmm, but we can derive num_local_experts without a sync: allocate the seen buffer at max possible? Can't know without a sync.\n\nOptions: wrap at install time and read num_local_experts from the router instance? fused_topk is a module-level function called from _compute_routing(self, ...) — self is the FusedTopKRouter, which knows num_experts… but wrapping the plain function can't access self.\n\nPragmatic solution consistent with the no-sync discipline: grow the seen buffer as needed: track observed max on device? Comparisons still require sync.\n\nActually the simplest: lazily allocate seen sized num_local_experts+1. num_local_experts = max(topk_ids.max()+1, previous buffer size)? topk_ids.max() triggers a D2H sync — ~46 times per step only when the instrument is enabled… upstream explicitly avoided this. But upstream had num_local_experts passed in.\n\nAlternative: size the seen buffer from topk_ids' dtype range? No.\n\nCan I check the fork? The repo's patches/ directory might contain the engine fork's patches. Let me check whether this repo's patches/ has anything touching fused_topk_router, or whether fn_expert_union is wired into the engine somewhere. Grep for fn_expert_union / _maybe_expert_union in the repo.\n\nActually, wait — the fork is github.com/mecattaf/vllm branch flashnext, mirrored as commits, patches/ holds patches. Let me search the repo for \"fn_expert_union\" or \"expert_union\" or \"make_routing_data\" or \"fused_topk\" to see how it's wired.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me check how the fork wires these instruments, and look at the existing test style.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5efe05f16250474cb6a8da10","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments && grep -rn \"fn_expert_union\\|fn_synctrace\\|fn_offload_batch\\|FN_PROFILE\\|FN_EXPERT_UNION\\|expert_union\" patches/ specs/flashnext/spec.md IMPORTS.md handoff/ 2>/dev/null | grep -v Binary | head -40; echo ---; git ls-files container/rootfs tests/ | head"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_0ae64714a42d407285e3f41c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments && sed -n '1,60p' tests/test_repo_invariants.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1881,"output":2142,"cacheRead":34816,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1908,"totalTokens":38839,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988175422,"responseId":"chatcmpl-283acb81-9f77-41e6-baf1-ec3bffd8b234","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5efe05f16250474cb6a8da10","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"IMPORTS.md:61:| [AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm](https://github.com/AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm) @ `a8f620d` | Apache-2.0 | Patch-overlay discipline (MANIFEST + verify + 12 packaging invariants, extended); host orchestration shape (husk-reaping, ray pool caps, 2-GPU gate, ExecStopPost); env doctrine (PYTHONHASHSEED=0, expandable_segments, HSA_ENABLE_INTERRUPT=1, caches off tmpfs, ray env-prefix propagation); instruments `ds4_synctrace.py`/`ds4_expert_union.py`/`ds4_offload_batch.py` → adapted as `fn_*` with notices | copy + adapt |\nhandoff/ROUTING.md:35:| instruments | qwen | default ladder; overseer spot-reads `fn_expert_union.py` post-merge |\n---\ncontainer/rootfs/.keep\ntests/test_repo_invariants.py\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988223918},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0ae64714a42d407285e3f41c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Repo packaging invariants — the offline half of the discipline.\n\nModeled on ds4-vllm's test_patchset_packaging.py (Apache-2.0), extended:\nnew-file line counts are audited too (the upstream suite skipped them and\n3 of its 12 MANIFEST counts drifted).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n\nclass RepoInvariants(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_license_is_apache2(self):\n        text = (ROOT / \"LICENSE\").read_text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Apache License\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Version 2.0\", text)\n\n    def test_no_gpl_text_in_tree(self):\n        needle = \"GNU GENERAL \" + \"PUBLIC LICENSE\"  # avoid self-match\n        for path in ROOT.rglob(\"*\"):\n            if path.is_dir() or \".git\" in path.parts \\\n                    or \"__pycache__\" in path.parts:\n                continue\n            # Evidence dossiers may QUOTE license headers they inspected.\n            if \"evidence\" in path.parts or path.name == \"test_repo_invariants.py\":\n                continue\n            if path.suffix in {\".safetensors\", \".gguf\"}:\n                continue\n            try:\n                text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            self.assertNotIn(needle, text, f\"GPL text found in {path}\")\n\n    def test_no_secret_material(self):\n        patterns = [re.compile(p) for p in\n                    (r\"BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY\", r\"hf_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}\",\n                     r\"ghp_[A-Za-z0-9]{30,}\", r\"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\")]\n        for path in ROOT.rglob(\"*\"):\n            if path.is_dir() or \".git\" in path.parts \\\n                    or \"__pycache__\" in path.parts:\n                continue\n            try:\n                text = path.read_text(errors=\"ignore\")\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n            for pat in patterns:\n                self.assertIsNone(pat.search(text),\n                                  f\"secret-like material in {path}: {pat.pattern}\")\n\n    def test_spec_artifacts_exist(self):\n        self.assertTrue((ROOT / \"specs/flashnext/spec.md\").is_file())\n        trace = json.loads((ROOT / \"specs/flashnext/trace.json\").read_text())\n        self.assertEqual(trace[\"schemaVersion\"], 1)\n        self.assertTrue(\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988223918},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good context. test_repo_invariants.py says \"modeled on ds4-vllm's test_patchset_packaging.py (Apache-2.0)\". In other words, this repo has an established convention for attribution in docstrings.\n\nNext, let's check the engine fork and understand the wiring of fn_expert_union. The fork is mecattaf/vllm branch flashnext. Is there a local checkout? Let's check ~/mecattaf. Actually, this worktree is a worktree of /home/tom/mecattaf/flashnext. Let's check if the vllm fork checkout exists locally, and whether the wrapper for fn_expert_union is wired in there (for example, a call to fn_expert_union.install() somewhere inside the fork). Let's try grepping.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_57312f396cd1494eab550a0f","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls /home/tom/mecattaf/ 2>/dev/null; grep -rn \"fn_expert_union\\|fn_synctrace\\|fn_offload_batch\" /home/tom/mecattaf/vllm 2>/dev/null | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":3797,"output":253,"cacheRead":35840,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":166,"totalTokens":39890,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988223923,"responseId":"chatcmpl-be81877c-b51a-46cf-9301-9295353367dd","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_57312f396cd1494eab550a0f","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"blog\ncrm\ndotfiles\nflashnext\ninvestor-crm\nnotes\npage-demo\npage-template\nsodimo-auto-email\nsodimo-crm\nsodimo-handbook\nsodimo-os\ntally.nix\nworker-salvage-2026-08-28\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988232735},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No local vllm fork checkout. Therefore, the instrument module has to be self-contained and defensive at install time: lazy import of `vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.router.fused_topk_router`, wrap `fused_topk`.\n\nSignature of stock vLLM's fused_topk (from vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py):\n\n```python\ndef fused_topk(\n    hidden_states: torch.Tensor,\n    gating_output: torch.Tensor,\n    topk: int,\n    renormalize: bool,\n) -> tuple[torch.Tensor, torch.Tensor]:\n    ...\n    return topk_weights, topk_ids\n```\n\nWrapper: call orig, then record(topk_ids). _record needs num_local_experts to size the `seen` buffer. Options:\n\n1. Make `_record(topk_ids)` size `seen` from a module-level `_n_local` estimate that grows without sync: use `torch.zeros(n+1)`, but if ids >= n+1… hmm.\n\nActually there's a clean device-only trick: `seen = torch.zeros(k, bool)` with k being the guess. If topk_ids exceeds k, out of range. To avoid both sync and wrong-size: size the seen buffer to `gating_output.shape[-1]` if the wrapper can see it — gating_output is the router logits of shape [M, num_local_experts]! That's exactly num_local_experts, available at wrap time as a tensor shape with zero sync (shapes are host metadata).\n\nSo the wrapper signature is wrapped(hidden_states, gating_output, topk, renormalize, *a, **kw) — get num_local_experts = gating_output.shape[-1]. But be defensive: if someone calls with a different arg order / kwargs, fall back. Handle positional or keyword 'gating_output', fall back to num_local_experts=None, and inside _record, skip recording if num_local_experts is None? Upstream recorded n_local_experts in the buffer. If unknown, we can use a placeholder, but... better: record with num_local_experts derived from shape, and skip if not obtainable.\n\nAlso, the topk_ids returned by fused_topk: for padding rows, may contain -1? Stock fused_topk returns topk_ids with -1 padding when num_tokens is padded? For the rocm_aiter path there may be padding. Keep slot-0 absorption trick (ids + 1).\n\nNext, FN_ kill switch and defaults: FN_EXPERT_UNION unset ⇒ off. install() is no-op when disabled. But who calls install()? Upstream: lazy install from decode path via _maybe_expert_union inside ds4_tl_indexer. In flashnext, handoff/ROUTING.md says \"overseer does spot check reading of fn_expert_union.py after merge\". There's no ds4_tl_indexer here; flashnext instruments will probably be driven by the engine fork patch (a separate task). For this task, make install() idempotent and callable, and also self-check env at install time (like upstream: install() returns if not _ENABLED). Keep atexit flush.\n\nAlso \"FN_PROFILE window\" for synctrace: upstream's docstring says driven from ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile, shares DS4_PROFILE window, no dedicated env var. Adapted version: driven from the FN_PROFILE window, no dedicated env var. Module itself: install/uninstall/reset/report. Keep the interface identical.\n\nNote the FN_ prefix: replace DS4_PROFILE reference with FN_PROFILE.\n\noffload batch: rename FRAC_ENV → \"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\", PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV → \"FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\". Keep defaults 0.25 / 0.5, and keep torch-free too.\n\nNotice header requirement: acceptance criterion greps for files with `grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l == 3`. So each file must contain the string \"Adapted from\" naming the upstream file and license. Example:\n\n```\n# Adapted from ds4_synctrace.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_synctrace.py),\n# Apache-2.0 licensed. Adaptations: DS4_ env prefix -> FN_, docstring re-targets.\n```\n\nAlso \"notice header travels with every adapted module\" — put it at the top (before or inside the docstring). The upstream offload_batch has an SPDX line followed by the docstring. I'll do this:\n\n```python\n# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ...\n```\n\nFor synctrace/expert_union (no SPDX upstream), add notice comment above the docstring.\n\nNext, the tests: tests/test_instruments.py\n\nRequirements:\n1. py_compile passes on each module (cfile to tempdir, following upstream discipline).\n2. Each module has the notice header (contains \"Adapted from\", names upstream file and Apache-2.0).\n3. fn_offload_batch's budget arithmetic matches reference invariants:\n   - Floor at max group size: resolve_store_batch_tokens(...) >= max(sizes).\n   - Promote counted in blocks: resolve_promote_block_budget returns int(num_blocks * frac) clamped; independent of token/block size (e.g., 2 groups with very different sizes give the same block budget).\n   - Also frac<=0 → None; num_blocks None/0 → None (reference invariant: stock fallback).\n\nTests import fn_offload_batch from container/rootfs via importlib, without torch. But wait — py_compile of fn_synctrace/expert_union: py_compile doesn't need torch. But if tests import those modules, they'd need torch. Per the task, tests should only verify py_compile + notice for synctrace/expert_union, and the arithmetic (via import) only for fn_offload_batch. Good — fn_offload_batch only imports os.\n\nImport method: importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_offload_batch\", ROOT/\"container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py\"). Deterministic.\n\nAlso test that env names are the FN_ ones: module's FRAC_ENV == \"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\" etc. This pins the rename. And the expert union module — should we check env names without importing (torch)? We can grep file text: contains FN_EXPERT_UNION etc. Good idea: text-level checks for env prefix + kill-switch default off.\n\nLet me verify budget arithmetic matches upstream exactly — just rename and adapt:\n\n_budget: same formula. Test invariants:\n- floor: with num_blocks=256, sizes=(128, 16) [sliding-window style], frac=0.25: budget_blocks = 64; keys_per_token = 1/128 + 1/16 = 0.0703125; budget_tokens = int(64/0.0703125) = 910.22→ int → 910? 64/0.0703125 = 910.222..., int → 910. max(910, 128) = 910 ≥ max(sizes). Also a case where the floor bites: tiny frac: frac=0.001, num_blocks=256 → budget_blocks = max(1, int(0.256)) = 1; budget_tokens = int(1/0.0703125)=14; floor → max(14,128)=128 = max(sizes). Assert equality.\n- promote: resolve_promote_block_budget(258, frac=0.5) == 129; independent of block size (only num_blocks and frac); frac=0 → None; num_blocks=0 → None.\n\nTest reading from env too? _read_frac uses os.getenv at call time — set env var via unittest.mock.patch.dict or os.environ and restore. Keep it simple: pass frac explicitly + one env test via env patching.\n\nStyle: match test_repo_invariants.py — pathlib, ROOT constant, unittest.\n\nThen, adapt the three modules.\n\n### fn_synctrace.py\n\nAdaptation points:\n- Notice header.\n- Docstring: change DS4_PROFILE → FN_PROFILE; change \"Driven from ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile\" → driven from the flashnext FN_PROFILE window caller. But watch the frame key split: upstream uses `f.f_code.co_filename.split('site-packages/')[-1]` — in flashnext's container, the instrument lands in /opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages (Containerfile line 117), so keep 'site-packages/'.\n- Keep the limitations paragraph.\n- The 2026-08-07 profile numbers in the docstring are ds4-specific measurements; adapt honestly: keep mechanism rationale but attribute to upstream. Write adapted docstring: state that it's an adapted copy, keep the design rationale (~25 events per step), note the upstream profiling context. Acceptance requires only \"Adapted from\" + compile + tests, but for honesty: don't claim flashnext measurements as its own. Retain upstream rationale while explicitly labeling it upstream.\n\nActually, the simpler and safest approach: preserve upstream docstring body nearly verbatim (it's Apache-2.0, notice retained), change DS4→FN references, remove specific references to ds4_tl_indexer, replace with \"the flashnext FN_PROFILE window driver\". The ~3,200 ops / 94% CPU numbers are upstream measurements — fine to keep as rationale in an adapted copy, they're comments.\n\nUpstream docstring says \"Driven from ds4_tl_indexer._maybe_profile so it shares the DS4_PROFILE window (no new env var, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\" Adapted version: \"Driven from the FN_PROFILE window (no new env var, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\" — flashnext also uses ray TP. Fine.\n\n### fn_offload_batch.py\n\nRename only + notice. Docstring references vLLM internals — keep. Env names: FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC, FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC. Keep DEFAULT_FRAC/DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC and the comment (mentions DS4 measurements — keep as upstream rationale; may add \"measured upstream on ds4-vllm\"). The comment \"Measured on a 4,645-token prompt against a 258-block tier\" is an upstream measurement — keep as is, it's a comment on an adapted file with notice.\n\n### fn_expert_union.py\n\nAdaptation points:\n- Notice header: Adapted from ds4_expert_union.py; re-target the wrap from gpt_oss make_routing_data to stock fused-mixture router entry fused_topk (vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py), per specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4.\n- Env: FN_EXPERT_UNION, FN_EU_START (200), FN_EU_CALLS (2000), FN_EU_OUT (~/vllm-prof).\n- install(): import vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.router.fused_topk_router as m; orig = m.fused_topk; wrapped(hidden_states, gating_output, topk, renormalize, *a, **kw): call orig first? or record first? Recording needs topk_ids, which fused_topk computes. So call orig, then record from result, then return result. But failure path: try record, except pass.\n\nUpstream's make_routing_data wrapper recorded from input topk_ids. Here record from output. Return value: topk_weights, topk_ids (tuple). Defensive: if result is a tuple with 2+ elements, topk_ids = result[1].\n\nnum_local_experts: from gating_output.shape[-1] (host metadata, no sync). Wrapped signature should also handle kwargs. Write like:\n\n```python\ndef wrapped(*a, **kw):\n    res = orig(*a, **kw)\n    try:\n        gating = kw.get(\"gating_output\", a[1] if len(a) > 1 else None)\n        n_local = gating.shape[-1] if gating is not None and gating.dim() >= 1 else None\n        topk_ids = res[1] if isinstance(res, tuple) and len(res) >= 2 else None\n        if topk_ids is not None:\n            _record(topk_ids, n_local)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return res\n```\n\n_record(topk_ids, num_local_experts): if num_local_experts is None, fall back to... skip recording? Slot-0 trick needs buffer of size n_local+1. If n_local is None, skip (or derive from ids.max()+1 — sync — no). Skip with counter? Keep it simple: if n_local is None: return. Hmm, but that could silently record nothing. In FusedTopKRouter, gating_output is always the router logits [M, E]. Fine.\n\nKeep the no-sync discipline comments, the two-stage gate, swallowing failures, atexit flush, TSV output `expert_union_<pid>.tsv` (maybe `fn_expert_union_<pid>.tsv`; keep as upstream name? adapt prefix: \"fn_expert_union\" print messages). Print tag \"[fn_expert_union]\".\n\nAlso default off: _ENABLED = FN_EXPERT_UNION == \"1\"; install() returns if not enabled. Two-stage gate note: caller may also check. Keep lazy install rationale: wrap at install() time — explain that install is lazy because the MoE layers are built by the first decode.\n\nAlso upstream's `wrapped._ds4_orig = orig` → `wrapped._fn_orig = orig`.\n\nEnv defaults: FN_EU_OUT default \"~/vllm-prof\" — keep.\n\nOne more consideration: acceptance criterion also runs `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v` from the repo root. tests package: does tests/ have __init__.py? `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments` requires tests to be a package, or works via unittest's namespace? `tests.test_instruments` requires tests to be importable — without __init__.py, does python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments work? unittest uses importlib; since Python 3.11+, namespace packages work for `tests.test_instruments` if cwd is on sys.path. Actually `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments` converts to a module path and imports — namespace packages are fine (does the repo have tests/__init__.py? ls shows only test_repo_invariants.py). And existing harness presumably runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`. To be safe, my tests should not depend on being imported as package (use ROOT-relative pathlib). Should I add __init__.py? The boundary says only touch container/rootfs/ and tests/ — adding tests/__init__.py is allowed but changes repo structure; `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments` on py3.11+: namespace package import works. Let me verify with python version in sandbox: python3 --version. Then run acceptance command to verify.\n\nEnvironment: does sandbox have python3? Probably. torch not needed.\n\nAlso verify: does this repo's CI run flake/style? Not mentioned. Style reference receipts-verify.py: plain stdlib, docstring header, type hints in some places.\n\nOK let me write the files.\n\nOne more check: \"All paths touched by any task commit … must remain inside conflictDomains\" — my commit adds container/rootfs/fn_*.py and tests/test_instruments.py. Fine. Don't touch container/rootfs/.keep.\n\nLet me write fn_synctrace.py:\n\n```python\n# Adapted from ds4_synctrace.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_synctrace.py),\n# Apache-2.0 licensed; DS4_ env surface renamed to FN_ and the profile-window\n# driver re-targeted to flashnext. Upstream notice retained below.\n\"\"\"Attribute blocking device->host syncs to python call sites.\n\n...adapted docstring...\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nHmm: \"notice header travels\" — header comment at top is enough.\n\nFor the docstring, adapt:\n\n```\n\"\"\"Attribute blocking device->host syncs to python call sites.\n\nAdapted from ds4_synctrace.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d (Apache-2.0).\nUpstream measured hipMemcpyWithStream at 42% of decode self-CPU and\nhipStreamSynchronize at 16% in its 2026-08-07 profile; ...\n```\n\nWeave the \"Adapted from\" line into both the header comment and the docstring? A single location is sufficient for grep. Put the notice as the first lines of the docstring, and/or as a comment. Upstream offload_batch puts SPDX first, then docstring. I'll do:\n\n```python\n# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ds4_synctrace.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d,\n# Apache License 2.0. Changes: DS4_ prefix -> FN_, ...\n```\n\nFor consistency, SPDX + Adapted-from header comment in all three files, plus mention in docstring.\n\nWait — one nuance: original upstream files ds4_synctrace.py and ds4_expert_union.py didn't have SPDX lines, only offload_batch did. Adding SPDX to adapted copies is fine.\n\nOK, now let me write the three files.\n\nfn_synctrace.py contents — adapt the body: keep everything, replace docstring DS4 references. Frame key split 'site-packages/' — keep (instrument lands in site-packages inside the image).\n\nfn_expert_union.py — write carefully.\n\n```python\n# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ds4_expert_union.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (Apache License 2.0). Adaptations:\n#   - DS4_ env prefix -> FN_ (kill switch FN_EXPERT_UNION, default off)\n#   - the wrap is RE-TARGETED: upstream wrapped\n#     vllm...fused_moe.experts.gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data,\n#     a routing entry the flashnext workload never calls\n#     (specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4). This wraps the stock\n#     fused-mixture router entry fused_topk in\n#     vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py.\n\"\"\"FN_EXPERT_UNION=1: measure how many DISTINCT experts a decode step touches.\n\n...\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nDocstring: adapt upstream's rationale. Qwen4-Flash-Next top_k is? Don't fabricate numbers like \"6-per-token / ~34 experts / K=6\" — those are DS4-specific. Rewrite the rationale generically: the decode roof is dominated by routed-expert bytes, which scale with the union of experts the step's positions select, not with top-k per token; correlated routing shrinks the union; nothing static can settle it — it has to be measured against real traffic. This is faithful and generic.\n\nBody:\n\n```python\nimport atexit\nimport os\n\nimport torch\n\n_ENABLED = os.environ.get(\"FN_EXPERT_UNION\") == \"1\"\n_START = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_EU_START\", \"200\"))\n_CALLS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_EU_CALLS\", \"2000\"))\n_OUT = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get(\"FN_EU_OUT\", \"~/vllm-prof\"))\n```\n\n_record(topk_ids, num_local_experts): similar to upstream, but `if num_local_experts is None: return` guard… wait, upstream signature was _record(topk_ids, num_local_experts). Keep it, add guard.\n\nActually note: `seen[ids + 1] = True` requires ids >= -1. ids may be uint? fused_topk returns int32/int64 topk_ids. .long() conversion handles that.\n\nWait, subtle: -1 padding absorption: seen has size n_local+1; ids are in range [-1, n_local-1]; ids+1 → [0, n_local]. OK.\n\ndef install():\n\n```python\ndef install():\n    \"\"\"Idempotently wrap fused_topk. Safe to call more than once.\"\"\"\n    global _installed\n    if not _ENABLED or _installed:\n        return\n    try:\n        from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.router import (\n            fused_topk_router as m,\n        )\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"[fn_expert_union] not installed: {exc}\", flush=True)\n        return\n\n    orig = m.fused_topk\n\n    def wrapped(*a, **kw):\n        res = orig(*a, **kw)\n        try:\n            gating = kw.get(\"gating_output\")\n            if gating is None and len(a) > 1:\n                gating = a[1]\n            topk_ids = res[1] if isinstance(res, tuple) and len(res) >= 2 else None\n            n_local = gating.shape[-1] if topk_ids is not None and gating is not None else None\n            if topk_ids is not None and n_local:\n                _record(topk_ids, n_local)\n        except Exception:\n            pass  # never let the probe break routing\n        return res\n\n    wrapped._fn_orig = orig\n    m.fused_topk = wrapped\n    _installed = True\n    atexit.register(_flush)\n    print(...)\n```\n\nNote: FusedTopKRouter._compute_routing calls module-level fused_topk — if it references via module global, re-binding m.fused_topk works. If the router function calls fused_topk as a same-module global, re-binding the module attribute works. Good.\n\nAdd docstring note about the lazy-install rationale: adapted from upstream — \"by the first decode the MoE layers are long since built; import-time wrapping from an instrument load would risk circular imports\". Keep the two-stage gate note too.\n\n_flush: file name `expert_union_<pid>.tsv` — keep? For clarity of provenance use `fn_expert_union_<pid>.tsv`. Hmm, the upstream analysis tool host/bench/expert_union.py reads expert_union_*.tsv; flashnext's overseer \"spot check reads fn_expert_union.py\". Use `expert_union_<pid>.tsv` for drop-in compatibility? Analysis tool unknown; keep upstream name (TSV header same too). Print \"[fn_expert_union] wrote ...\".\n\nfn_offload_batch.py: rename only + notice. FRAC_ENV = \"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\", PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV = \"FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\". Docstring mentions `$DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC` → `$FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC`, `DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC=0` → `FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC=0`. Keep measurements in comments (those are upstream measurements — with notice header, retainable; add \"(measured upstream)\" clarification? Comments are fine as-is).\n\nNext, tests/test_instruments.py:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Instrument overlay tests — compile, notices, and budget invariants.\n\nThe offline half for container/rootfs/fn_*.py: py_compile each module,\ncheck every adapted module carries its upstream notice, and check the\nfn_offload_batch budget arithmetic against the reference invariants\n(floor at the max group size; promote counted in blocks). fn_offload_batch\nis torch-free by design, so that module is imported and exercised directly.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport pathlib\nimport py_compile\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nROOTFS = ROOT / \"container\" / \"rootfs\"\nMODULES = (\"fn_synctrace.py\", \"fn_offload_batch.py\", \"fn_expert_union.py\")\n\n\ndef _load_offload_batch():\n    path = ROOTFS / \"fn_offload_batch.py\"\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_offload_batch\", path)\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n    return mod\n\n\nclass InstrumentPackaging(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_modules_compile(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:\n            for name in MODULES:\n                path = ROOTFS / name\n                self.assertTrue(path.is_file(), f\"{path} missing\")\n                py_compile.compile(str(path), cfile=f\"{td}/{name}c\", doraise=True)\n\n    def test_notice_headers(self):\n        for name in MODULES:\n            text = (ROOTFS / name).read_text()\n            self.assertIn(\"Adapted from\", text, name)\n            self.assertIn(\"ds4-vllm\", text, name)\n            self.assertIn(\"Apache\", text, name)\n            upstream = \"ds4_\" + name[len(\"fn_\"):]\n            self.assertIn(upstream, text, f\"{name} must name {upstream}\")\n\n    def test_env_prefix_is_fn(self):\n        ... text checks: fn_expert_union.py contains FN_EXPERT_UNION, FN_EU_START, FN_EU_CALLS, FN_EU_OUT and no \"DS4_\" token; same for synctrace (FN_PROFILE); offload: FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC/FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC.\n```\n\nWait: careful — the notice header itself contains \"ds4\" (upstream file names). \"No DS4_ token\" check: notice mentions ds4_synctrace.py (no trailing underscore? \"ds4_\" + suffix — \"ds4_synctrace.py\" contains \"ds4_\"!). So assert \"DS4_\" not in text.upper()? That would match the \"DS4_SYNCTRACE.PY\" from the notice. Instead, check that specific env-var names aren't present: \"DS4_PROFILE\", \"DS4_EXPERT_UNION\", \"DS4_EU_\", \"DS4_OFFLOAD_\". These strings won't appear in the notice text (file names are ds4_synctrace.py etc.). Good.\n\nBudget arithmetic tests:\n\n```python\nclass OffloadBudgetInvariants(unittest.TestCase):\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        cls.mod = _load_offload_batch()\n\n    def test_store_floor_is_max_group_size(self):\n        m = self.mod\n        # tiny frac so the raw token budget lands under the coarsest block\n        budget = m.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16), frac=0.001)\n        self.assertEqual(budget, 128)  # floor bites exactly at max(sizes)\n\n    def test_store_budget_scales_with_frac(self):\n        m = self.mod\n        # frac 0.25 of 256 blocks = 64 blocks; rates 1/128 + 1/16 keys/token\n        self.assertEqual(m.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16), frac=0.25), 910)\n```\n\nLet me double-check: budget_blocks = max(1, int(256*0.25)) = 64. keys_per_token = 1/128 + 1/16 = 0.0078125 + 0.0625 = 0.0703125. 64 / 0.0703125 = 910.2222..., int → 910. Floor max(910, 128) = 910. ✓\n\nfrac=0.001: budget_blocks = max(1, int(0.256)) = 1; 1/0.0703125 = 14.222 → 14; max(14,128)=128 ✓ floor equals max group size.\n\n    def test_store_disabled_paths_return_none(self):\n        frac<=0 → None; num_blocks None/0 → None; empty sizes → None.\n\n    def test_promote_counted_in_blocks(self):\n        m = self.mod\n        b = m.resolve_promote_block_budget(258, frac=0.5)\n        self.assertEqual(b, 129)\n        # Block-counted: the result depends on num_blocks and frac only --\n        # group sizes do not enter the signature at all.\n        # Also invariant: never more than the tier, at least 1.\n        self.assertEqual(m.resolve_promote_block_budget(258, frac=2.0), 258)\n        self.assertEqual(m.resolve_promote_block_budget(1, frac=0.5), 1)\n        self.assertIsNone(m.resolve_promote_block_budget(258, frac=0))\n        self.assertIsNone(m.resolve_promote_block_budget(0))\n        self.assertIsNone(m.resolve_promote_block_budget(None))\n\n    def test_env_var_names(self):\n        m = self.mod\n        self.assertEqual(m.FRAC_ENV, \"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\")\n        self.assertEqual(m.PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV, \"FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\")\n        self.assertEqual(m.DEFAULT_FRAC, 0.25)\n        self.assertEqual(m.DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC, 0.5)\n\n    def test_env_overrides_frac(self):\n        with unittest.mock.patch.dict(os.environ, {m.FRAC_ENV: \"0.5\"}):\n            budget = m.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16))\n        expected: budget_blocks = int(256*0.5) = 128; 128/0.0703125 = 1820.44 → 1820. Assert 1820.\n```\n\nNote: frac parameter defaults to None → reads env. ✓\n\nAlso kill-switch default-off test for expert union + synctrace at text level:\n- fn_expert_union: `os.environ.get(\"FN_EXPERT_UNION\") == \"1\"` (default off).\n- Text check: contains 'FN_EXPERT_UNION\") == \"1\"'? Fragile to formatting. Instead, just check FN_EXPERT_UNION present and FN_EU_START/FN_EU_CALLS/FN_EU_OUT present.\n\nAnd \"default off\": fn_synctrace has no env var, install is only via explicit call — text check that it does not auto-install at import: assert \"install()\" appears but not called at module top-level... skip; too fragile. Stick to spec: py_compile, notices, budget invariants. Adding env pinning tests because they are the deliverable of the rename (\"rename to FN_ env prefix\").\n\nNow let me write everything. Also run acceptance commands before committing.\n\nOne more point on the fn_expert_union docstring's cost line: upstream claimed \"~4 extra small kernel launches per MoE call\". Our _record does: reshape/long, zeros, index-set, three scalar assignments — similar. Retain the adapted cost note, roughly: \"~4 small extra kernel launches per routing call; off unless FN_EXPERT_UNION=1.\"\n\nAlso delete upstream's \"Analyse the dump with host/bench/expert_union.py\"? flashnext doesn't have that file. Rephrase: \"Dump is a TSV: one row per recorded routing call.\" Fine.\n\nAlso note in the module docstring: why fused_topk: the flashnext workload routes through FusedTopKRouter → fused_topk (qsa-53896.md §4); upstream's make_routing_data target is gpt-oss triton_kernels path this workload doesn't hit.\n\nnum_local_experts from gating_output.shape[-1]: in FusedTopKRouter._compute_routing, fused_topk(hidden_states, router_logits, top_k, renormalize) — router_logits shape [num_tokens, num_experts].\n\nEdge case: some vLLM versions' fused_topk signature is (hidden_states, gating_output, topk, renormalize). The wrapper uses *a, **kw and only peeks at a[1]/kw[\"gating_output\"]; if different, n_local is None → skip record, never crash. Good.\n\nNow let me write the files. Line lengths modest.\n\nFull fn_synctrace.py:\n\n```python\n# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ds4_synctrace.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_synctrace.py),\n# Apache License 2.0. Changes: DS4_ env surface renamed to FN_; the module is\n# driven from the flashnext FN_PROFILE window instead of ds4_tl_indexer.\n\"\"\"Attribute blocking device->host syncs to python call sites.\n\nThe upstream motivation (measured on ds4-vllm's 2026-08-07 profile):\nhipMemcpyWithStream at 42% of decode self-CPU and hipStreamSynchronize at\n16% -- together the dominant cost once kernel launches are down. But\n`hipMemcpyWithStream` in a profiler table is just a count; it does not say\nwhich line caused it.\n\n`with_stack=True` on the torch profiler answers that in principle and is\nunusable in practice here: it captures a python stack for every one of\n~3,200 ops per step, which pegged the worker at 94% CPU and stalled the\nengine on shm_broadcast.\n\nThis is the cheap alternative. It wraps only the handful of Tensor methods\nthat can force a blocking D2H, and records one `sys._getframe` per call --\n~25 events per step rather than ~3,200. Overhead is a dict increment on an\nalready-blocking operation, i.e. noise.\n\nLimitation worth knowing (retained from upstream): boolean-mask indexing\n(`x[mask]`) reaches nonzero() inside C++ `at::index`, not through the\npython method, so it is NOT counted here. Anything unattributed after this\nis a candidate for that.\n\nDriven from the flashnext FN_PROFILE window driver so it shares that\nwindow (no new env var of its own, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\nDefault off: nothing installs at import; install()/uninstall() bracket the\nwindow and are the only switches.\n\"\"\"\n```\n\nBody identical to upstream (names unchanged: install/uninstall/reset/report).\n\nfn_offload_batch.py: SPDX + notice + adapted docstring (rename the DS4 mention in the body? The docstring body mentions OffloadingConnectorScheduler etc. — keep). Internal references `$DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC` → `$FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC`, `DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC=0` → `FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC=0`.\n\nNote in the docstring \"This lives outside ``vllm`` so the budget arithmetic is unit-testable without importing torch...\" — keep.\n\nOK let me write the files. Then run acceptance commands, then commit.\n\nCommit message style — look at git log: \"container-recipe: Container recipe: pinned wheel set...\", \"receipts: weights staged...\", \"handoff: ...\". Tally probably has its own convention. Prefix \"instruments:\". Write like: \"instruments: Adapt the ds4-vllm engagement-proof instruments as fn_* overlay\".\n\nNow let me write the files.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need. The house conventions are clear (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md already declares exactly these three adapted files with retained notices). Now writing the three adapted modules.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_84fcd37b76fd4c998373ad68","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py","content":"# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ds4_synctrace.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_synctrace.py),\n# Apache License 2.0. Changes: DS4_ surface renamed to FN_; the module is\n# driven from the flashnext FN_PROFILE window instead of ds4_tl_indexer.\n\"\"\"Attribute blocking device->host syncs to python call sites.\n\nThe upstream motivation (measured on ds4-vllm's 2026-08-07 profile):\nhipMemcpyWithStream at 42% of decode self-CPU and hipStreamSynchronize at\n16% -- together the dominant cost, once kernel launches are down. But\n`hipMemcpyWithStream` in a profiler table is just a count; it does not say\nwhich line caused it.\n\n`with_stack=True` on the torch profiler answers that in principle and is\nunusable in practice here: it captures a python stack for every one of\n~3,200 ops per step, which pegged the worker at 94% CPU and stalled the\nengine on shm_broadcast.\n\nThis is the cheap alternative. It wraps only the handful of Tensor methods\nthat can force a blocking D2H, and records one `sys._getframe` per call --\n~25 events per step rather than ~3,200. Overhead is a dict increment on an\nalready-blocking operation, i.e. noise.\n\nLimitation worth knowing (retained from upstream): boolean-mask indexing\n(`x[mask]`) reaches nonzero() inside C++ `at::index`, not through the\npython method, so it is NOT counted here. Anything unattributed after this\nis a candidate for that.\n\nDriven from the flashnext FN_PROFILE window driver so it shares that\nwindow (no new env var of its own, hence no ray restart to propagate one).\nDefault off: nothing installs at import; install()/uninstall() bracket the\nwindow and are the only switches.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport collections\nimport sys\n\nimport torch\n\n_counts = collections.Counter()\n_installed = False\n_orig = {}\n# Tensor methods that block on a device->host transfer.\n_TARGETS = (\"item\", \"tolist\", \"cpu\", \"numpy\", \"nonzero\", \"__float__\", \"__int__\")\n\n\ndef _wrap(name):\n    orig = getattr(torch.Tensor, name)\n\n    def wrapper(self, *a, **kw):\n        try:\n            f = sys._getframe(1)\n            _counts[f\"{f.f_code.co_filename.split('site-packages/')[-1]}:\"\n                    f\"{f.f_lineno} {f.f_code.co_name}() [{name}]\"] += 1\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        return orig(self, *a, **kw)\n\n    _orig[name] = orig\n    setattr(torch.Tensor, name, wrapper)\n\n\ndef install():\n    global _installed\n    if _installed:\n        return\n    for n in _TARGETS:\n        try:\n            _wrap(n)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    _installed = True\n\n\ndef uninstall():\n    global _installed\n    for n, o in _orig.items():\n        try:\n            setattr(torch.Tensor, n, o)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    _orig.clear()\n    _installed = False\n\n\ndef reset():\n    _counts.clear()\n\n\ndef report(steps=1.0):\n    \"\"\"Formatted table, per-decode-step, most frequent first.\"\"\"\n    if not _counts:\n        return (\"### BLOCKING-SYNC ATTRIBUTION ###\\n  (no events -- either the \"\n                \"tracer never installed, or every sync is bool-mask indexing / \"\n                \"C++-internal and invisible to a python hook)\\n\\n\")\n    total = sum(_counts.values())\n    out = [f\"### BLOCKING-SYNC ATTRIBUTION ({total} events over {steps:.2f} \"\n           f\"decode steps = {total / max(steps, 1e-9):.1f}/step) ###\"]\n    for site, n in _counts.most_common(30):\n        out.append(f\"  {n / max(steps, 1e-9):7.1f}/step  ({n:5d})  {site}\")\n    out.append(\"\")\n    return \"\\n\".join(out) + \"\\n\\n\"\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1059,"output":8986,"cacheRead":38912,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":7885,"totalTokens":48957,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988232741,"responseId":"chatcmpl-d68016cc-1bcc-4a42-8caf-22c4a50f3db4","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_84fcd37b76fd4c998373ad68","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 3520 bytes to /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/fn_synctrace.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988413709},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Understood. I will follow these instructions.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_b4a1a97b31b34f5bbd473563","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ds4_offload_batch.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_offload_batch.py),\n# Apache License 2.0. Changes: DS4_ env surface renamed to FN_\n# (FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC, FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC); arithmetic and\n# invariants unchanged from the reference.\n\"\"\"Store-batch budget for the KV offloading connector.\n\nWhy this exists\n---------------\n``OffloadingConnectorScheduler._build_store_jobs`` asks the offloading manager\nto stage every not-yet-offloaded block of a request in a single\n``prepare_store()`` call. That call is all-or-nothing: the CPU primary tier\nreturns ``None`` unless it can make room for *every* key at once, and the\ncaller's failure path logs ``cannot store blocks`` and ``continue``s **without\nadvancing** ``next_stored_block_idx``.\n\nSo a single refusal is not self-correcting. The next step recomputes the range\nfrom the same unadvanced cursor against a larger ``num_offloadable_tokens``,\nasks for strictly more than it just failed to get, and fails again. The ask\nratchets upward until the request is demanding its entire prefix in one call,\nwhich no small tier can ever satisfy. The observed symptom upstream — a 182K\nprefill against a 256 MiB tier refusing stores — reads like \"the tier must be\nsized to the in-flight sequence\", but the tier is a proper LRU cache with\nrefcounting: ``TieringOffloadingManager.complete_store`` pins a block via\n``primary.prepare_read()`` and ``_process_finished_jobs`` unpins it via\n``primary.complete_read()`` as soon as the secondary-tier write lands. Blocks\n*do* recycle. Nothing was bounding the ask.\n\nBounding it turns the primary tier into a streaming window: each step stages at\nmost a budget's worth of blocks, those drain to disk, their ref_cnt drops, and\nthe next step reuses the same slots. The tier then has to cover the drain\nlatency, not the sequence — which is what makes a disk cache affordable behind\na few hundred MiB of RAM.\n\nThis lives outside ``vllm`` so the budget arithmetic is unit-testable without\nimporting torch or the connector's dependency graph.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"resolve_store_batch_tokens\",\n    \"resolve_promote_block_budget\",\n    \"DEFAULT_FRAC\",\n    \"FRAC_ENV\",\n    \"DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC\",\n    \"PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV\",\n]\n\nFRAC_ENV = \"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\"\nPROMOTE_FRAC_ENV = \"FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\"\n\n# A quarter of the tier per step. The remaining three quarters absorb blocks\n# whose disk write is still in flight (ref_cnt > 0, so not evictable) plus the\n# resident prefix-cache entries the tier exists to serve.\nDEFAULT_FRAC = 0.25\n\n# Half the tier per request for reads. Promotion has the mirror-image failure\n# of the store ratchet, and it is worse because it wastes disk bandwidth before\n# failing: lookup() initiates one promotion per matched block with nothing\n# bounding the total, so a prefix longer than the primary tier evicts its own\n# earlier promotions to make room for later ones. The prefix is then never\n# wholly resident, _maximal_prefix_lookup never confirms it, and the request\n# recomputes everything anyway -- after paying the full disk read. Measured\n# upstream on a 4,645-token prompt against a 258-block tier: 258 blocks\n# (512 MiB) read from disk, \"cannot store blocks\", and zero hits.\n#\n# Capping the ask below the tier size means the promoted prefix stays resident,\n# so a partial hit is real work saved instead of thrash. The remainder is left\n# for in-flight stores, which share the same tier.\nDEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC = 0.5\n\n\ndef _read_frac(frac: float | None, env: str, default: float) -> float:\n    if frac is not None:\n        return frac\n    raw = os.getenv(env)\n    if raw is None or raw == \"\":\n        return default\n    try:\n        return float(raw)\n    except ValueError:\n        return default\n\n\ndef resolve_store_batch_tokens(\n    num_blocks: int | None,\n    offloaded_block_sizes: \"list[int] | tuple[int, ...]\",\n    frac: float | None = None,\n) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Token budget for one prepare_store() call, or None for unbounded.\n\n    Args:\n        num_blocks: Blocks in the CPU primary tier. None/0 (a spec that does\n            not expose it) disables bounding.\n        offloaded_block_sizes: ``offloaded_block_size`` of every KV group. One\n            token range yields one key per group, so the key count a token\n            budget produces is the sum of the per-group rates.\n        frac: Fraction of the tier to spend per step. Defaults to\n            ``$FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC`` then ``DEFAULT_FRAC``. A value\n            <= 0 disables bounding, restoring stock vLLM behaviour.\n\n    Returns:\n        Token budget, never smaller than one block of the coarsest group.\n\n        That floor is load-bearing, not a rounding nicety. Groups keep separate\n        cursors over a shared token position, so a budget measured from the\n        laggard group has to be wide enough to reach every group's existing\n        cursor; the gap is at most one block of the coarsest group. Below the\n        floor, some group's target would land under its own cursor, and\n        ``_build_store_jobs`` assigns ``next_stored_block_idx = num_blocks``\n        outright — it never takes a max — so the cursor would rewind and the\n        blocks in between would be skipped for good.\n    \"\"\"\n    return _budget(num_blocks, offloaded_block_sizes, frac, FRAC_ENV, DEFAULT_FRAC)\n\n\ndef resolve_promote_block_budget(\n    num_blocks: int | None, frac: float | None = None\n) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"Max blocks one request may promote, or None for unbounded.\n\n    Deliberately counted in **blocks, not tokens**. The token form of this\n    budget divides by the summed per-group key rate, which a sliding-window\n    group wrecks: its blocks are tiny and numerous (208 of them against 26 for\n    a full-attention group on the same 4,645 tokens, measured upstream), so it\n    dominates the rate and collapses the budget to a few hundred tokens --\n    about 6% of the prompt -- even though its lookup only ever touches a\n    bounded tail. Counting the promotions themselves needs no model of any of\n    that.\n\n    Applies to the full-attention prefix scan only; see the call site.\n    ``FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC=0`` restores stock behaviour (promote the whole\n    matched prefix, and thrash if it does not fit).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not num_blocks or num_blocks <= 0:\n        return None\n    frac = _read_frac(frac, PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV, DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC)\n    if frac <= 0:\n        return None\n    return max(1, int(num_blocks * min(frac, 1.0)))\n\n\ndef _budget(num_blocks, offloaded_block_sizes, frac, env, default):\n    if not num_blocks or num_blocks <= 0:\n        return None\n    sizes = [int(s) for s in offloaded_block_sizes if s and s > 0]\n    if not sizes:\n        return None\n\n    frac = _read_frac(frac, env, default)\n    if frac <= 0:\n        return None\n\n    budget_blocks = max(1, int(num_blocks * min(frac, 1.0)))\n    keys_per_token = sum(1.0 / s for s in sizes)\n    budget_tokens = int(budget_blocks / keys_per_token)\n\n    return max(budget_tokens, max(sizes))\n","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":9084,"output":1935,"cacheRead":39936,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":9,"totalTokens":50955,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988413715,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e125f7ad-679b-47c3-8bfd-3cea31015260","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b4a1a97b31b34f5bbd473563","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 7100 bytes to /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/fn_offload_batch.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988449440},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"From now on, it's an expert union module that has a wrap that has been re-targeted.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_58f5ba86bcf04b7fbeffb121","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n# Adapted from ds4_expert_union.py in AlexKGwyn/ds4-vllm @ a8f620d\n# (container/rootfs/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/ds4_expert_union.py),\n# Apache License 2.0. Changes:\n#   - DS4_ env surface renamed to FN_ (kill switch FN_EXPERT_UNION, default off).\n#   - The wrap is RE-TARGETED. Upstream wrapped the gpt-oss triton_kernels\n#     routing entry (gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data), which the\n#     flashnext workload never calls: it routes through the stock fused-mixture\n#     FusedTopKRouter instead (specs/flashnext/evidence/qsa-53896.md section 4).\n#     This wraps fused_topk in\n#     vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py.\n\"\"\"FN_EXPERT_UNION=1: measure how many DISTINCT experts a decode step touches.\n\nThe decode roof is dominated by routed-expert bytes, and those scale with the\n*union* of experts the step's positions select, not with top-k-per-token.\nIndependent routing pushes that union toward num_experts per layer; perfectly\ncorrelated routing keeps it at top-k. That spread moves the physics ceiling by\na large factor, and nothing static can settle it -- it has to be measured\nagainst real traffic.\n\nThis wraps ``fused_topk`` in vLLM's stock fused-mixture router entry\n(``vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py``), the\nchoke point the flashnext workload actually routes through (FusedMoEFactory ->\nFusedTopKRouter -> fused_topk). The upstream ds4 target -- the gpt-oss\ntriton_kernels ``make_routing_data`` -- is never on this model's path, and\nvLLM's own ``--enable-return-routed-experts`` capturer hangs off\n``BaseRouter.route()``, which the fused path does not call either.\n\n``num_local_experts`` is read from ``gating_output.shape[-1]`` (router logits\nare ``[M, num_experts]``): tensor shape is host metadata, so that costs no\ndevice sync.\n\nPer call it records (n_rows, n_distinct, n_local_experts) into a preallocated\ndevice buffer using only elementwise kernels -- no D2H copy, no sync, so it\ndoes not serialise the step it is measuring. The buffer is copied out once\nwhen the window closes. Slot 0 of the seen-mask absorbs any -1 padding rows so\nno boolean mask (and therefore no size-dependent sync) is needed.\n\nCost: a few extra small kernel launches per routing call. Off unless\nFN_EXPERT_UNION=1.\n\nEnv:\n    FN_EXPERT_UNION=1         enable (default: off)\n    FN_EU_START=200           skip this many calls first (warmup + prefill)\n    FN_EU_CALLS=2000          window size in routing calls\n    FN_EU_OUT=~/vllm-prof     output directory\n\nInstall is deliberately lazy: by the first decode the MoE layers are long\nsince built, and wrapping at import time of whatever loads this module would\nrisk a circular import. The caller drives install() once the engine is up;\ninstall() itself re-checks FN_EXPERT_UNION, so a stale call stays a no-op.\nA probe must never take the engine down: every failure path swallows the\nexception.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport atexit\nimport os\n\nimport torch\n\n_ENABLED = os.environ.get(\"FN_EXPERT_UNION\") == \"1\"\n_START = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_EU_START\", \"200\"))\n_CALLS = int(os.environ.get(\"FN_EU_CALLS\", \"2000\"))\n_OUT = os.path.expanduser(os.environ.get(\"FN_EU_OUT\", \"~/vllm-prof\"))\n\n_buf = None          # [_CALLS, 3] int32 on device\n_n = 0               # calls seen\n_done = False\n_installed = False\n\n\ndef _record(topk_ids, num_local_experts):\n    \"\"\"Accumulate one routing call. Device-only; never synchronises.\"\"\"\n    global _buf, _n, _done\n    if _done or not num_local_experts:\n        return\n    _n += 1\n    if _n <= _START:\n        return\n    i = _n - _START - 1\n    if i >= _CALLS:\n        _flush()\n        return\n\n    ids = topk_ids.reshape(-1).long()\n    if _buf is None:\n        _buf = torch.zeros(_CALLS, 3, dtype=torch.int32, device=ids.device)\n\n    # Slot 0 absorbs the -1 padding rows so no boolean mask (and therefore no\n    # size-dependent sync) is needed; real experts land at 1..num_local.\n    seen = torch.zeros(num_local_experts + 1, dtype=torch.bool, device=ids.device)\n    seen[ids + 1] = True\n\n    _buf[i, 0] = topk_ids.shape[0]\n    _buf[i, 1] = seen[1:].sum()\n    _buf[i, 2] = num_local_experts\n\n\ndef _flush():\n    \"\"\"Copy the buffer out once and write the dump.\"\"\"\n    global _done\n    if _done or _buf is None:\n        return\n    _done = True\n    try:\n        rows = _buf.cpu().tolist()\n        os.makedirs(_OUT, exist_ok=True)\n        path = os.path.join(_OUT, f\"expert_union_{os.getpid()}.tsv\")\n        with open(path, \"w\") as fh:\n            fh.write(\"# n_rows\\tn_distinct\\tn_local_experts\\n\")\n            for n_rows, n_distinct, n_local in rows:\n                if n_rows:\n                    fh.write(f\"{n_rows}\\t{n_distinct}\\t{n_local}\\n\")\n        print(f\"[fn_expert_union] wrote {path}\", flush=True)\n    except Exception as exc:  # a probe must never take the engine down\n        print(f\"[fn_expert_union] flush failed: {exc}\", flush=True)\n\n\ndef install():\n    \"\"\"Idempotently wrap fused_topk. Safe to call more than once.\"\"\"\n    global _installed\n    if not _ENABLED or _installed:\n        return\n    try:\n        from vllm.model_executor.layers.fused_moe.router import (\n            fused_topk_router as m,\n        )\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"[fn_expert_union] not installed: {exc}\", flush=True)\n        return\n\n    orig = m.fused_topk\n\n    def wrapped(*a, **kw):\n        res = orig(*a, **kw)\n        try:\n            # fused_topk(hidden_states, gating_output, topk, renormalize)\n            # -> (topk_weights, topk_ids). num_local_experts comes off\n            # gating_output's shape -- host metadata, no device sync.\n            gating = kw.get(\"gating_output\")\n            if gating is None and len(a) > 1:\n                gating = a[1]\n            topk_ids = res[1] if isinstance(res, tuple) and len(res) >= 2 else None\n            n_local = gating.shape[-1] if gating is not None else None\n            if topk_ids is not None:\n                _record(topk_ids, n_local)\n        except Exception:\n            pass  # never let the probe break routing\n        return res\n\n    wrapped._fn_orig = orig\n    m.fused_topk = wrapped\n    _installed = True\n    # Also flush on shutdown, so a run that ends before the window fills still\n    # leaves a (shorter) usable dump rather than nothing.\n    atexit.register(_flush)\n    print(\n        f\"[fn_expert_union] installed: skip {_START} calls, window {_CALLS}, \"\n        f\"out {_OUT}\",\n        flush=True,\n    )\n","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2890,"output":1925,"cacheRead":48128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":21,"totalTokens":52943,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988449445,"responseId":"chatcmpl-913aa08c-c7e7-42b8-93db-9faa219e2679","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_58f5ba86bcf04b7fbeffb121","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 6461 bytes to /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/fn_expert_union.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1787988481594},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Next up is tests/test_instruments.py.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now the test suite:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_df0b946f7ad0444190e0b68e","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"\"\"\"Instrument overlay tests — compile, notices, and budget invariants.\n\nThe offline half for container/rootfs/fn_*.py: py_compile each module (cfile\ninto a tempdir, so no bytecode lands in the overlay), check every adapted\nmodule carries its upstream notice header, and check fn_offload_batch's\nbudget arithmetic against the reference invariants (floor at the max group\nsize; promote counted in blocks). fn_offload_batch is torch-free by design,\nso that module alone is imported and exercised directly; the other two are\nchecked at the text/compile level so this suite runs on a host without\ntorch or vllm.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport importlib.util\nimport os\nimport pathlib\nimport py_compile\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest import mock\n\nROOT = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nROOTFS = ROOT / \"container\" / \"rootfs\"\n\n# name -> (upstream file the notice must cite, env vars the module must expose)\nMODULES = {\n    \"fn_synctrace.py\": (\"ds4_synctrace.py\", (\"FN_PROFILE\",)),\n    \"fn_offload_batch.py\": (\n        \"ds4_offload_batch.py\",\n        (\"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\", \"FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\"),\n    ),\n    \"fn_expert_union.py\": (\n        \"ds4_expert_union.py\",\n        (\"FN_EXPERT_UNION\", \"FN_EU_START\", \"FN_EU_CALLS\", \"FN_EU_OUT\"),\n    ),\n}\n\n# Stock env names the rename must have retired; none may survive in an\n# adapted module (the notice headers cite file names like ds4_synctrace.py,\n# which do not contain these).\n_RETIRED = (\"DS4_PROFILE\", \"DS4_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\",\n            \"DS4_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\", \"DS4_EXPERT_UNION\", \"DS4_EU_START\",\n            \"DS4_EU_CALLS\", \"DS4_EU_OUT\")\n\n\ndef _load_offload_batch():\n    path = ROOTFS / \"fn_offload_batch.py\"\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"fn_offload_batch\", path)\n    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(mod)\n    return mod\n\n\nclass InstrumentPackaging(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_every_module_compiles(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as td:\n            for name in MODULES:\n                path = ROOTFS / name\n                self.assertTrue(path.is_file(), f\"{path} missing from the overlay\")\n                py_compile.compile(str(path),\n                                   cfile=str(pathlib.Path(td) / (name + \"c\")),\n                                   doraise=True)\n\n    def test_every_module_carries_the_notice(self):\n        for name, (upstream, _) in MODULES.items():\n            text = (ROOTFS / name).read_text()\n            self.assertIn(\"Adapted from\", text, f\"{name} lacks an adaptation notice\")\n            self.assertIn(upstream, text, f\"{name} does not name {upstream}\")\n            self.assertIn(\"ds4-vllm\", text, f\"{name} does not name the upstream repo\")\n            self.assertIn(\"Apache License 2.0\", text, f\"{name} does not name the license\")\n\n    def test_env_surface_is_renamed_to_fn(self):\n        for name, (_, envs) in MODULES.items():\n            text = (ROOTFS / name).read_text()\n            for env in envs:\n                self.assertIn(env, text, f\"{name} does not expose {env}\")\n            for retired in _RETIRED:\n                self.assertNotIn(retired, text,\n                                 f\"{name} still carries the stock env {retired}\")\n\n    def test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay(self):\n        for path in ROOTFS.rglob(\"*\"):\n            self.assertNotEqual(path.suffix, \".pyc\", f\"bytecode in overlay: {path}\")\n            self.assertNotIn(\"__pycache__\", path.parts, f\"bytecode dir in overlay: {path}\")\n\n\nclass OffloadBudgetInvariants(unittest.TestCase):\n    \"\"\"fn_offload_batch arithmetic must match the reference invariants.\"\"\"\n\n    @classmethod\n    def setUpClass(cls):\n        cls.mod = _load_offload_batch()\n\n    def test_constants_match_the_reference(self):\n        self.assertEqual(self.mod.FRAC_ENV, \"FN_OFFLOAD_STORE_BATCH_FRAC\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.mod.PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV, \"FN_OFFLOAD_PROMOTE_FRAC\")\n        self.assertEqual(self.mod.DEFAULT_FRAC, 0.25)\n        self.assertEqual(self.mod.DEFAULT_PROMOTE_FRAC, 0.5)\n\n    def test_store_budget_arithmetic(self):\n        # 0.25 of 256 blocks = 64 blocks; key rate 1/128 + 1/16 per token\n        # -> 64 / 0.0703125 = 910 tokens (floor does not bite).\n        self.assertEqual(\n            self.mod.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16), frac=0.25), 910)\n\n    def test_store_floor_is_the_max_group_size(self):\n        # The floor is load-bearing: at frac 0.001 the raw budget is 14 tokens,\n        # under the coarsest group's 128-token block; the result must clamp to\n        # exactly max(sizes) so no group's cursor can rewind.\n        budget = self.mod.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16), frac=0.001)\n        self.assertEqual(budget, max(128, 16))\n        self.assertGreaterEqual(budget, 128)\n\n    def test_store_disabled_paths_return_none(self):\n        r = self.mod.resolve_store_batch_tokens\n        self.assertIsNone(r(None, (128, 16), frac=0.25))\n        self.assertIsNone(r(0, (128, 16), frac=0.25))\n        self.assertIsNone(r(256, (), frac=0.25))\n        self.assertIsNone(r(256, (0,), frac=0.25))\n        # frac <= 0 is the kill switch: unbounded == stock behaviour.\n        self.assertIsNone(r(256, (128, 16), frac=0))\n        self.assertIsNone(r(256, (128, 16), frac=-1))\n\n    def test_store_frac_reads_the_fn_env(self):\n        with mock.patch.dict(os.environ, {self.mod.FRAC_ENV: \"0.5\"}):\n            # 128 blocks / 0.0703125 keys-per-token = 1820 tokens.\n            self.assertEqual(\n                self.mod.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16)), 1820)\n        # Garbage in the env falls back to the default, never raises.\n        with mock.patch.dict(os.environ, {self.mod.FRAC_ENV: \"not-a-number\"}):\n            self.assertEqual(\n                self.mod.resolve_store_batch_tokens(256, (128, 16)), 910)\n\n    def test_promote_is_counted_in_blocks(self):\n        p = self.mod.resolve_promote_block_budget\n        # Blocks, not tokens: only num_blocks and frac enter the arithmetic.\n        self.assertEqual(p(258, frac=0.5), 129)\n        self.assertEqual(p(258, frac=0.0001), 1)       # floor of 1 block\n        self.assertEqual(p(258, frac=2.0), 258)        # capped at the tier\n        # Kill switch and degenerate specs restore stock behaviour.\n        self.assertIsNone(p(258, frac=0))\n        self.assertIsNone(p(0))\n        self.assertIsNone(p(None))\n\n    def test_promote_frac_reads_the_fn_env(self):\n        with mock.patch.dict(os.environ, {self.mod.PROMOTE_FRAC_ENV: \"0.25\"}):\n            self.assertEqual(self.mod.resolve_promote_block_budget(256), 64)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n","path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/tests/test_instruments.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":2318,"output":1954,"cacheRead":50688,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":9,"totalTokens":54960,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1787988481600,"responseId":"chatcmpl-f65de7f4-6d3d-41e1-9dfa-4ce9ce920891","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_df0b946f7ad0444190e0b68e","toolName":"w