e_in_the_overlay) ... FAIL\ntest_constants_match_the_reference (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_constants_match_the_reference) ... ok\ntest_promote_frac_reads_the_fn_env (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_promote_frac_reads_the_fn_env) ... ok\ntest_promote_is_counted_in_blocks (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_promote_is_counted_in_blocks) ... ok\ntest_store_budget_arithmetic (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_store_budget_arithmetic) ... ok\ntest_store_disabled_paths_return_none (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_store_disabled_paths_return_none) ... ok\ntest_store_floor_is_the_max_group_size (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_store_floor_is_the_max_group_size) ... ok\ntest_store_frac_reads_the_fn_env (tests.test_instruments.OffloadBudgetInvariants.test_store_frac_reads_the_fn_env) ... ok\n\n======================================================================\nFAIL: test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay (tests.test_instruments.InstrumentPackaging.test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay)\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/tests/test_instruments.py\", line 83, in test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay\n    self.assertNotIn(\"__pycache__\", path.parts, f\"bytecode dir in overlay: {path}\")\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAssertionError: '__pycache__' unexpectedly found in ('/', 'home', 'tom', '.local', 'state', 'tally', 'campaigns', 'flashnext', 'flashnext', 'ed7013e7b4ab', 'instruments', 'container', 'rootfs', '__pycache__') : bytecode dir in overlay: /home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/container/rootfs/__pycache__\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\nRan 11 tests in 0.004s\n\nFAILED (failures=1)\n\n\nCommand exited with code 1"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1787988523440},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"the `python3 -m py_compile` I ran earlier on the acceptance side wrote `__pycache__` into container/rootfs. This is the very trap that upstream's discipline is aware of (\"py_compile all overlay .py files, redirect cfile to tempdir\"). The acceptance criterion itself runs `python3 -m py_compile container/rootfs/...`, which generates `__pycache__` directories! In other words, the acceptance criterion itself creates bytecode directories inside the overlay, and my own test_no_bytecode test ends up failing whenever it's run in the acceptance chain.\n\nOptions:\n1. Remove the bytecode test (or restrict it to .pyc files tracked by git). The acceptance criterion command itself generates __pycache__, so a filesystem-level bytecode check can't run after py_compile within the same acceptance script. Upstream dealt with this by using a tempdir cfile inside tests, but the acceptance criterion's raw py_compile still generates them anyway.\n\nNote: `__pycache__` is gitignored (.gitignore has `__pycache__/` and `*.pyc`), so it will never be committed. My test should only check what gets committed / what's in the overlay… The simplest, most robust approach: either remove the bytecode test entirely, or skip directories and check only for the presence of *.pyc, but… even so, __pycache__/*.pyc gets created by the acceptance py_compile.\n\nBetter approach: keep the invariant but limit it to files tracked by git. Use git ls-files container/rootfs and assert that none of them are .pyc or __pycache__. That's the actual packaging invariant (nothing baked into the image). Let's rewrite that test to consult git.\n\nDelete the existing __pycache__ directory as well.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The acceptance criterion's own plain `py_compile` creates a `__pycache__` inside the overlay, so a filesystem-level bytecode check will self-destruct within the same acceptance chain. The real invariant is that nothing bytecode-derived gets *committed* (which is what COPY would bake into the image). Let's pin the test to what git actually tracks:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_65821db137334b5b8ef735a2","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"import importlib.util\nimport os\nimport pathlib\nimport py_compile\nimport subprocess\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest import mock","oldText":"import importlib.util\nimport os\nimport pathlib\nimport py_compile\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest import mock"},{"newText":"    def test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay(self):\n        # What matters is what is TRACKED: COPY bakes tracked files into the\n        # image, while stray local __pycache__ (e.g. from a bare py_compile)\n        # is gitignored and never ships.\n        out = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"ls-files\", str(ROOTFS)],\n                             capture_output=True, text=True,\n                             cwd=ROOT, check=True).stdout\n        for rel in out.splitlines():\n            self.assertFalse(rel.endswith(\".pyc\"), f\"bytecode tracked: {rel}\")\n            self.assertNotIn(\"__pycache__\", pathlib.PurePosixPath(rel).parts,\n                             f\"bytecode dir tracked: {rel}\")","oldText":"    def test_no_bytecode_in_the_overlay(self):\n        for path in ROOTFS.rglob(\"*\"):\n            self.assertNotEqual(path.suffix, \".pyc\", f\"bytecode in overlay: {path}\")\n            self.assertNotIn(\"__pycache__\", path.parts, f\"bytecode dir in overlay: {path}\")"}],"path":"/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/flashnext/ed7013e7b4ab/instruments/tests/test_instruments.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":908,"output":837,"cacheRead":54912,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":369,"totalTokens":56657,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheR