 re-target: the upstream wrap (`gpt_oss_triton_kernels_moe.make_routing_data`) is never called by this workload, so the wrap now sits on the stock fused-mixture router entry **`fused_topk`** in `vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/router/fused_topk_router.py` (per qsa-53896.md §4). `num_local_experts` comes off `gating_output.shape[-1]` — host metadata, preserving the no-sync discipline. Kill switch `FN_EXPERT_UNION` (default off), window env `FN_EU_START`/`FN_EU_CALLS`/`FN_EU_OUT`; every failure path swallows exceptions.\n\n4. **`tests/test_instruments.py`** — 11 host-runnable tests: py_compile with cfile into a tempdir, notice-header checks (names upstream file, repo, license), FN_ env-surface rename verified (and stock `DS4_*` env names asserted absent), tracked-bytecode overlay invariant, and the reference budget invariants (floor clamps exactly to max group size at frac 0.001; promote counted in blocks, capped at the tier, floored at 1; all disabled/degenerate paths return `None`; env-read paths with garbage fallback).\n\n**Verification:** the exact acceptance argv passes — all three modules compile, `grep -l 'Adapted from' container/rootfs/fn_*.py | wc -l` = 3, `python3 -m unittest tests.test_instruments -v` → 11/11 OK. Full repo suite (`unittest discover -s tests`) → 20/20 OK. Not pushed, not merged, no other worklist task read.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: my bytecode-in-overlay test pins to `git ls-files` rather than the filesystem, because the acceptance command's own plain `py_compile` creates a transient (gitignored) `__pycache__` in the overlay — what ships into the image via `COPY` is only the tracked content, which is what the invariant guards."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen-token-plan","model":"qwen3.8-max","usage":{"input":1553,"output":933,"cacheRead":57344,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":136,"totalTokens":59830,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787988583166,"r